26	FGP Architecture Analyzer	Analyzes student implementation code in the FGP (Fundamentals of Geometry Processing) C++ project for correctness, code quality, and adherence to assignment requirements.	{"name": "FGP Architecture Analyzer", "edges": [{"to": "analyze_structure", "from": "start"}, {"to": "a1_review", "from": "analyze_structure"}, {"to": "a2_review", "from": "a1_review"}, {"to": "a3_review", "from": "a2_review"}, {"to": "code_quality", "from": "a3_review"}, {"to": "compile_report", "from": "code_quality"}, {"to": "check_critical", "from": "compile_report"}, {"to": "create_issues", "from": "check_critical"}, {"to": "end", "from": "check_critical"}, {"to": "end", "from": "create_issues"}], "nodes": [{"id": "start", "name": "Start", "type": "start"}, {"id": "analyze_structure", "name": "Analyze Student Code Structure", "type": "claude_agent", "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "outputs": [{"name": "structure_analysis", "values": []}, {"name": "structure_severity", "values": ["CRITICAL", "HIGH", "MEDIUM", "LOW"]}], "timeout": 600, "prompt_template": "You are a C++ teaching assistant analyzing student code for the FGP (Fundamentals of Geometry Processing) course.\\n\\nRepository: {{repo_path}}\\nWorking directory: {{worktree_path}}\\nTarget folder/area: {{task_description}}\\n\\n**IMPORTANT: Only analyze files in src/student/. Do NOT review src/helper/ or src/main.cpp — those are the pre-provided framework and must not be modified.**\\n\\n**Student files to analyze:**\\n- Mesh.h/cpp — Half-edge mesh container, load(), queries, decimation\\n- Vertex.h/cpp — Vertex class with adjacency queries, decimation helpers\\n- Face.h/cpp — Face class with normal/area/center calculations\\n- HalfEdge.h/cpp — Half-edge class (mostly pre-implemented)\\n- Volume.h/cpp — 3D volumetric grid, trilinear interpolation\\n- MarchingCubes.h/cpp — Marching cubes algorithm\\n- SignedDistances.h — Signed distance functions (torus, rounded cube)\\n\\n**Assignment rules (from assignment sheet):**\\n- Only modify files in src/student/\\n- Do NOT add new members or classes (testing system casts between reference and student classes)\\n- Do NOT change function signatures (required by test system)\\n- New members, if absolutely necessary, must be added at the BOTTOM of class declarations\\n- Only standard library includes allowed, no external libraries\\n- LLVM code style enforced via clang-format\\n\\nAnalyze the student code structure:\\n\\n1. **File organization** — Are .h/.cpp properly paired? Are declarations in headers, implementations in source?\\n2. **Class interface compliance** — Have any function signatures been modified from the original? Have new members been added correctly (at bottom of class)?\\n3. **Include hygiene** — Any unnecessary includes? Circular dependencies? Only standard library used?\\n4. **Code organization within files** — Are functions implemented in a logical order? Is related code grouped?\\n5. **Compliance with assignment rules** — Any violations that would cause the testing system to fail?\\n\\nList every file, read them, and analyze. Provide specific file paths and line numbers.\\n\\nEnd your response with a severity rating: CRITICAL, HIGH, MEDIUM, or LOW."}, {"id": "a1_review", "name": "A1: Mesh Load & Queries Review", "type": "claude_agent", "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "outputs": [{"name": "a1_analysis", "values": []}, {"name": "a1_severity", "values": ["CRITICAL", "HIGH", "MEDIUM", "LOW"]}], "timeout": 600, "prompt_template": "You are a geometry processing expert reviewing Assignment 1 (Mesh Load & Queries) for the FGP course.\\n\\nRepository: {{repo_path}}\\nWorking directory: {{worktree_path}}\\nTarget folder/area: {{task_description}}\\n\\n**Only review src/student/ files. Read all .h and .cpp files in that directory.**\\n\\n**Assignment 1 Requirements (8 pts load + 12 pts queries = 20 pts total):**\\n\\n**Mesh::load (8 pts)** — Fill the half-edge data structure from PLY data:\\n- Input: vector of Points, vector of Colours, vector of Triangles (already sorted as in PLY)\\n- Must create Vertex, Face, HalfEdge objects and fill vertices_, faces_, half_edges_ vectors\\n- Assign vertex IDs in same order as points list (first point = first vertex ID via getNewVertexID())\\n- Must set up all half-edge links: next, prev, pair, origin vertex, face\\n- PLY files use clockwise orientation — implementation must be consistent (CW or CCW, but consistent)\\n- **EFFICIENCY IS CRITICAL**: Must be O(n), NOT O(n²). The testing system has a time threshold. Hint: use a map/hash to find half-edge pairs efficiently\\n\\n**Query 1 (2 pts): Face::getAdjacentHalfEdges** — Return all 3 half-edges of a face\\n**Query 2 (2 pts): Vertex::getAdjacentHalfEdges** — Return only OUTGOING half-edges from vertex v\\n**Query 3 (2 pts): Face::getAdjacentVertices** — Return the 3 corner vertices of a face\\n**Query 4 (2 pts): Vertex::getAdjacentFaces** — Return all faces adjacent to vertex v\\n**Query 5 (2 pts): Mesh::getVertexAtPosition + Vertex::isVertexAtPosition** — Find vertex at (x,y,z), O(n)\\n**Query 6 (2 pts): Vertex::getOneRingNeighbourhood** — All vertices in 1-ring of v (use lecture version!)\\n\\n**Half-edge data structure (from assignment sheet):**\\n- Face: pointer to one adjacent half-edge\\n- Vertex: pointer to one outgoing half-edge\\n- HalfEdge: pair_ (opposite), next_ (next in face), prev_ (previous in face), origin_ (vertex it starts from), face_ (face it belongs to)\\n\\n**Review checklist:**\\n1. Is Mesh::load implemented? Is it O(n)? Does it use a map/hash for pair finding?\\n2. Are all 6 queries implemented correctly using half-edge traversal?\\n3. Is one-ring traversal following half-edge chains correctly (not just iterating all vertices)?\\n4. Are boundary cases handled (mesh boundaries, isolated vertices)?\\n5. Are half-edge links (next/prev/pair) set up correctly and consistently?\\n6. Any bugs: null pointer dereference, infinite loops in traversal, wrong traversal direction?\\n\\nFor each finding provide file path, line numbers, issue, and suggested fix.\\n\\nEnd with a severity rating: CRITICAL, HIGH, MEDIUM, or LOW."}, {"id": "a2_review", "name": "A2: Marching Cubes Review", "type": "claude_agent", "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "outputs": [{"name": "a2_analysis", "values": []}, {"name": "a2_severity", "values": ["CRITICAL", "HIGH", "MEDIUM", "LOW"]}], "timeout": 600, "prompt_template": "You are a geometry processing expert reviewing Assignment 2 (Marching Cubes) for the FGP course.\\n\\nRepository: {{repo_path}}\\nWorking directory: {{worktree_path}}\\nTarget folder/area: {{task_description}}\\n\\n**Only review src/student/ files. Read SignedDistances.h, Volume.h/cpp, MarchingCubes.h/cpp, and Mesh.h/cpp (for addTriangle context).**\\n\\n**Assignment 2 Requirements (20 pts total):**\\n\\n**Signed Distance Functions (2 pts):**\\n- dist_fun_1 (torus): s(x,y,z) = sqrt((sqrt(x²+y²) - R)² + z²) - r, with R=7.5, r=3, centered in 32x32x32 grid (center at 16,16,16 like the sphere example)\\n- dist_fun_2 (rounded cube): s(x,y,z) = ||(max(|x|-a/2, 0), max(|y|-a/2, 0), max(|z|-a/2, 0))|| + min(max(|x|-a/2, |y|-a/2, |z|-a/2), 0) - r, with r=2.5, a=16, centered in grid\\n- Volume *vol parameter is NOT used in SDF functions (only in volume interpolation)\\n\\n**Trilinear Interpolation (4 pts) — Volume::interpolate:**\\n- Given float x,y,z, estimate distance using 8 surrounding integer corners\\n- Get corners by floor/ceil of input coordinates\\n- c000 to c111 are distance values at corners via Volume::at()\\n- Compute xd=x-x0, yd=y-y0, zd=z-z0 (denominators are always 1)\\n- Interpolate along x: c00=c000*(1-xd)+c100*xd, c01=c001*(1-xd)+c101*xd, c10=c010*(1-xd)+c110*xd, c11=c011*(1-xd)+c111*xd\\n- Then y: c0=c00*(1-yd)+c10*yd, c1=c01*(1-yd)+c11*yd\\n- Then z: c=c0*(1-zd)+c1*zd\\n\\n**Cell Code (2 pts) — MarchingCubes::getCellCode:**\\n- 8-bit unsigned int, each bit = one corner\\n- Corner inside surface (distance < 0) = set bit, outside (distance >= 0) = unset bit\\n- Use the corners array from framework for corner traversal order\\n\\n**Add Triangle (2 pts) — MarchingCubes::addTriangle:**\\n- Add a triangle (3 vertices) to the mesh\\n- Must avoid duplicating vertices at same position (check if vertex already exists)\\n- Create proper half-edge structure for the new triangle\\n\\n**Marching Cubes Algorithm (10 pts) — MarchingCubes::marchingCubes:**\\n- Iterate all cells in 32x32x32 lattice (cells from (0,0,0) to (31,31,31))\\n- For each cell: compute cell code, look up triangulation table\\n- Triangulation table entries: pairs of corner indices representing edges. Each 6 values = 1 triangle (3 edges × 2 corners). Stop at first -1.\\n- Linear interpolation for vertex positions between corners: d1=|s(u)|, d2=|s(v)|, w1=d1/(d1+d2), w2=d2/(d1+d2), t=(1-w1)*u+(1-w2)*v\\n\\n**Review checklist:**\\n1. Are both SDFs mathematically correct? Properly centered at (16,16,16)?\\n2. Is trilinear interpolation formula correct? Watch for typos in c000-c111 indexing.\\n3. Is cell code computation correct (bit ordering matches corners array)?\\n4. Does addTriangle properly handle vertex deduplication?\\n5. Does marchingCubes iterate correctly, read triangulation table properly, stop at -1?\\n6. Is linear interpolation for vertex positions correct?\\n7. Boundary conditions: what happens at grid edges (x=0 or x=31)?\\n\\nFor each finding provide file path, line numbers, issue, and suggested fix.\\n\\nEnd with a severity rating: CRITICAL, HIGH, MEDIUM, or LOW."}, {"id": "a3_review", "name": "A3: Mesh Decimation Review", "type": "claude_agent", "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "outputs": [{"name": "a3_analysis", "values": []}, {"name": "a3_severity", "values": ["CRITICAL", "HIGH", "MEDIUM", "LOW"]}], "timeout": 600, "prompt_template": "You are a geometry processing expert reviewing Assignment 3 (Mesh Decimation) for the FGP course.\\n\\nRepository: {{repo_path}}\\nWorking directory: {{worktree_path}}\\nTarget folder/area: {{task_description}}\\n\\n**Only review src/student/ files. Read Face.h/cpp, Vertex.h/cpp, Mesh.h/cpp, and HalfEdge.h/cpp.**\\n\\n**Assignment 3 Requirements (20 pts total):**\\n\\n**Face calculations:**\\n- Face::calcNormal (1 pt): Normal = (v1-v0) × (v2-v1). Store in normal_. Use half-edge traversal to get vertices.\\n- Face::calcArea (1 pt): Area = 0.5 * ||normal||. The area-weighted normal nA(T) = (vj-vi) × (vk-vi), area = 0.5*||nA(T)||. Store in area_.\\n- Face::calcCenter (1 pt): Barycenter = (v0+v1+v2)/3. Store in center_.\\n\\n**Vertex calculations:**\\n- Vertex::calcAverageNormal (1 pt): Area-weighted average of unit normals from adjacent faces. Formula: navg = sum(Ai*ni) / sum(Ai) where ni are UNIT normals.\\n- Vertex::calcAveragePoint (1 pt): Area-weighted average of face centroids. Formula: pavg = sum(Ai*pi) / sum(Ai) where pi are face barycenters.\\n- Vertex::calcDistanceToAveragePlane (1 pt): D = (v - pavg) · navg / |navg|. Distance from vertex to the average plane.\\n- Vertex::isInConvexNeighbourhood (1 pt): Check ALL vertices in one-ring for convexity using: ((vi-vi-1) × (vi+1-vi)) · navg >= 0. Be careful with CW vs CCW orientation! Use only getters, not calc functions.\\n\\n**Mesh decimation:**\\n- Mesh::findSuitableVertex (1 pt): Search entire mesh for vertex with minimum D that passes convexity check. Skip removed vertices.\\n- Mesh::decimate (12 pts for 10%-50% decimation): Call findSuitableVertex, then removeVertex.\\n- Mesh::removeVertex: Remove vertex and all adjacent half-edges (including pairs) and faces. Call remove() methods. Then re-triangulate the resulting polygon hole using shell-formed triangulation. Important: create NEW half-edges and faces, do NOT reuse removed ones. Hint: can reuse inner ring or create entirely new half-edges (like calling load for new triangles).\\n\\n**Mathematical formulas to verify:**\\n- Normal: n = (v1-v0) × (v2-v1), must be consistent with CW/CCW choice\\n- Area-weighted normal: nA = (vj-vi) × (vk-vi)\\n- Area: A = 0.5 * ||nA||\\n- Average normal: navg = sum(Ai*ni) / sum(Ai)\\n- Average point: pavg = sum(Ai*pi) / sum(Ai)\\n- Distance: D = (v-pavg) · navg / |navg|\\n- Convexity: ((vi-vi-1) × (vi+1-vi)) · navg >= 0\\n\\n**Review checklist:**\\n1. Are normal, area, center calculations mathematically correct?\\n2. Is calcAverageNormal using UNIT normals weighted by area (not area-weighted normals)?\\n3. Is convexity check correct for the chosen orientation (CW vs CCW)?\\n4. Does findSuitableVertex skip removed vertices? Does it correctly find minimum D?\\n5. Does removeVertex properly remove all adjacent half-edges, their pairs, and faces?\\n6. Is re-triangulation done correctly (shell-formed, new half-edges, not reused)?\\n7. Are half-edge links consistent after re-triangulation (next/prev/pair all correct)?\\n8. Does it handle edge cases: boundary vertices? Last vertices?\\n\\nFor each finding provide file path, line numbers, issue, and suggested fix.\\n\\nEnd with a severity rating: CRITICAL, HIGH, MEDIUM, or LOW."}, {"id": "code_quality", "name": "Code Quality & Bugs", "type": "claude_agent", "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "outputs": [{"name": "quality_analysis", "values": []}, {"name": "quality_severity", "values": ["CRITICAL", "HIGH", "MEDIUM", "LOW"]}], "timeout": 600, "prompt_template": "You are a C++ code reviewer analyzing student code in the FGP geometry processing project.\\n\\nRepository: {{repo_path}}\\nWorking directory: {{worktree_path}}\\nTarget folder/area: {{task_description}}\\n\\n**Only review src/student/ files.**\\n\\nThis is C++14 code. Read every .h and .cpp file in src/student/ and check for:\\n\\n**Memory & Safety:**\\n- Null pointer dereference — especially after half-edge traversal (getPair(), getNext(), etc.)\\n- Infinite loops — in one-ring traversal if half-edge links are broken\\n- Dangling pointers — referencing removed vertices/faces/half-edges\\n- Division by zero — in normal calculations (zero-area faces), in interpolation, in distance calculations\\n- Array/vector out of bounds — accessing vertices_, faces_, half_edges_ with invalid IDs\\n\\n**Efficiency (critical for A1):**\\n- Is Mesh::load O(n) or O(n²)? Does it use a hash map for finding half-edge pairs?\\n- Any unnecessary nested loops that could be flattened?\\n\\n**Correctness:**\\n- Floating point comparisons (using == on floats instead of epsilon)\\n- Off-by-one errors in grid iteration (marching cubes: 0 to 31 vs 0 to 32)\\n- Wrong sign in SDF functions (inside should be negative)\\n- Inconsistent CW/CCW orientation between load and decimation\\n\\n**Code Quality:**\\n- Missing const on methods that don't modify state\\n- Raw loops where range-for would work\\n- Magic numbers without explanation\\n- Dead code or unused variables\\n- Missing error handling (null returns, empty vectors)\\n\\nFor every finding provide file path, line numbers, what the issue is, why it matters, and fix.\\n\\nEnd with a severity rating: CRITICAL, HIGH, MEDIUM, or LOW."}, {"id": "compile_report", "name": "Compile Final Report", "type": "claude_agent", "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "outputs": [{"name": "final_report", "values": []}, {"name": "needs_issues", "values": ["YES", "NO"]}], "timeout": 600, "prompt_template": "You are a teaching assistant compiling a comprehensive review report for a student's FGP geometry processing implementation.\\n\\nRepository: {{repo_path}}\\nTarget folder/area: {{task_description}}\\n\\nBelow are results from four independent analyses of the student's code in src/student/.\\n\\n---\\n**STRUCTURE ANALYSIS** (Severity: {{structure_severity}})\\n{{structure_analysis}}\\n\\n---\\n**A1: MESH LOAD & QUERIES** (Severity: {{a1_severity}})\\n{{a1_analysis}}\\n\\n---\\n**A2: MARCHING CUBES** (Severity: {{a2_severity}})\\n{{a2_analysis}}\\n\\n---\\n**A3: MESH DECIMATION** (Severity: {{a3_severity}})\\n{{a3_analysis}}\\n\\n---\\n**CODE QUALITY & BUGS** (Severity: {{quality_severity}})\\n{{quality_analysis}}\\n\\n---\\n\\nCreate a final report with:\\n\\n1. **Executive Summary** — Overall assessment of the implementation\\n2. **Assignment 1 Score Risk** — Issues that would cause point deductions (8 pts load + 12 pts queries). Flag efficiency problems that would fail the time threshold.\\n3. **Assignment 2 Score Risk** — Issues that would cause point deductions (2 pts SDFs + 4 pts interpolation + 2 pts cell code + 2 pts addTriangle + 10 pts algorithm)\\n4. **Assignment 3 Score Risk** — Issues that would cause point deductions (7 pts helper functions + 1 pt findSuitableVertex + 12 pts decimation)\\n5. **Critical Bugs** — Issues that would cause crashes, infinite loops, or wrong output\\n6. **Quick Fixes** — Easy corrections that would gain points\\n7. **Unimplemented Functions** — List any TODO functions that are still empty\\n\\nBe specific with file paths, line numbers, and mathematical corrections.\\n\\nEnd with an estimated score: X/20 for each assignment.\\n\\nRespond with either YES or NO: are there critical issues that need immediate GitHub issues created?"}, {"id": "check_critical", "name": "Critical Issues Found?", "type": "condition", "branches": {"NO": "end", "YES": "create_issues"}, "default_branch": "end", "condition_field": "needs_issues"}, {"id": "create_issues", "name": "Create GitHub Issues", "type": "claude_agent", "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "outputs": [{"name": "created_issues", "values": []}], "timeout": 300, "prompt_template": "You are creating GitHub issues for critical findings in the FGP student implementation.\\n\\nRepository: {{repo_path}}\\nWorking directory: {{worktree_path}}\\n\\n{{final_report}}\\n\\nCreate GitHub issues for CRITICAL findings only (bugs that cause crashes, wrong output, or would fail the testing system). Use `gh issue create --repo {{repo_path}} --title \\"...\\" --body \\"...\\"`\\n\\nFor each issue include the file path, line numbers, the mathematical formula that's wrong (if applicable), and a suggested C++ fix.\\n\\nList all created issue numbers when done."}, {"id": "end", "name": "Analysis Complete", "type": "end", "result_template": "{{final_report}}"}], "version": "1.0"}	2026-03-15 12:21:42.589548+00	2026-03-15 12:31:51.079744+00
27	FGP Development Pipeline	FGP-specific pipeline for implementing assignment tasks. Knows all assignment requirements, formulas, and grading criteria from the assignment sheet.	{"name": "FGP Development Pipeline", "edges": [{"to": "check_blockers", "from": "start"}, {"to": "blocker_gate", "from": "check_blockers"}, {"to": "check_clarity", "from": "blocker_gate"}, {"to": "blocked_fail", "from": "blocker_gate"}, {"to": "clarity_gate", "from": "check_clarity"}, {"to": "analyze", "from": "clarity_gate"}, {"to": "refine_issue", "from": "clarity_gate"}, {"to": "vague_fail", "from": "clarity_gate"}, {"to": "check_clarity", "from": "refine_issue"}, {"to": "plan", "from": "analyze"}, {"to": "develop", "from": "plan"}, {"to": "review", "from": "develop"}, {"to": "review_gate", "from": "review"}, {"to": "done", "from": "review_gate"}, {"to": "develop", "from": "review_gate"}, {"to": "failed", "from": "review_gate"}], "nodes": [{"id": "start", "name": "Start", "type": "start", "targets": ["check_blockers"]}, {"id": "check_blockers", "name": "Check Blockers", "type": "claude_agent", "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "outputs": [{"name": "blocker_status", "values": ["READY", "BLOCKED"]}, {"name": "blocker_reason", "values": []}], "targets": ["blocker_gate"], "timeout": 300, "status_label": "checking blockers", "prompt_template": "You are a BLOCKER CHECK agent for the FGP geometry processing project.\\n\\nDetermine if issue #{{issue_number}} can be worked on right now.\\n\\nIssue: {{issue_title}}\\n{{issue_body}}\\n\\n## FGP Assignment Dependencies\\n- A1 (Mesh Load) is required for A2 and A3\\n- A2 (Marching Cubes) is independent of A3\\n- A3 (Mesh Decimation) requires A1 queries (especially one-ring neighbourhood)\\n- Within A1: load() must work before queries can be tested\\n- Within A2: SDFs and interpolation must work before marchingCubes\\n- Within A3: Face calc functions → Vertex calc functions → findSuitableVertex → removeVertex\\n\\n## Instructions\\n1. Run `gh issue list --repo {{repo_path}} --state open --limit 50` to see open issues.\\n2. Check if this issue depends on unfinished work tracked in other issues.\\n3. Check the actual code to see if prerequisite functions are implemented.\\n\\nIf blocked, respond with BLOCKED and explain why.\\nIf ready, respond with READY."}, {"id": "blocker_gate", "name": "Blocker Gate", "type": "condition", "branches": [{"value": "READY", "target": "check_clarity"}, {"value": "BLOCKED", "target": "blocked_fail"}], "status_label": "checking blocker result", "condition_field": "blocker_status"}, {"id": "blocked_fail", "name": "Blocked", "type": "failed", "reason_template": "Issue #{{issue_number}} is blocked: {{blocker_reason}}"}, {"id": "check_clarity", "name": "Check Clarity", "type": "claude_agent", "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "outputs": [{"name": "clarity_status", "values": ["CLEAR", "VAGUE"]}, {"name": "clarity_reason", "values": []}], "targets": ["clarity_gate"], "timeout": 300, "status_label": "checking clarity", "prompt_template": "You are a CLARITY CHECK agent for the FGP project.\\n\\n1. Fetch the issue: `gh issue view {{issue_number}} --repo {{repo_path}}`\\n2. Check if the issue clearly specifies which TODO function(s) to implement.\\n\\nContext — the 24 TODO functions in src/student/:\\n**A1:** Mesh::load, Face::getAdjacentHalfEdges, Face::getAdjacentVertices, Vertex::getAdjacentHalfEdges, Vertex::getAdjacentFaces, Mesh::getVertexAtPosition, Vertex::isVertexAtPosition, Vertex::getOneRingNeighbourhood\\n**A2:** SignedDistances::dist_fun_1 (torus), SignedDistances::dist_fun_2 (rounded cube), Volume::interpolate, MarchingCubes::getCellCode, MarchingCubes::addTriangle, MarchingCubes::marchingCubes\\n**A3:** Face::calcNormal, Face::calcArea, Face::calcCenter, Vertex::calcAverageNormal, Vertex::calcAveragePoint, Vertex::calcDistanceToAveragePlane, Vertex::isInConvexNeighbourhood, Mesh::findSuitableVertex, Mesh::decimate, Mesh::removeVertex\\n\\nIf the issue maps to known TODO function(s), respond CLEAR.\\nIf too vague, respond VAGUE and explain what's missing."}, {"id": "clarity_gate", "name": "Clarity Gate", "type": "condition", "branches": [{"value": "CLEAR", "target": "analyze"}, {"value": "VAGUE", "target": "refine_issue"}], "status_label": "checking clarity result", "max_iterations": 1, "condition_field": "clarity_status", "max_iterations_target": "vague_fail"}, {"id": "refine_issue", "name": "Refine Issue", "type": "template", "targets": ["check_clarity"], "template_id": 15, "status_label": "refining issue"}, {"id": "vague_fail", "name": "Too Vague", "type": "failed", "reason_template": "Issue #{{issue_number}} is still too vague after refinement: {{clarity_reason}}"}, {"id": "analyze", "name": "Analyze Project", "type": "claude_agent", "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "outputs": [{"name": "project_context", "values": []}], "targets": ["plan"], "timeout": 600, "status_label": "analyzing project", "prompt_template": "You are a PROJECT ANALYST for the FGP C++ geometry processing project. Gather context for issue #{{issue_number}}: {{issue_title}}.\\n\\n{{issue_body}}\\n\\n## FGP Project Structure\\n- src/student/ — Student implementation files (ONLY these should be modified)\\n- src/helper/ — Framework utilities (DO NOT modify): Point, Vector3d, Colour, Triangle, FileHandler (PLY I/O), TriangleTable (256-entry MC lookup), HelpMesh/HelpVertex/HelpFace/HelpHalfEdge (getters/setters)\\n- src/main.cpp — CLI entry point (DO NOT modify for submission)\\n- src/config.h — LOGGING_ACTIVE macro, WORKING_DIR\\n- res/meshes/ — PLY test files: tetrahedron.ply (simplest), sphere.ply, cow.ply, cow_colour.ply\\n- res/volumes/ — Binary volumes: volume_cube.bin, volume_bunny.bin, volume_charmander.bin (32x32x32 float grids)\\n\\n## Half-Edge Data Structure\\n- HalfEdge: pair_ (opposite), next_ (next in face), prev_ (previous in face), origin_ (start vertex), face_\\n- Vertex: pointer to one outgoing half-edge, position (Point), colour\\n- Face: pointer to one adjacent half-edge\\n- IDs assigned via getNewVertexID/FaceID/HalfEdgeID (sequential)\\n- Removed entities: call remove() method, sets removed_=true and pointers to nullptr\\n\\n## Key Mathematical Formulas\\n- Normal: n = (v1-v0) × (v2-v1)\\n- Area: A = 0.5 * ||(vj-vi) × (vk-vi)||\\n- Barycenter: (v0+v1+v2)/3\\n- Torus SDF: s(x,y,z) = sqrt((sqrt(x²+y²)-R)²+z²) - r, R=7.5, r=3, centered at (16,16,16)\\n- Rounded Cube SDF: s = ||(max(|x|-a/2,0), max(|y|-a/2,0), max(|z|-a/2,0))|| + min(max(|x|-a/2,|y|-a/2,|z|-a/2),0) - r, r=2.5, a=16\\n- Trilinear interpolation: interpolate x→y→z using 8 corners\\n- MC vertex interpolation: d1=|s(u)|, d2=|s(v)|, w1=d1/(d1+d2), w2=d2/(d1+d2), t=(1-w1)*u+(1-w2)*v\\n- Average normal: navg = sum(Ai*ni)/sum(Ai) where ni are UNIT normals\\n- Average point: pavg = sum(Ai*pi)/sum(Ai)\\n- Distance to plane: D = (v-pavg)·navg / |navg|\\n- Convexity: ((vi-vi-1) × (vi+1-vi)) · navg >= 0\\n\\n## Instructions\\n1. Read the relevant src/student/ files for this issue.\\n2. Read corresponding src/helper/ files to understand the provided interface.\\n3. Check which functions are already implemented vs still TODO.\\n4. Check `git log --oneline -20` for recent work.\\n5. Note any dependencies on other functions.\\n\\nOutput a concise summary of relevant files, existing code, and what needs to be done. Do NOT write code."}, {"id": "plan", "name": "Plan", "type": "claude_agent", "model": "claude-opus-4-6", "outputs": [{"name": "plan", "values": []}], "targets": ["develop"], "timeout": 600, "status_label": "planning", "prompt_template": "You are a PLANNER for the FGP C++ geometry processing project. Plan implementation of issue #{{issue_number}}: {{issue_title}}.\\n\\n{{issue_body}}\\n\\n## Project Context\\n{{project_context}}\\n\\n## FGP Rules\\n- Only modify files in src/student/\\n- Do NOT add new classes or members (except at bottom of class if absolutely necessary)\\n- Do NOT change function signatures\\n- Only standard library includes allowed\\n- C++14 standard (GCC 5+, Clang 3.4+)\\n- Use getNewVertexID()/getNewFaceID()/getNewHalfEdgeID() for new entities\\n- Use shared_ptr<Point> and shared_ptr<Colour> for points/colours\\n- Raw pointers for half-edge topology (Vertex*, Face*, HalfEdge*)\\n- Mark removed entities with remove() method, never delete\\n- Mesh::load MUST be O(n) — use std::map or std::unordered_map for half-edge pair lookup\\n- LLVM code style\\n- Test with: `sh fgp.sh build && ./bin/fgp <command> <args>`\\n  - A1: `./bin/fgp query res/meshes/tetrahedron.ply <query_number> <param>`\\n  - A2: `./bin/fgp marchingCubes res/volumes/volume_bunny.bin 0`\\n  - A3: `./bin/fgp decimation res/meshes/cow.ply 10`\\n\\n## Instructions\\n1. List exactly which TODO function(s) to implement.\\n2. For each function, specify the algorithm step-by-step with formulas.\\n3. Note data structures to use (maps, vectors, etc.).\\n4. Note edge cases to handle.\\n5. List files to modify.\\n\\nOutput ONLY the plan. Do NOT write code. Do NOT make git changes."}, {"id": "develop", "name": "Develop", "type": "claude_agent", "model": "claude-opus-4-6", "outputs": [{"name": "dev_result", "values": []}], "targets": ["review"], "timeout": 900, "resume_self": true, "status_label": "developing", "prompt_template": "You are a DEVELOPER for the FGP C++ geometry processing project. Implement issue #{{issue_number}}: {{issue_title}} on branch {{branch}}.\\n\\n{{issue_body}}\\n\\n## Project Context\\n{{project_context}}\\n\\n## Plan\\n{{plan}}\\n\\n## FGP Development Rules\\n- ONLY modify files in src/student/. NEVER modify src/helper/ or src/main.cpp.\\n- Do NOT add new classes. Do NOT change function signatures.\\n- C++14 only. Standard library only (no external libs).\\n- Use getNewVertexID()/getNewFaceID()/getNewHalfEdgeID() for new entities.\\n- shared_ptr<Point> for points, shared_ptr<Colour> for colours. Raw pointers for topology.\\n- For Mesh::load: MUST be O(n). Use std::map<pair<size_t,size_t>, HalfEdge*> or similar for pair finding.\\n- After removing entities: call remove() which sets removed_=true and pointers to nullptr.\\n- When creating new triangles in removeVertex: create NEW half-edges/faces, never reuse removed ones.\\n- Check for nullptr before dereferencing any half-edge pointer.\\n- Use Vector3d for all vector math (cross(), dot(), abs(), normalize()).\\n- Guard debug output with `if (LOGGING_ACTIVE)`.\\n- Build: `mkdir -p build && cd build && cmake .. && make`\\n- Test A1: `./bin/fgp query res/meshes/tetrahedron.ply 3 0` (query 3, vertex 0)\\n- Test A2: `./bin/fgp marchingCubes res/volumes/volume_bunny.bin 0`\\n- Test A3: `./bin/fgp decimation res/meshes/cow.ply 10`\\n\\n## Instructions\\n1. Implement the functions according to the plan.\\n2. Build and verify compilation.\\n3. Test with provided meshes.\\n4. Commit, push, and open a PR.\\n\\nIf retrying after review feedback, address ALL requested changes.\\n\\nOutput the PR URL at the end."}, {"id": "review", "name": "Review", "type": "claude_agent", "model": "claude-opus-4-6", "outputs": [{"name": "review_result", "values": []}, {"name": "review_verdict", "values": ["APPROVED", "CHANGES_REQUESTED"]}], "targets": ["review_gate"], "timeout": 600, "status_label": "reviewing", "prompt_template": "You are a CODE REVIEWER for the FGP geometry processing project. Review the PR on branch {{branch}} for issue #{{issue_number}}: {{issue_title}}.\\n\\n## FGP Review Checklist\\n1. **Only src/student/ modified** — No changes to helper/, main.cpp, or CMakeLists.txt\\n2. **No new classes or changed signatures** — Testing system requires exact interface match\\n3. **Mathematical correctness** — Verify formulas match the assignment sheet:\\n   - Normals: n = (v1-v0) × (v2-v1)\\n   - Area: 0.5 * ||(vj-vi) × (vk-vi)||\\n   - Torus SDF: sqrt((sqrt(x²+y²)-7.5)²+z²) - 3, centered at 16\\n   - Trilinear: correct c000-c111 indexing and interpolation order (x→y→z)\\n   - Distance to plane: (v-pavg)·navg / |navg|\\n   - Convexity: ((vi-vi-1) × (vi+1-vi)) · navg >= 0\\n4. **Efficiency** — Mesh::load must be O(n), not O(n²). Uses map for pair lookup?\\n5. **Memory safety** — nullptr checks before dereferencing, no dangling pointers, no leaks\\n6. **Half-edge integrity** — All links (next/prev/pair/origin/face) consistent after modifications\\n7. **Edge cases** — Boundary handling, degenerate triangles, division by zero guards\\n8. **C++14 compliance** — No C++17/20 features\\n9. **Standard library only** — No external includes\\n\\n## Instructions\\n1. Read the PR diff: `gh pr diff --repo {{repo_path}}`\\n2. Read source files for full context.\\n3. Verify compilation: `cd build && cmake .. && make`\\n4. Focus on correctness — this code is graded by an automated testing system.\\n\\nIf correct, respond APPROVED.\\nIf issues found, respond CHANGES_REQUESTED with specific fixes."}, {"id": "review_gate", "name": "Review Gate", "type": "condition", "branches": [{"value": "APPROVED", "target": "done"}, {"value": "CHANGES_REQUESTED", "target": "develop"}], "status_label": "checking review", "max_iterations": 2, "condition_field": "review_verdict", "iteration_counter": "review_round", "max_iterations_target": "failed"}, {"id": "done", "name": "Ready to Merge", "type": "end", "result_template": "Issue #{{issue_number}} implemented and reviewed. PR ready to merge."}, {"id": "failed", "name": "Failed", "type": "failed", "reason_template": "Pipeline failed after max review rounds for issue #{{issue_number}}"}], "version": "1.0"}	2026-03-15 12:21:42.782877+00	2026-03-15 12:31:51.282325+00
