e": "CLEAR", "target": "analyze"}, {"value": "VAGUE", "target": "refine_issue"}], "position": {"x": 240, "y": 560}, "status_label": "checking clarity result", "max_iterations": 1, "condition_field": "clarity_status", "max_iterations_target": "vague_fail"}, {"id": "vague_fail", "name": "Too Vague", "type": "failed", "targets": [], "position": {"x": 0, "y": 700}, "reason_template": "Issue #{{issue_number}} is still too vague after refinement: {{clarity_reason}}"}, {"id": "analyze", "name": "Analyze Project", "type": "claude_agent", "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "retry": {"max_attempts": 1}, "outputs": [{"name": "project_context", "values": []}], "targets": ["plan"], "timeout": 600, "position": {"x": 240, "y": 700}, "status_label": "analyzing project", "prompt_template": "You are a PROJECT ANALYST agent. Explore the codebase and gather context for implementing issue #{{issue_number}}: {{issue_title}}.\\n\\n{{issue_body}}\\n\\n## Instructions\\n1. Run to get the latest code.\\n2. Explore the project structure — check key directories, configs, and conventions.\\n3. Look at recent commits with  to understand current development patterns.\\n4. Find files and code relevant to this issue.\\n5. Note the tech stack, coding patterns, and conventions used.\\n6. Check if needed APIs, DB tables, services, or dependencies exist.\\n\\n## Output\\nProvide a concise project context summary covering:\\n- Relevant files and their purpose\\n- Coding patterns and conventions to follow\\n- Existing code that can be reused\\n- Any technical considerations for the implementation\\n\\nKeep it focused on what the planner and developer need to know. Do NOT write code or create a plan."}, {"id": "plan", "name": "Plan", "type": "claude_agent", "model": "claude-opus-4-6", "retry": {"max_attempts": 1}, "outputs": [{"name": "plan", "values": []}], "targets": ["develop"], "timeout": 600, "position": {"x": 240, "y": 840}, "status_label": "planning", "prompt_template": "You are a PLANNER agent. Create an implementation plan for issue #{{issue_number}}: {{issue_title}}.\\n\\n{{issue_body}}\\n\\n## Project Context\\n{{project_context}}\\n\\n## Instructions\\n1. Based on the project context, design a clear implementation approach.\\n2. List every file to create or modify with specific changes needed.\\n3. Note any edge cases, risks, or dependencies.\\n4. Keep the plan actionable — bullet points, not essays.\\n5. Follow existing patterns and conventions from the project context.\\n6. Prefer reusing existing code over duplicating.\\n\\n## Output\\nOutput ONLY the implementation plan. Do NOT write any code.\\nDo NOT open PRs, create branches, or make any git changes."}, {"id": "develop", "name": "Develop", "type": "claude_agent", "model": "claude-opus-4-6", "retry": {"max_attempts": 1}, "outputs": [{"name": "dev_result", "values": []}], "targets": ["review"], "timeout": 900, "position": {"x": 414, "y": 948}, "resume_self": true, "status_label": "developing", "prompt_template": "You are a DEVELOPER agent. Implement the changes for issue #{{issue_number}}: {{issue_title}} on branch {{branch}}.\\n\\n{{issue_body}}\\n\\n## Project Context\\n{{project_context}}\\n\\n## Plan\\n{{plan}}\\n\\n## Instructions\\n1. Implement the changes according to the plan.\\n2. Write clean, minimal code. Only change what is needed.\\n3. Follow the existing patterns and conventions.\\n4. Reuse existing code — do not duplicate.\\n5. Run tests if they exist.\\n6. Commit with clear, descriptive messages.\\n7. Push your branch.\\n8. Open a PR with .\\n\\nIf this is a retry after review feedback, the feedback is in your conversation history — address ALL requested changes, push, and update the PR.\\n\\n## Output\\nAt the end, output the PR URL on its own line."}, {"id": "review", "name": "Review", "type": "claude_agent", "model": "claude-opus-4-6", "retry": {"max_attempts": 1}, "outputs": [{"name": "review_result", "values": []}, {"name": "review_verdict", "values": ["APPROVED", "CHANGES_REQUESTED"]}], "targets": ["review_gate"], "timeout": 600, "position": {"x": 175, "y": 1120}, "status_label": "reviewing", "prompt_template": "You are a CODE REVIEWER agent. Review the PR on branch {{branch}} for issue #{{issue_number}}: {{issue_title}}.\\n\\n## Instructions\\n1. Read the PR diff and the relevant source files for full context.\\n2. Check for:\\n   - Bugs or logic errors\\n   - Security vulnerabilities\\n   - Missing edge cases\\n   - Code style consistency with the rest of the codebase\\n   - Whether tests exist and are adequate\\n   - Whether the implementation matches the requirements\\n3. Be pragmatic — do not nitpick style if the code works correctly.\\n\\nIf the code is good, respond with APPROVED.\\nIf changes are needed, respond with CHANGES_REQUESTED and list the specific fixes needed."}, {"id": "review_gate", "name": "Review Gate", "type": "condition", "branches": [{"value": "APPROVED", "target": "done"}, {"value": "CHANGES_REQUESTED", "target": "develop"}], "position": {"x": 240, "y": 1260}, "status_label": "checking review", "max_iterations": 2, "condition_field": "review_verdict", "iteration_counter": "review_round", "max_iterations_target": "failed"}, {"id": "done", "name": "Ready to Merge", "type": "end", "targets": [], "position": {"x": 120, "y": 1400}, "result_template": "Issue #{{issue_number}} implemented and reviewed. PR ready to merge."}, {"id": "failed", "name": "Failed", "type": "failed", "targets": [], "position": {"x": 360, "y": 1400}, "reason_template": "Pipeline failed after max review rounds for issue #{{issue_number}}"}, {"id": "refine_issue", "name": "Refine Issue", "type": "template", "targets": ["check_clarity"], "position": {"x": 613.9133972999781, "y": 597.4213181102986}, "template_id": 15, "status_label": "refining issue"}]}	2026-03-06 21:28:29.949563+00	2026-03-09 14:18:47.045594+00
24	Talavo Native Swift Development Pipeline	Talavo iOS-specific pipeline: blocker check → clarity check → analyze → plan → develop → review loop. Prompts are tailored to the Talavo SwiftUI browser app architecture.	{"name": "Talavo Native Swift Development Pipeline", "edges": [{"to": "check_blockers", "from": "start"}, {"to": "blocker_gate", "from": "check_blockers"}, {"to": "check_clarity", "from": "blocker_gate"}, {"to": "blocked_fail", "from": "blocker_gate"}, {"to": "clarity_gate", "from": "check_clarity"}, {"to": "analyze", "from": "clarity_gate"}, {"to": "refine_issue", "from": "clarity_gate"}, {"to": "vague_fail", "from": "clarity_gate"}, {"to": "check_clarity", "from": "refine_issue"}, {"to": "plan", "from": "analyze"}, {"to": "develop", "from": "plan"}, {"to": "review", "from": "develop"}, {"to": "review_gate", "from": "review"}, {"to": "done", "from": "review_gate"}, {"to": "develop", "from": "review_gate"}, {"to": "failed", "from": "review_gate"}], "nodes": [{"id": "start", "name": "Start", "type": "start", "targets": ["check_blockers"], "position": {"x": 120, "y": 0}}, {"id": "check_blockers", "name": "Check Blockers", "type": "claude_agent", "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "outputs": [{"name": "blocker_status", "values": ["READY", "BLOCKED"]}, {"name": "blocker_reason", "values": []}], "targets": ["blocker_gate"], "timeout": 300, "position": {"x": 120, "y": 140}, "status_label": "checking blockers", "prompt_template": "You are a BLOCKER CHECK agent for the Talavo iOS project (a native SwiftUI browser app).\\n\\nDetermine if issue #{{issue_number}} can be worked on right now.\\n\\nIssue: {{issue_title}}\\n{{issue_body}}\\n\\n## Instructions\\n1. Run `gh issue list --repo {{repo_path}} --state open --limit 50` to see all open issues.\\n2. Read the current issue carefully. Check if it references, depends on, or is blocked by any other open issue.\\n3. Look for keywords like: blocked by, depends on, requires, after #X, needs #X first.\\n4. Also check if the issue implies a dependency on work that has its own open issue.\\n\\nIf the issue IS blocked by another open issue, respond with BLOCKED and explain which issue(s) block it and why.\\nIf the issue is NOT blocked, respond with READY.\\n\\nBe concise. Do NOT explore the codebase — only check issues."}, {"id": "blocker_gate", "name": "Blocker Gate", "type": "condition", "branches": [{"value": "READY", "target": "check_clarity"}, {"value": "BLOCKED", "target": "blocked_fail"}], "position": {"x": 120, "y": 280}, "status_label": "checking blocker result", "condition_field": "blocker_status"}, {"id": "blocked_fail", "name": "Blocked", "type": "failed", "targets": [], "position": {"x": 0, "y": 420}, "reason_template": "Issue #{{issue_number}} is blocked: {{blocker_reason}}"}, {"id": "check_clarity", "name": "Check Clarity", "type": "claude_agent", "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "outputs": [{"name": "clarity_status", "values": ["CLEAR", "VAGUE"]}, {"name": "clarity_reason", "values": []}], "targets": ["clarity_gate"], "timeout": 300, "position": {"x": 240, "y": 420}, "status_label": "checking clarity", "prompt_template": "You are a CLARITY CHECK agent for the Talavo iOS project.\\n\\n## Instructions\\n1. Fetch the latest issue content: `gh issue view {{issue_number}} --repo {{repo_path}}`\\n2. Read the fetched issue and check if it has:\\n   - Clear requirements or acceptance criteria\\n   - Enough detail to understand what needs to be built or changed\\n   - Specific enough scope (not just a vague idea)\\n\\nContext: Talavo is a native SwiftUI browser app for iOS with features like ad blocking, video downloads, browsing history, shortcuts, sleep timer, and a Liquid Glass UI. The codebase uses MVVM, ObservableObject, UserDefaults persistence, and URLSession networking.\\n\\nAn issue does NOT need to be perfectly written. If a competent iOS developer can understand what to do from the title and description, it is CLEAR.\\n\\nIf the issue is too vague or missing critical information, respond with VAGUE and explain what is missing.\\nIf the issue is clear enough, respond with CLEAR.\\n\\nBe concise. Do NOT explore the codebase."}, {"id": "clarity_gate", "name": "Clarity Gate", "type": "condition", "branches": [{"value": "CLEAR", "target": "analyze"}, {"value": "VAGUE", "target": "refine_issue"}], "position": {"x": 402.7872512335307, "y": 558.6694709589194}, "status_label": "checking clarity result", "max_iterations": 1, "condition_field": "clarity_status", "max_iterations_target": "vague_fail"}, {"id": "refine_issue", "name": "Refine Issue", "type": "template", "targets": ["check_clarity"], "position": {"x": 120, "y": 700}, "template_id": 15, "status_label": "refining issue"}, {"id": "vague_fail", "name": "Too Vague", "type": "failed", "targets": [], "position": {"x": 413.2211616432273, "y": 827.7307879437454}, "reason_template": "Issue #{{issue_number}} is still too vague after refinement: {{clarity_reason}}"}, {"id": "analyze", "name": "Analyze Project", "type": "claude_agent", "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "outputs": [{"name": "project_context", "values": []}], "targets": ["plan"], "timeout": 600, "position": {"x": 600, "y": 700}, "status_label": "analyzing project", "prompt_template": "You are a PROJECT ANALYST agent for the Talavo iOS project. Explore the codebase and gather context for implementing issue #{{issue_number}}: {{issue_title}}.\\n\\n{{issue_body}}\\n\\n## Talavo iOS Architecture\\nTalavo is a native SwiftUI browser app at {{repo_path}}. Key architecture details:\\n\\n- **Structure:** App/ (TalavoApp, RootView, AppRouter), Core/ (Constants, DI/AppDependencies, Theme/AppTheme+AppColors, Utils, Widgets, Shaders), Features/ (AdBlock, Browser, Downloads, History, Home, Settings, etc.), LiveActivityExtension/\\n- **Pattern:** MVVM + service locator (AppDependencies). ViewModels are ObservableObject with @Published. 19 EnvironmentObjects injected at root.\\n- **UI:** 100% SwiftUI with Liquid Glass design (GlassCard, FrostedGlassBar, LiquidGlassModifier). iOS 26+ .glassEffect with .ultraThinMaterial fallback. MeshBackground for home. TapScaleButton for interactions. Metal shaders for ripple effects.\\n- **Browser:** WKWebView via UIViewRepresentable (VideoWebViewHolder, ShortsWebViewHolder). Prewarmed persistent instances. SPA DOM injection for in-page navigation. Script injection for ad blocking (ContentRuleManager, ScriptManager, ScriptletManager).\\n- **Persistence:** UserDefaults only (no Core Data/SwiftData). JSON encode/decode for complex types. TabPersistenceStore, HistoryStore, ShortcutsStore, SettingsStore.\\n- **Networking:** URLSession direct (no Alamofire). API at https://api.talavo.app. Custom user agent spoofing for YouTube.\\n- **Navigation:** Custom AppRouter with NavigationStack + Route enum.\\n- **Build:** XcodeGen (project.yml). iOS 16+ target. iPhone only. No external dependencies.\\n- **Localization:** 16 languages.\\n\\n## Instructions\\n1. Explore the specific files and folders relevant to this issue.\\n2. Look at how similar features are implemented in the codebase.\\n3. Check recent commits with `git log --oneline -20` to understand current development patterns.\\n4. Find existing code that can be reused.\\n5. Note any technical considerations specific to this issue.\\n\\n## Output\\nProvide a concise project context summary covering:\\n- Relevant existing files and their purpose\\n- Coding patterns and conventions to follow (naming, file organization, state management)\\n- Existing code/components that should be reused\\n- Technical considerations for the implementation\\n\\nKeep it focused on what the developer needs to know. Do NOT write code or create a plan."}, {"id": "plan", "name": "Plan", "type": "claude_agent", "model": "claude-opus-4-6", "outputs": [{"name": "plan", "values": []}], "targets": ["develop"], "timeout": 600, "position": {"x": 600, "y": 840}, "status_label": "planning", "prompt_template": "You are a PLANNER agent for the Talavo iOS project. Create an implementation plan for issue #{{issue_number}}: {{issue_title}}.\\n\\n{{issue_body}}\\n\\n## Project Context\\n{{project_context}}\\n\\n## Talavo Conventions to Follow\\n- New features go in Features/{FeatureName}/ with Views/, ViewModels/, Models/ subfolders\\n- ViewModels are ObservableObject classes with @Published properties\\n- Inject dependencies via AppDependencies and distribute as @EnvironmentObject\\n- Use GlassCard for card surfaces, FrostedGlassBar for bars, LiquidGlassModifier for custom glass shapes\\n- Use AppTheme.surface(for:), AppTheme.text(for:) for colors, AppColors for brand colors\\n- Persist data with UserDefaults via JSON encode/decode (follow SettingsStore/HistoryStore patterns)\\n- Network calls use URLSession.shared with async/await\\n- Navigation via AppRouter — add new Route cases as needed\\n- Use SF Symbols for icons\\n- Support dark mode via the theme system\\n- File naming: PascalCase for types, one type per file, file name matches type name\\n\\n## Instructions\\n1. Design a clear implementation approach following Talavo's patterns.\\n2. List every file to create or modify with specific changes needed.\\n3. Note any edge cases, risks, or dependencies.\\n4. Keep the plan actionable — bullet points, not essays.\\n5. Prefer reusing existing components (GlassCard, TapScaleButton, AppSheet, etc.).\\n\\n## Output\\nOutput ONLY the implementation plan. Do NOT write any code.\\nDo NOT open PRs, create branches, or make any git changes."}, {"id": "develop", "name": "Develop", "type": "claude_agent", "model": "claude-opus-4-6", "outputs": [{"name": "dev_result", "values": []}], "targets": ["review"], "timeout": 900, "position": {"x": 323.2499594552182, "y": 1015.9242841091784}, "resume_self": true, "status_label": "developing", "prompt_template": "You are a DEVELOPER agent for the Talavo iOS project. Implement the changes for issue #{{issue_number}}: {{issue_title}} on branch {{branch}}.\\n\\n{{issue_body}}\\n\\n## Project Context\\n{{project_context}}\\n\\n## Plan\\n{{plan}}\\n\\n## Talavo Development Rules\\n- Write SwiftUI views. No UIKit unless wrapping WKWebView or system APIs.\\n- Use Liquid Glass design: GlassCard for containers, FrostedGlassBar for bars, LiquidGlassModifier for custom shapes. Gate iOS 26 APIs with #available.\\n- Use AppTheme/AppColors for all colors. Never hardcode Color values.\\n- ViewModels must be ObservableObject with @Published. Add @MainActor if doing async work.\\n- Use [weak self] in all closures that capture self in ObservableObject classes.\\n- Persist with UserDefaults following existing store patterns (SettingsStore, HistoryStore).\\n- Network with URLSession async/await. Handle errors gracefully.\\n- Add new features under Features/{FeatureName}/Views/, ViewModels/, Models/.\\n- Register new dependencies in AppDependencies if needed.\\n- Add new routes to AppRouter.Route enum if adding screens.\\n- Use SF Symbols for icons. Support dark mode.\\n- Keep views under 200 lines. Extract subviews.\\n- Follow Swift API Design Guidelines for naming.\\n\\n## Instructions\\n1. Implement the changes according to the plan.\\n2. Write clean, minimal code. Only change what is needed.\\n3. Reuse existing components — do not duplicate.\\n4. Commit with clear, descriptive messages.\\n5. Push your branch.\\n6. Open a PR with `gh pr create`.\\n\\nIf this is a retry after review feedback, the feedback is in your conversation history — address ALL requested changes, push, and update the PR.\\n\\n## Output\\nAt the end, output the PR URL on its own line."}, {"id": "review", "name": "Review", "type": "claude_agent", "model": "claude-opus-4-6", "outputs": [{"name": "review_result", "values": []}, {"name": "review_verdict", "values": ["APPROVED", "CHANGES_REQUESTED"]}], "targets": ["review_gate"], "timeout": 600, "position": {"x": 665, "y": 1120}, "status_label": "reviewing", "prompt_template": "You are a CODE REVIEWER agent for the Talavo iOS project. Review the PR on branch {{branch}} for issue #{{issue_number}}: {{issue_title}}.\\n\\n## Talavo Review Checklist\\n1. **SwiftUI correctness** — Proper use of @State/@StateObject/@ObservedObject/@EnvironmentObject. No business logic in view bodies. Views under 200 lines.\\n2. **Memory safety** — [weak self] in closures, Combine cancellables stored, no retain cycles in WKWebView delegates/callbacks.\\n3. **Liquid Glass consistency** — Uses GlassCard/FrostedGlassBar/LiquidGlassModifier, not raw materials or custom blurs. iOS 26 APIs gated with #available.\\n4. **Theme compliance** — Uses AppTheme/AppColors, no hardcoded colors. Supports dark mode.\\n5. **Architecture** — Follows MVVM, new code in correct Feature folder, dependencies registered in AppDependencies.\\n6. **Persistence** — UserDefaults usage follows existing patterns. JSON encode/decode has error handling.\\n7. **Networking** — URLSession with async/await, proper error handling, no hardcoded URLs (use AppConstants).\\n8. **Code quality** — No force unwraps, no force casts, proper access control, no dead code.\\n9. **Matches requirements** — Implementation matches what the issue asked for.\\n\\n## Instructions\\n1. Read the PR diff: `gh pr diff --repo {{repo_path}}`\\n2. Read relevant source files for full context.\\n3. Be pragmatic — do not nitpick style if the code works correctly and follows Talavo conventions.\\n\\nIf the code is good, respond with APPROVED.\\nIf changes are needed, respond with CHANGES_REQUESTED and list specific fixes."}, {"id": "review_gate", "name": "Review Gate", "type": "condition", "branches": [{"value": "APPROVED", "target": "done"}, {"value": "CHANGES_REQUESTED", "target": "develop"}], "position": {"x": 600, "y": 1260}, "status_label": "checking review", "max_iterations": 2, "condition_field": "review_verdict", "iteration_counter": "review_round", "max_iterations_target": "failed"}, {"id": "done", "name": "Ready to Merge", "type": "end", "targets": [], "position": {"x": 480, "y": 1400}, "result_template": "Issue #{{issue_number}} implemented and reviewed. PR ready to merge."}, {"id": "failed", "name": "Failed", "type": "failed", "targets": [], "position": {"x": 720, "y": 1400}, "reason_template": "Pipeline failed after max review rounds for issue #{{issue_number}}"}]}	2026-03-15 08:55:52.047991+00	2026-03-15 10:11:11.892291+00
13	Talavo Architecture Analyzer	Analyzes a specified folder in the Talavo project for code quality, deduplication, UI improvements, modernization opportunities, and bugs.	{"name": "Talavo Architecture Analyzer", "edges": [{"to": "analyze_structure", "from": "start"}, {"to": "code_quality_and_bugs", "from": "analyze_structure"}, {"to": "deduplication_analysis", "from": "code_quality_and_bugs"}, {"to": "ui_review", "from": "deduplication_analysis"}, {"to": "modernization_check", "from": "ui_review"}, {"to": "compile_report", "from": "modernization_check"}, {"to": "check_critical", "from": "compile_report"}, {"to": "create_issues", "from": "check_critical"}, {"to": "end", "from": "check_critical"}, {"to": "end", "from": "create_issues"}], "nodes": [{"id": "start", "name": "Start", "type": "start", "targets": ["analyze_structure"], "position": {"x": 0, "y": 0}}, {"id": "analyze_structure", "name": "Analyze Folder Structure", "type": "claude_agent", "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "outputs": [{"name": "structure_analysis", "values": []}, {"name": "structure_severity", "values": ["CRITICAL", "HIGH", "MEDIUM", "LOW"]}], "targets": ["code_quality_and_bugs"], "timeout": 600, "position": {"x": 0, "y": 140}, "prompt_template": "You are a senior Flutter/Dart architect analyzing an iOS-focused Flutter project called Talavo.\\n\\nRepository: {{repo_path}}\\nWorking directory: {{worktree_path}}\\nTarget folder/area: {{task_description}}\\n\\nPerform a thorough structural analysis of the specified folder. This is a Flutter project primarily targeting iOS.\\n\\n1. **File & folder organization** — Are .dart files logically grouped by feature? Are screens, widgets, models, services, and providers properly separated? Are naming conventions consistent (snake_case for files, PascalCase for classes)?\\n2. **Architecture patterns** — What pattern is used (BLoC, Provider, Riverpod, Clean Architecture, MVVM)? Is it applied consistently across all features?\\n3. **Dependency flow** — Are there circular imports between Dart files? Are widgets directly calling repositories or APIs instead of going through proper layers?\\n4. **Separation of concerns** — Is business logic leaking into widgets? Are StatefulWidgets doing too much? Is data transformation happening in the UI layer?\\n5. **Module boundaries** — Are feature folders self-contained? Are there cross-feature imports that break module boundaries?\\n6. **iOS-specific structure** — Is the ios/ folder properly configured? Are platform channels organized? Are iOS-specific assets and configurations in the right place?\\n\\nList every file in the target folder recursively, then analyze the structure. Provide specific file paths for every finding.\\n\\nEnd your response with a severity rating: CRITICAL, HIGH, MEDIUM, or LOW."}, {"id": "code_quality_and_bugs", "name": "Code Quality & Bug Detection", "type": "claude_agent", "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "outputs": [{"name": "quality_analysis", "values": []}, {"name": "quality_severity", "values": ["CRITICAL", "HIGH", "MEDIUM", "LOW"]}], "targets": ["deduplication_analysis"], "timeout": 600, "position": {"x": 0, "y": 280}, "prompt_template": "You are a senior Flutter/Dart code reviewer and bug hunter analyzing an iOS-focused Flutter project called Talavo.\\n\\nRepository: {{repo_path}}\\nWorking directory: {{worktree_path}}\\nTarget folder/area: {{task_description}}\\n\\nPerform a deep code quality and bug analysis of the specified folder. Read every .dart file and inspect carefully.\\n\\n**Bug Detection:**\\n- Null safety violations — improper use of `!` operator, nullable types not handled, late variables that may not be initialized\\n- Future/async misuse — missing `await`, unhandled Future errors, setState after dispose\\n- Memory leaks — StreamSubscription not cancelled, AnimationController not disposed, listeners not removed in dispose()\\n- State management bugs — stale state, missing notifyListeners(), incorrect provider scoping\\n- Platform channel errors — unhandled PlatformException, missing iOS method channel implementations\\n- Navigation bugs — context used after widget unmounted, Navigator stack issues\\n- iOS-specific crashes — missing Info.plist permissions, unsafe platform checks\\n\\n**Code Quality:**\\n- Widget build methods that are too long (>50 lines) or do too many things\\n- Deeply nested widget trees that should be extracted into separate widgets\\n- Business logic inside widgets instead of in providers/blocs/services\\n- Inconsistent Dart style — not following Effective Dart guidelines\\n- Magic numbers/strings that should be constants or theme values\\n- Dead code, unused imports, unreachable branches\\n- Missing or incorrect type annotations, overuse of `dynamic`\\n- Anti-patterns: setState in initState, building widgets in loops without keys, synchronous file I/O on main isolate\\n\\nFor every finding, provide:\\n- The exact file path and line number(s)\\n- What the issue is\\n- Why it matters\\n- A suggested Dart/Flutter fix\\n\\nEnd your response with a severity rating: CRITICAL, HIGH, MEDIUM, or LOW."}, {"id": "deduplication_analysis", "name": "Deduplication Analysis", "type": "claude_agent", "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "outputs": [{"name": "dedup_analysis", "values": []}, {"name": "dedup_severity", "values": ["CRITICAL", "HIGH", "MEDIUM", "LOW"]}], "targets": ["ui_review"], "timeout": 600, "position": {"x": 0, "y": 420}, "prompt_template": "You are a Dart/Flutter code deduplication specialist analyzing an iOS-focused Flutter project called Talavo.\\n\\nRepository: {{repo_path}}\\nWorking directory: {{worktree_path}}\\nTarget folder/area: {{task_description}}\\n\\nAnalyze the specified folder for code duplication and redundancy. Read all .dart files and compare them.\\n\\n**Look for:**\\n1. **Copy-pasted widgets** — Identical or near-identical widget trees across screens/pages. Similar Container/Padding/Column patterns that differ only in text or callbacks\\n2. **Similar widget patterns** — Screens or components that follow the same structure with minor variations (e.g., similar list pages, similar form pages, similar detail pages)\\n3. **Repeated models/DTOs** — Duplicate data classes, fromJson/toJson boilerplate that could use code generation (freezed, json_serializable)\\n4. **Repeated styling** — Same TextStyle, BoxDecoration, EdgeInsets, or Color values hardcoded in multiple widgets instead of using a shared theme or constants\\n5. **Utility duplication** — Common operations (date formatting, string manipulation, validation) reimplemented in multiple files instead of shared extension methods or utility classes\\n6. **API/service duplication** — Similar HTTP call patterns, repeated error handling, duplicate repository methods\\n7. **State management boilerplate** — Repeated provider/bloc patterns that could be abstracted into a base class\\n\\nFor each finding:\\n- List the exact .dart files and line ranges that are duplicated\\n- Show what Dart/Flutter code is repeated\\n- Suggest how to consolidate (shared widget, mixin, extension method, base class, code generation)\\n- Estimate lines of Dart code that could be removed\\n\\nEnd your response with a severity rating: CRITICAL, HIGH, MEDIUM, or LOW."}, {"id": "ui_review", "name": "UI & UX Review", "type": "claude_agent", "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "outputs": [{"name": "ui_analysis", "values": []}, {"name": "ui_severity", "values": ["CRITICAL", "HIGH", "MEDIUM", "LOW"]}], "targets": ["modernization_check"], "timeout": 600, "position": {"x": 0, "y": 560}, "prompt_template": "You are a Flutter UI/UX code reviewer specializing in iOS app best practices, analyzing a Flutter project called Talavo.\\n\\nRepository: {{repo_path}}\\nWorking directory: {{worktree_path}}\\nTarget folder/area: {{task_description}}\\n\\nAnalyze the specified folder for Flutter UI and UX code issues. Read all widget files, screens, themes, and styling code.\\n\\n**Analyze:**\\n1. **Widget design** — Are widgets reusable and composable? Are build() methods too large? Should StatelessWidget be used instead of StatefulWidget? Are there god-widgets doing too much?\\n2. **State management** — Unnecessary rebuilds? Is state lifted too high or too low? Missing Consumer/Selector for granular rebuilds? Are providers scoped correctly?\\n3. **iOS design compliance** — Does the UI follow iOS Human Interface Guidelines? Are CupertinoWidget alternatives used where appropriate? Proper use of SafeArea, iOS-style navigation (CupertinoNavigationBar), iOS-appropriate gestures?\\n4. **Responsive layout** — Hardcoded pixel dimensions instead of MediaQuery/LayoutBuilder? Does the layout work across iPhone SE, standard iPhones, and iPhone Pro Max sizes? Missing SafeArea for notch/Dynamic Island?\\n5. **Theme consistency** — Hardcoded colors, font sizes, padding instead of using Theme.of(context)? Inconsistent spacing that should use a design system? Dark mode support?\\n6. **Performance** — Unnecessary widget rebuilds, missing const constructors, ListView without itemBuilder for long lists, heavy computation in build(), missing RepaintBoundary for complex animations, images not cached\\n7. **User feedback** — Missing loading indicators, error widgets, empty state placeholders, pull-to-refresh, haptic feedback for iOS\\n8. **Navigation** — Inconsistent navigation patterns, missing hero animations, improper use of Navigator 2.0 or GoRouter, missing iOS back swipe gesture support\\n\\nFor each finding provide the .dart file path, line numbers, what the issue is, and a concrete Flutter/Dart suggestion.\\n\\nIf the target folder has no UI code, state that clearly and skip this analysis.\\n\\nEnd your response with a severity rating: CRITICAL, HIGH, MEDIUM, or LOW."}, {"id": "modernization_check", "name": "Modernization Check", "type": "claude_agent", "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "outputs": [{"name": "modernization_analysis", "values": []}, {"name": "modernization_severity", "values": ["CRITICAL", "HIGH", "MEDIUM", "LOW"]}], "targets": ["compile_report"], "timeout": 600, "position": {"x": 0, "y": 700}, "prompt_template": "You are a Flutter/Dart modernization consultant analyzing an iOS-focused Flutter project called Talavo.\\n\\nRepository: {{repo_path}}\\nWorking directory: {{worktree_path}}\\nTarget folder/area: {{task_description}}\\n\\nAnalyze the specified folder for outdated Flutter/Dart patterns and modernization opportunities. Read the .dart source files, pubspec.yaml, and any configuration files.\\n\\n**Check for:**\\n1. **Deprecated Flutter/Dart APIs** — Usage of deprecated widgets (e.g., FlatButton→TextButton, RaisedButton→ElevatedButton), deprecated methods, or packages with newer alternatives\\n2. **Outdated Dart patterns** — Old-style null handling pre-null-safety, unnecessary null checks on non-nullable types, FutureBuilder where async/await with state management would be cleaner\\n3. **Dart 3+ features** — Missing usage of records, patterns, sealed classes, switch expressions, if-case, class modifiers (final, interface, mixin class) where they would improve the code\\n4. **Flutter framework updates** — Using old Material 2 widgets instead of Material 3, missing ThemeExtension usage, old Navigator 1.0 patterns where declarative routing (GoRouter) would be better\\n5. **Dependency health** — Check pubspec.yaml for outdated or unmaintained packages, packages with better alternatives, missing null-safe versions\\n6. **Build & tooling** — Outdated analysis_options.yaml rules, missing recommended lints, outdated iOS deployment target in Podfile/Xcode config, missing build_runner or code generation where beneficial\\n7. **iOS-specific modernization** — Old iOS deployment targets, deprecated CocoaPods configurations, missing App Store privacy manifests, outdated Xcode project settings\\n\\nFor each finding:\\n- Identify the outdated pattern with file path and lines\\n- Explain the modern Flutter/Dart replacement\\n- Assess migration effort (trivial, moderate, significant)\\n- Note any breaking changes the modernization would introduce\\n\\nEnd your response with a severity rating: CRITICAL, HIGH, MEDIUM, or LOW."}, {"id": "compile_report", "name": "Compile Final Report", "type": "claude_agent", "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "outputs": [{"name": "final_report", "values": []}, {"name": "needs_issues", "values": ["YES", "NO"]}], "targets": ["check_critical"], "timeout": 600, "position": {"x": 0, "y": 840}, "prompt_template": "You are a Flutter technical lead compiling a comprehensive architecture review report for the Talavo iOS Flutter app.\\n\\nRepository: {{repo_path}}\\nTarget folder/area: {{task_description}}\\n\\nBelow are the results from five independent analyses of this Flutter/Dart codebase. Compile them into a single, actionable report.\\n\\n---\\n**STRUCTURE ANALYSIS** (Severity: {{structure_severity}})\\n{{structure_analysis}}\\n\\n---\\n**CODE QUALITY & BUGS** (Severity: {{quality_severity}})\\n{{quality_analysis}}\\n\\n---\\n**DEDUPLICATION** (Severity: {{dedup_severity}})\\n{{dedup_analysis}}\\n\\n---\\n**UI/UX REVIEW** (Severity: {{ui_severity}})\\n{{ui_analysis}}\\n\\n---\\n**MODERNIZATION** (Severity: {{modernization_severity}})\\n{{modernization_analysis}}\\n\\n---\\n\\nCreate a final report with:\\n\\n1. **Executive Summary** — 3-5 sentence overview of the codebase health\\n2. **Critical Findings** — Issues that need immediate attention (bugs, security, crashes)\\n3. **High Priority Improvements** — Important but not urgent improvements\\n4. **Quick Wins** — Low-effort changes with high impact\\n5. **Long-term Recommendations** — Larger refactoring or modernization efforts\\n6. **Metrics Summary** — Overall severity, estimated total issues found, categories breakdown\\n\\nRank all findings by priority. Be specific with file paths and actionable suggestions.\\n\\nEnd with an overall health rating: CRITICAL, NEEDS_WORK, FAIR, or GOOD.\\n\\nRespond with either YES or NO: are there critical issues that need immediate GitHub issues created?"}, {"id": "check_critical", "name": "Critical Issues Found?", "type": "condition", "branches": {"NO": "end", "YES": "create_issues"}, "position": {"x": 0, "y": 980}, "default_branch": "end", "condition_field": "needs_issues"}, {"id": "create_issues", "name": "Create GitHub Issues", "type": "claude_agent", "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "outputs": [{"name": "created_issues", "values": []}], "targets": ["end"], "timeout": 300, "position": {"x": 65, "y": 1120}, "prompt_template": "You are a project manager creating GitHub issues for critical findings.\\n\\nRepository: {{repo_path}}\\nWorking directory: {{worktree_path}}\\n\\nBased on the architecture review report below, create GitHub issues for the CRITICAL findings only. Use the `gh` CLI tool.\\n\\n{{final_report}}\\n\\nFor each critical finding:\\n1. Create a GitHub issue with a clear, descriptive title\\n2. Include the file paths, line numbers, and description of the issue\\n3. Include a suggested fix\\n4. Add appropriate labels\\n\\nCreate the issues using: gh issue create --repo {{repo_path}} --title \\"...\\" --body \\"...\\"\\n\\nList all created issue numbers when done."}, {"id": "end", "name": "Analysis Complete", "type": "end", "targets": [], "position": {"x": 0, "y": 1260}, "result_template": "{{final_report}}"}]}	2026-03-07 15:39:54.20363+00	2026-03-07 16:03:22.286682+00
15	Issue Refiner	Checks if a GitHub issue is detailed enough, and if not, analyzes the codebase and rewrites it	{"name": "Issue Refiner", "edges": [{"to": "check_quality", "from": "start"}, {"to": "analyze", "from": "quality_gate"}, {"to": "skip_done", "from": "quality_gate"}, {"to": "done", "from": "rewrite"}, {"to": "rewrite", "from": "analyze"}, {"to": "quality_gate", "from": "check_quality"}], "nodes": [{"id": "start", "name": "Start", "type": "start", "targets": ["check_quality"], "position": {"x": 120, "y": 0}}, {"id": "check_quality", "name": "Check Quality", "type": "claude_agent", "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "outputs": [{"name": "issue_quality", "values": ["GOOD", "VAGUE"]}], "targets": ["quality_gate"], "timeout": 120, "position": {"x": 120, "y": 140}, "status_label": "checking", "prompt_template": "You are evaluating whether GitHub issue #{{issue_number}} is detailed enough for a developer to implement.\\n\\nIssue title: {{issue_title}}\\nIssue body:\\n{{issue_body}}\\n\\nA GOOD issue has:\\n- Clear description of what needs to change\\n- Enough context for a developer to start without asking questions\\n- Some notion of acceptance criteria or expected behavior\\n\\nA VAGUE issue is missing most of the above — it is just a title, a one-liner, or lacks actionable detail.\\n\\nRespond with exactly one word: GOOD or VAGUE"}, {"id": "quality_gate", "name": "Quality Gate", "type": "condition", "branches": [{"value": "VAGUE", "target": "analyze"}, {"value": "GOOD", "target": "skip_done"}], "position": {"x": 120, "y": 280}, "condition_field": "issue_quality"}, {"id": "analyze", "name": "Analyze Codebase", "type": "claude_agent", "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "outputs": [], "targets": ["rewrite"], "timeout": 300, "position": {"x": 240, "y": 420}, "status_label": "analyzing", "prompt_template": "You are analyzing GitHub issue #{{issue_number}} in this repository to help rewrite it with proper detail.\\n\\nIssue title: {{issue_title}}\\nIssue body:\\n{{issue_body}}\\n\\nYour task:\\n1. Read and understand what this issue is asking for\\n2. Explore the codebase to understand:\\n   - Which files and modules are affected\\n   - What the current behavior is (if it is a bug or change request)\\n   - What dependencies or related code exists\\n   - Any relevant patterns or conventions in the codebase\\n\\nOutput a structured analysis covering:\\n- What the issue is really asking for (in concrete terms)\\n- Affected files and modules (list actual file paths you found)\\n- Current behavior vs expected behavior\\n- Key technical considerations and edge cases\\n- Suggested labels that are used in this repo\\n- Estimated complexity: small, medium, or large"}, {"id": "rewrite", "name": "Rewrite Issue", "type": "claude_agent", "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "outputs": [], "targets": ["done"], "timeout": 300, "position": {"x": 240, "y": 560}, "status_label": "rewriting", "prompt_template": "You are rewriting GitHub issue #{{issue_number}} to make it clear and actionable for a developer.\\n\\nOriginal title: {{issue_title}}\\nOriginal body:\\n{{issue_body}}\\n\\nCodebase analysis from the previous step:\\n{{_raw_analyze}}\\n\\nRewrite this issue with a proper, detailed description using this structure:\\n\\n## Summary\\n1-2 sentence clear description of what needs to be done.\\n\\n## Current Behavior\\nWhat happens now (if applicable, otherwise omit this section).\\n\\n## Expected Behavior\\nWhat should happen after implementation.\\n\\n## Affected Files\\nList the specific files and modules that will need changes.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\nBulleted checklist of specific, testable criteria.\\n\\n## Technical Notes\\nImplementation hints or considerations from the codebase analysis.\\n\\nThen update the issue on GitHub:\\n1. Run: gh issue edit {{issue_number}} --body \\"<your rewritten body>\\"\\n2. Only change the title if the original is truly unclear: gh issue edit {{issue_number}} --title \\"<better title>\\"\\n3. Add the appropriate label if not already set: gh issue edit {{issue_number}} --add-label \\"<label>\\"\\n\\nThe rewritten issue must be detailed enough that a developer can start implementing without needing to ask clarifying questions."}, {"id": "done", "name": "Refined", "type": "end", "targets": [], "position": {"x": 240, "y": 700}, "result_template": "Issue #{{issue_number}} refined successfully"}, {"id": "skip_done", "name": "Already Good", "type": "end", "targets": [], "position": {"x": 0, "y": 420}, "result_template": "Issue #{{issue_number}} is already detailed enough — no changes made"}]}	2026-03-08 10:57:56.014126+00	2026-03-08 12:52:03.754972+00
21	Flutter Dependency Updater	Audit and update all Flutter dependencies to latest major versions, one by one. Fixes or reverts broken updates, creates PR with report.	{"name": "Flutter Dependency Updater", "edges": [{"to": "audit", "from": "start"}, {"to": "updater", "from": "audit"}, {"to": "build_check", "from": "updater"}, {"to": "create_pr", "from": "build_check"}, {"to": "emergency_fix", "from": "build_check"}, {"to": "fix_check", "from": "emergency_fix"}, {"to": "create_pr", "from": "fix_check"}, {"to": "fail", "from": "fix_check"}, {"to": "done", "from": "create_pr"}], "nodes": [{"id": "start", "name": "Start", "type": "start", "targets": ["audit"], "position": {"x": 250, "y": 0}}, {"id": "audit", "name": "Audit Dependencies", "type": "claude_agent", "model": null, "retry": {"max_attempts": 1}, "extract": {}, "outputs": [], "targets": ["updater"], "timeout": 300, "position": {"x": 250, "y": 150}, "requires": [], "status_label": "auditing dependencies", "prompt_template": "You are auditing Flutter dependencies for major version updates.\\nThe repo is already pulled and on a fresh state.\\n\\nSteps:\\n1. Create a new branch: `chore/update-flutter-deps`\\n2. Navigate to the Flutter project directory (look for pubspec.yaml)\\n3. Run `flutter pub outdated` to see all outdated dependencies\\n4. Identify all dependencies that have a newer MAJOR version available (resolvable column)\\n5. List them clearly\\n\\nOutput your findings as a structured list. For each outdated dependency, include:\\n- Package name\\n- Current version\\n- Latest available major version\\n\\nIf no dependencies need major updates, say NONE.\\nEnd your response with the full list in this exact format:\\nOUTDATED_DEPS: package1 current1 latest1, package2 current2 latest2, ...\\nOr: OUTDATED_DEPS: NONE"}, {"id": "updater", "name": "Update & Validate", "type": "claude_agent", "model": null, "retry": {"max_attempts": 1}, "extract": {}, "outputs": [{"name": "build_status", "values": ["PASS", "FAIL"]}], "targets": ["build_check"], "timeout": 1800, "position": {"x": 250, "y": 350}, "requires": [], "resume_from": "audit", "status_label": "updating dependencies", "prompt_template": "You are updating Flutter dependencies ONE BY ONE to their latest major versions.\\n\\nIMPORTANT RULES:\\n- Update ONE dependency at a time in pubspec.yaml\\n- After each update: run `flutter pub get`, then `dart analyze`, then `flutter build apk --debug`\\n- If analyze or build fails after updating a dep:\\n  1. Try to fix the breaking changes (API changes, deprecations, etc.)\\n  2. Run analyze + build again after fixing\\n  3. If you cannot fix it after a reasonable attempt, REVERT that dependency to its original version\\n  4. Run `flutter pub get` again after reverting to restore clean state\\n- After each successful update (or revert), `git add -A && git commit` with a descriptive message\\n- Keep track of what was updated successfully and what had to be reverted\\n\\nAfter processing ALL dependencies, write a summary report:\\n## Updated Successfully\\n- package_name: old_version -> new_version\\n\\n## Failed to Update (reverted)\\n- package_name: old_version -> attempted_version — reason for failure\\n\\n## No Changes Needed\\n- (if applicable)\\n\\nEnd with: BUILD_STATUS: PASS or BUILD_STATUS: FAIL"}, {"id": "build_check", "name": "Build OK?", "type": "condition", "branches": {"FAIL": "emergency_fix", "PASS": "create_pr"}, "position": {"x": 250, "y": 550}, "default_branch": "create_pr", "condition_field": "build_status"}, {"id": "emergency_fix", "name": "Emergency Fix", "type": "claude_agent", "model": null, "retry": {"max_attempts": 1}, "extract": {}, "outputs": [{"name": "fixed", "values": ["YES", "NO"]}], "targets": ["fix_check"], "timeout": 1200, "position": {"x": 500, "y": 700}, "requires": ["build_status"], "resume_from": "updater", "status_label": "fixing build errors", "prompt_template": "The Flutter build is failing after dependency updates.\\n\\n1. Run `dart analyze` and `flutter build apk --debug` to see current errors\\n2. Fix what you can\\n3. If a specific dependency update is causing unfixable errors, revert JUST that dependency\\n4. Run `flutter pub get` after any reverts\\n5. Keep going until `flutter build apk --debug` passes\\n6. Commit your fixes\\n\\nThe build MUST pass. Revert problematic deps if needed.\\n\\nEnd with: FIXED: YES or FIXED: NO"}, {"id": "fix_check", "name": "Fixed?", "type": "condition", "branches": {"NO": "fail", "YES": "create_pr"}, "position": {"x": 500, "y": 900}, "default_branch": "fail", "condition_field": "fixed"}, {"id": "create_pr", "name": "Create PR", "type": "claude_agent", "model": null, "retry": {"max_attempts": 1}, "extract": {"pr_url": "regex:https://github\\\\.com/[^\\\\s)]+/pull/\\\\d+"}, "outputs": ["pr_url"], "targets": ["done"], "timeout": 300, "position": {"x": 250, "y": 1050}, "requires": [], "resume_from": "updater", "status_label": "creating PR", "prompt_template": "Create a pull request with all the dependency updates.\\n\\n1. Push the current branch to origin\\n2. Create a PR with:\\n   - Title: `chore: update Flutter dependencies`\\n   - Body: Include a full report of what was updated, what was reverted, and why\\n   - List all version changes\\n3. The PR body should be a clear changelog\\n\\nOutput the PR URL at the end."}, {"id": "done", "name": "Done", "type": "end", "status": "done", "targets": [], "position": {"x": 250, "y": 1200}}, {"id": "fail", "name": "Failed", "type": "end", "status": "failed", "targets": [], "position": {"x": 500, "y": 1050}}]}	2026-03-13 18:28:46.20739+00	2026-03-13 19:16:09.325864+00
25	Talavo iOS Architecture Analyzer	Analyzes a specified folder in the native Swift Talavo iOS browser app for code quality, deduplication, UI improvements, modernization opportunities, and bugs.	{"name": "Talavo iOS Architecture Analyzer", "edges": [{"to": "analyze_structure", "from": "start"}, {"to": "code_quality_and_bugs", "from": "analyze_structure"}, {"to": "deduplication_analysis", "from": "code_quality_and_bugs"}, {"to": "ui_review", "from": "deduplication_analysis"}, {"to": "modernization_check", "from": "ui_review"}, {"to": "compile_report", "from": "modernization_check"}, {"to": "check_critical", "from": "compile_report"}, {"to": "create_issues", "from": "check_critical"}, {"to": "end", "from": "check_critical"}, {"to": "end", "from": "create_issues"}], "nodes": [{"id": "start", "name": "Start", "type": "start"}, {"id": "analyze_structure", "name": "Analyze Folder Structure", "type": "claude_agent", "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "outputs": [{"name": "structure_analysis", "values": []}, {"name": "structure_severity", "values": ["CRITICAL", "HIGH", "MEDIUM", "LOW"]}], "timeout": 600, "prompt_template": "You are a senior iOS/Swift architect analyzing Talavo, a native SwiftUI browser app for iOS.\\n\\nRepository: {{repo_path}}\\nWorking directory: {{worktree_path}}\\nTarget folder/area: {{task_description}}\\n\\n**Project context:** Talavo is an iOS browser app built with 100% SwiftUI + WKWebView (via UIViewRepresentable). It uses MVVM + a service locator pattern (AppDependencies). The project is generated with XcodeGen (project.yml). There are no external dependencies — it's purely native (URLSession, WebKit, AVFoundation, Combine). The app targets iOS 16+ and is iPhone-only.\\n\\n**Codebase structure convention:**\\n- `App/` — TalavoApp.swift, RootView, AppRouter\\n- `Core/` — Constants, DI (AppDependencies), Theme (AppTheme, AppColors), Utils, Widgets (reusable UI), Shaders (Metal)\\n- `Features/` — Feature modules (AdBlock, Browser, Downloads, History, Home, Settings, etc.) each with Views/, ViewModels/, Models/ subfolders\\n- `Resources/` — Assets\\n- `LiveActivityExtension/` — Lock screen widget extension\\n\\nPerform a thorough structural analysis of the specified folder:\\n\\n1. **File & folder organization** — Are .swift files in the right feature folder? Do feature folders consistently have Views/, ViewModels/, Models/ subfolders? Are naming conventions consistent?\\n2. **MVVM consistency** — Does each feature follow the MVVM pattern? Are there Views with business logic that should be in a ViewModel? Are there ViewModels that are actually just data stores?\\n3. **AppDependencies (DI)** — Is the service locator being bypassed? Are services instantiated directly in Views instead of being injected? Currently 19 EnvironmentObjects are injected at the root — are any unnecessary or could they be consolidated?\\n4. **Separation of concerns** — Is business logic leaking into SwiftUI Views? Are ViewModels doing too much (networking + persistence + UI state)? Is WebView JavaScript injection logic properly isolated in managers (ScriptManager, ContentRuleManager)?\\n5. **Module boundaries** — Are feature folders self-contained? Are there cross-feature imports that create tight coupling? Could any features be extracted into Swift packages?\\n6. **XcodeGen / project.yml** — Is the project.yml properly configured? Are targets and schemes correct?\\n\\nList every file in the target folder recursively, then analyze the structure. Provide specific file paths for every finding.\\n\\nEnd your response with a severity rating: CRITICAL, HIGH, MEDIUM, or LOW."}, {"id": "code_quality_and_bugs", "name": "Code Quality & Bug Detection", "type": "claude_agent", "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "outputs": [{"name": "quality_analysis", "values": []}, {"name": "quality_severity", "values": ["CRITICAL", "HIGH", "MEDIUM", "LOW"]}], "timeout": 600, "prompt_template": "You are a senior Swift/iOS code reviewer and bug hunter analyzing Talavo, a native SwiftUI browser app.\\n\\nRepository: {{repo_path}}\\nWorking directory: {{worktree_path}}\\nTarget folder/area: {{task_description}}\\n\\n**Project context:** Talavo is a SwiftUI browser app using WKWebView (UIViewRepresentable). State is managed via ObservableObject + @Published properties, distributed as @EnvironmentObject from the root. Persistence is entirely UserDefaults (no Core Data/SwiftData/Keychain). Networking uses URLSession directly against https://api.talavo.app. The app has persistent prewarmed WebView instances (VideoWebViewHolder, ShortsWebViewHolder) and uses JavaScript injection for SPA navigation and ad blocking.\\n\\nRead every .swift file in the specified folder and inspect carefully.\\n\\n**Bug Detection:**\\n- Force unwrapping (`!`) on optionals that could be nil — missing guard/if-let\\n- Retain cycles — missing `[weak self]` in closures, especially in Combine subscriptions, WKWebView callbacks, and timer closures\\n- Main thread violations — UI updates (@Published property changes) happening off the main thread, especially in URLSession completion handlers and WKNavigationDelegate callbacks\\n- WKWebView issues — JavaScript evaluation without error handling, WKScriptMessageHandler retain cycles, missing WKNavigationDelegate edge cases, WKProcessPool lifecycle issues\\n- Memory leaks — Combine AnyCancellable not stored, NotificationCenter/Darwin notification observers not removed, WebView not properly cleaned up\\n- UserDefaults misuse — sensitive data (device IDs, user tokens) stored in UserDefaults instead of Keychain, missing synchronize in critical paths, JSON encoding/decoding without error handling\\n- Crash-prone patterns — force casting (`as!`), array index out of bounds, unhandled thrown errors in async contexts\\n- Concurrency issues — data races in shared state, missing @MainActor annotations on ViewModel classes\\n\\n**Code Quality:**\\n- SwiftUI Views over 200 lines that should be decomposed\\n- ViewModels or Managers doing too many things (BrowserViewModel, DownloadService)\\n- Business logic inside SwiftUI view bodies instead of ViewModels\\n- Magic numbers/strings — hardcoded URLs, timing values, UserDefaults keys that should be constants\\n- Dead code, unused imports, unreachable branches\\n- Missing access control — properties/methods that should be `private` or `fileprivate`\\n- Anti-patterns: excessive EnvironmentObject usage, singletons that should be injected, completion handlers where async/await would be cleaner\\n\\nFor every finding provide the exact file path, line number(s), what the issue is, why it matters, and a suggested Swift fix.\\n\\nEnd your response with a severity rating: CRITICAL, HIGH, MEDIUM, or LOW."}, {"id": "deduplication_analysis", "name": "Deduplication Analysis", "type": "claude_agent", "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "outputs": [{"name": "dedup_analysis", "values": []}, {"name": "dedup_severity", "values": ["CRITICAL", "HIGH", "MEDIUM", "LOW"]}], "timeout": 600, "prompt_template": "You are a Swift code deduplication specialist analyzing Talavo, a native SwiftUI browser app.\\n\\nRepository: {{repo_path}}\\nWorking directory: {{worktree_path}}\\nTarget folder/area: {{task_description}}\\n\\n**Project context:** Talavo has feature modules under Features/ (Browser, Downloads, History, Home, Settings, etc.) with SwiftUI views, ObservableObject ViewModels, and service classes. It uses custom UI components like GlassCard, FrostedGlassBar, TapScaleButton, and AppSheet. Styling uses AppTheme/AppColors. Two WebView holders (VideoWebViewHolder, ShortsWebViewHolder) manage persistent WKWebView instances.\\n\\nRead all .swift files in the specified folder and compare them.\\n\\n**Look for:**\\n1. **Duplicated SwiftUI views** — Similar view bodies across screens (e.g., similar list rows, similar overlays, similar sheet content). Repeated VStack/HStack/ZStack patterns that differ only in content or callbacks\\n2. **WebView holder duplication** — VideoWebViewHolder and ShortsWebViewHolder likely share significant code (WKWebView setup, configuration, navigation delegates, JavaScript injection). Could they share a base class or protocol?\\n3. **Repeated styling** — Same colors (AppColors references), font sizes, padding values, or glass effects hardcoded across multiple views instead of using shared ViewModifiers\\n4. **ViewModel boilerplate** — Repeated @Published property patterns, similar UserDefaults read/write logic, similar URLSession networking code across ViewModels/Stores\\n5. **UserDefaults patterns** — Repeated JSON encode/decode boilerplate for persisting models. Similar get/set patterns that could use a property wrapper\\n6. **Networking duplication** — Similar URLSession.shared.data(from:) patterns, repeated JSON decoding, duplicate error handling across UserManager, DownloadService, ReferralManager, TrialManager\\n7. **JavaScript injection duplication** — Similar evaluateJavaScript patterns, repeated script construction, duplicate message handler setup\\n\\nFor each finding:\\n- List the exact .swift files and line ranges that are duplicated\\n- Show what code is repeated\\n- Suggest how to consolidate (protocol, extension, generic type, ViewModifier, base class, property wrapper)\\n- Estimate lines of code that could be removed\\n\\nEnd your response with a severity rating: CRITICAL, HIGH, MEDIUM, or LOW."}, {"id": "ui_review", "name": "UI & UX Review", "type": "claude_agent", "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "outputs": [{"name": "ui_analysis", "values": []}, {"name": "ui_severity", "values": ["CRITICAL", "HIGH", "MEDIUM", "LOW"]}], "timeout": 600, "prompt_template": "You are an iOS UI/UX code reviewer analyzing Talavo, a native SwiftUI browser app that uses Apple's Liquid Glass design language.\\n\\nRepository: {{repo_path}}\\nWorking directory: {{worktree_path}}\\nTarget folder/area: {{task_description}}\\n\\n**Project context:** Talavo is 100% SwiftUI (no storyboards/UIKit views except WKWebView wrappers). It uses a custom design system: AppTheme for color resolution, AppColors for brand colors (talavoMint, talavoTeal), GlassCard/FrostedGlassBar for Liquid Glass surfaces, MeshBackground for gradient home screen, TapScaleButton for interactive buttons, and Metal shaders for ripple effects. Navigation uses a custom AppRouter with NavigationStack. The app targets iOS 16+ with iOS 26+ checks for native .glassEffect API (falling back to .ultraThinMaterial).\\n\\n**Analyze:**\\n1. **View composition** — Are SwiftUI view bodies concise (<40 lines)? Are subviews properly extracted? Are there god-views doing layout + logic + styling all at once?\\n2. **State management correctness** — Incorrect @State vs @StateObject vs @ObservedObject vs @EnvironmentObject usage? Views re-rendering unnecessarily due to observing entire ObservableObjects when only one property changed? Are any of the 19 EnvironmentObjects causing unnecessary redraws?\\n3. **Liquid Glass consistency** — Is GlassCard used consistently for card surfaces? Are there views using raw .ultraThinMaterial or custom blur instead of the GlassCard/LiquidGlassModifier components? Is the iOS 26 .glassEffect properly feature-gated with #available? Are backgrounds translucent to let glass effects work? Does the FrostedGlassBar appear consistently for navigation/toolbars? Flag any opaque surfaces that break the glass aesthetic.\\n4. **AppTheme/AppColors usage** — Are views using AppTheme.surface/AppTheme.text for color resolution, or hardcoding Color values? Are AppColors constants used consistently? Does every view properly support dark mode via the theme system?\\n5. **Responsive layout** — Hardcoded dimensions that won't work across iPhone SE to Pro Max? Missing SafeArea handling for Dynamic Island? Proper keyboard avoidance (the app has a custom KeyboardObserver)?\\n6. **Performance** — Heavy work in SwiftUI body, missing const/static for repeated values, LazyVStack/LazyHStack for long lists, unnecessary GeometryReader usage, AnyView type erasure killing diffing performance, missing .task over .onAppear for async\\n7. **Animations & haptics** — Are animations consistent with the app's style (TapScaleButton, breathing effects)? Proper use of UIImpactFeedbackGenerator? Are Metal shader effects properly gated for device capability?\\n8. **User feedback** — Missing loading states (ProgressView), error handling UI, empty states, pull-to-refresh where appropriate\\n9. **Navigation via AppRouter** — Is AppRouter used consistently? Are there views doing manual NavigationLink or sheet presentation instead of going through the router? Is deep linking supported?\\n\\nFor each finding provide the .swift file path, line numbers, what the issue is, and a concrete Swift suggestion.\\n\\nEnd your response with a severity rating: CRITICAL, HIGH, MEDIUM, or LOW."}, {"id": "modernization_check", "name": "Modernization Check", "type": "claude_agent", "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "outputs": [{"name": "modernization_analysis", "values": []}, {"name": "modernization_severity", "values": ["CRITICAL", "HIGH", "MEDIUM", "LOW"]}], "timeout": 600, "prompt_template": "You are a Swift/iOS modernization consultant analyzing Talavo, a native SwiftUI browser app.\\n\\nRepository: {{repo_path}}\\nWorking directory: {{worktree_path}}\\nTarget folder/area: {{task_description}}\\n\\n**Project context:** Talavo targets iOS 16+, built with Swift 5.9, using XcodeGen (project.yml). No external dependencies — purely native. Uses ObservableObject + @Published for state, UserDefaults for persistence, URLSession for networking, WKWebView for browsing, AVFoundation for media, Combine sparingly (mostly PassthroughSubject). Has a LiveActivityExtension for lock screen widgets.\\n\\n**Check for:**\\n1. **ObservableObject → @Observable migration** — The entire app uses ObservableObject + @Published. Identify which ViewModels/Stores would benefit from migrating to the @Observable macro (iOS 17+). This would eliminate @StateObject/@ObservedObject/@EnvironmentObject boilerplate and improve view re-render granularity. Assess the scope of this migration.\\n2. **Outdated Swift patterns** — Completion handler callbacks that should use async/await, manual DispatchQueue.main.async where @MainActor would be cleaner, if-let chains that could use guard, old-style string interpolation or formatting\\n3. **Swift 5.9+ / 6.0 features** — Missing usage of #Preview macro (vs PreviewProvider), if/switch expressions, typed throws, noncopyable types for unique resources (WebView holders?)\\n4. **SwiftUI modernization** — NavigationView usage that should be NavigationStack (already using NavigationStack?), .onChange(of:) old signature vs new two-parameter version, .task vs .onAppear for async work, missing .sensoryFeedback modifier (iOS 17+) vs manual UIImpactFeedbackGenerator\\n5. **UserDefaults → SwiftData** — Evaluate whether the UserDefaults-based persistence (tabs, history, shortcuts, settings, downloads metadata) would benefit from SwiftData migration for better querying, relationships, and type safety\\n6. **Security concerns** — Device ID and user data stored in UserDefaults — should sensitive data use Keychain? Are API endpoints properly secured? Is NSAppTransportSecurity configured minimally?\\n7. **Build & tooling** — Is project.yml (XcodeGen) up to date? Missing SwiftLint/SwiftFormat? Should strict concurrency checking be enabled? Is the iOS deployment target (16.0) still appropriate or should it be raised to unlock newer APIs?\\n8. **Missing platform features** — App Intents for Siri/Shortcuts integration, TipKit for feature discovery, StoreKit 2 for subscriptions, Privacy Manifest (PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy) for App Store compliance\\n\\nFor each finding:\\n- Identify the outdated pattern with file path and lines\\n- Explain the modern Swift/iOS replacement\\n- Assess migration effort (trivial, moderate, significant)\\n- Note minimum iOS version requirements and breaking changes\\n\\nEnd your response with a severity rating: CRITICAL, HIGH, MEDIUM, or LOW."}, {"id": "compile_report", "name": "Compile Final Report", "type": "claude_agent", "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "outputs": [{"name": "final_report", "values": []}, {"name": "needs_issues", "values": ["YES", "NO"]}], "timeout": 600, "prompt_template": "You are an iOS technical lead compiling a comprehensive architecture review report for Talavo, a native SwiftUI browser app.\\n\\nRepository: {{repo_path}}\\nTarget folder/area: {{task_description}}\\n\\nBelow are the results from five independent analyses of this Swift/iOS codebase. Compile them into a single, actionable report.\\n\\n---\\n**STRUCTURE ANALYSIS** (Severity: {{structure_severity}})\\n{{structure_analysis}}\\n\\n---\\n**CODE QUALITY & BUGS** (Severity: {{quality_severity}})\\n{{quality_analysis}}\\n\\n---\\n**DEDUPLICATION** (Severity: {{dedup_severity}})\\n{{dedup_analysis}}\\n\\n---\\n**UI/UX REVIEW** (Severity: {{ui_severity}})\\n{{ui_analysis}}\\n\\n---\\n**MODERNIZATION** (Severity: {{modernization_severity}})\\n{{modernization_analysis}}\\n\\n---\\n\\nCreate a final report with:\\n\\n1. **Executive Summary** — 3-5 sentence overview of the codebase health\\n2. **Critical Findings** — Issues that need immediate attention (crashes, memory leaks, security, retain cycles)\\n3. **High Priority Improvements** — Important but not urgent (architecture, deduplication, performance)\\n4. **Quick Wins** — Low-effort changes with high impact (access control, missing [weak self], ViewModifier extraction)\\n5. **Long-term Recommendations** — Larger efforts (@Observable migration, SwiftData, modularization)\\n6. **Metrics Summary** — Overall severity, estimated total issues found, categories breakdown\\n\\nRank all findings by priority. Be specific with file paths and actionable suggestions.\\n\\nEnd with an overall health rating: CRITICAL, NEEDS_WORK, FAIR, or GOOD.\\n\\nRespond with either YES or NO: are there critical issues that need immediate GitHub issues created?"}, {"id": "check_critical", "name": "Critical Issues Found?", "type": "condition", "branches": {"NO": "end", "YES": "create_issues"}, "default_branch": "end", "condition_field": "needs_issues"}, {"id": "create_issues", "name": "Create GitHub Issues", "type": "claude_agent", "model": "claude-sonnet-4-6", "outputs": [{"name": "created_issues", "values": []}], "timeout": 300, "prompt_template": "You are a project manager creating GitHub issues for critical findings in the Talavo native Swift iOS browser app.\\n\\nRepository: {{repo_path}}\\nWorking directory: {{worktree_path}}\\n\\nBased on the architecture review report below, create GitHub issues for the CRITICAL findings only. Use the `gh` CLI tool.\\n\\n{{final_report}}\\n\\nFor each critical finding:\\n1. Create a GitHub issue with a clear, descriptive title\\n2. Include the file paths, line numbers, and description of the issue\\n3. Include a suggested Swift fix\\n4. Add appropriate labels\\n\\nCreate the issues using: gh issue create --repo {{repo_path}} --title \\"...\\" --body \\"...\\"\\n\\nList all created issue numbers when done."}, {"id": "end", "name": "Analysis Complete", "type": "end", "result_template": "{{final_report}}"}], "version": "1.0"}	2026-03-15 09:14:52.841933+00	2026-03-15 09:33:12.982637+00
