192	1	f5454ee561e8	/projects/talavo	886	Remove dead fake Dynamic Island feature	Remove dead fake Dynamic Island feature	done	\N	doohub/issue-886-remove-dead-fake-dynamic-island-feature	892	https://github.com/bakicelebi/talavo/pull/892	\N	0	claude-opus-4-6	0	\N	2026-03-16 22:01:18.78256+00	2026-03-16 22:06:43.680034+00	24	[{"error": null, "output": null, "status": "completed", "node_id": "start", "node_name": "Start", "node_type": "start", "duration_s": 0.1, "started_at": "2026-03-16T22:01:20.181230+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-16T22:01:20.266088+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "blocker_status=READY, blocker_reason=READY\\n\\nIssue #886 has no blockers. It references #837 (Live Activity) only to explain *why* the fake Dynamic Island is dead code — not as a dependency. #837 is open but unrelated to this removal task. The work is purely deleting dead code.", "status": "completed", "node_id": "check_blockers", "node_name": "Check Blockers", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 20.3, "started_at": "2026-03-16T22:01:20.316977+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-16T22:01:40.614272+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "blocker_status=READY → check_clarity", "status": "completed", "node_id": "blocker_gate", "node_name": "Blocker Gate", "node_type": "condition", "duration_s": 0.1, "started_at": "2026-03-16T22:01:40.714663+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-16T22:01:40.837218+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "clarity_status=CLEAR, clarity_reason=**CLEAR**\\n\\nThe issue is clear. A competent iOS developer knows exactly what to do:\\n\\n- Delete `DynamicIslandManager` and `GlobalDynamicIslandView`\\n- Remove the related Settings toggle (that enables/disables it)\\n- Clean up any references to these removed classes/files\\n\\nThe scope is well-defined: remove dead code that was never wired up and actively breaks the mini player when toggled on.", "status": "completed", "node_id": "check_clarity", "node_name": "Check Clarity", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 14.4, "started_at": "2026-03-16T22:01:40.939698+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-16T22:01:55.296613+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "clarity_status=CLEAR → analyze", "status": "completed", "node_id": "clarity_gate", "node_name": "Clarity Gate", "node_type": "condition", "duration_s": 0.1, "started_at": "2026-03-16T22:01:55.482729+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-16T22:01:55.561005+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "project_context=## Project Context Summary: Issue #886 — Remove Fake Dynamic Island\\n\\n### Key Finding\\nThe `app/` Flutter folder was already removed (commit `982d5cc`). Only the **Swift iOS** side needs cleanup.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Files to Remove Entirely\\n- **`/projects/talavo/talavo-ios/talavo/Features/DynamicIsland/`** — entire folder:\\n  - `ViewModels/DynamicIslandManager.swift` — `ObservableObject` with `@Published isVisible`, `source`, callbacks\\n  - `Views/GlobalDynamicIslandView.swift` — SwiftUI view with `VideoIslandContent` and `AudioIslandContent`\\n\\n### Files to Edit (Surgical Removals)\\n\\n| File | What to remove |\\n|------|----------------|\\n| `Core/DI/AppDependencies.swift` | `let dynamicIslandManager: DynamicIslandManager` property + init line |\\n| `App/TalavoApp.swift` | `.environmentObject(dependencies.dynamicIslandManager)` |\\n| `App/RootView.swift` | `@EnvironmentObject private var dynamicIsland: DynamicIslandManager` + `if dynamicIsland.isVisible { GlobalDynamicIslandView()... }` block |\\n| `Features/Browser/Views/BrowserScreen.swift` | `@EnvironmentObject private var dynamicIsland: DynamicIslandManager` + the `if !settings.dynamicIslandEnabled` guard that hides the mini player — **always show `FloatingMiniPlayerView`** |\\n| `Features/Settings/Views/SettingsScreen.swift` | The \\"Dynamic Island\\" toggle tile (lines ~87–92) |\\n| `Features/Settings/Store/SettingsStore.swift` | `Keys.dynamicIslandEnabled` UserDefaults key, `@Published var dynamicIslandEnabled` property, and its init line |\\n| `Core/Constants/AppConstants.swift` | 4 constants: `dynamicIslandCompactHeight/Width`, `dynamicIslandExpandedHeight`, `dynamicIslandTopOffset` — **only if not used by `LiveActivityExtension`** |\\n\\n### Critical Constraint: AppConstants\\n`TalavoLiveActivityWidget.swift` uses the native iOS Live Activity API with `.dynamicIsland {}` — check whether `AppConstants.dynamicIslandCompactWidth/Height` are referenced there before removing those constants. If not used by LiveActivity, remove them too.\\n\\n### Coding Patterns to Follow\\n- **19 EnvironmentObjects** are injected at root in `TalavoApp.swift` — removing one is safe, just delete the line\\n- `AppDependencies` is a service locator with `let` stored properties — remove property + init assignment\\n- `SettingsStore` uses `UserDefaults` directly with a `Keys` enum — remove the key case and the `@Published` property with its `didSet`\\n- No test files to update (no test targets observed)\\n- After removal, `BrowserScreen` should unconditionally render `FloatingMiniPlayerView` — the `dynamicIslandEnabled` guard was the only thing gating it\\n\\n### What NOT to Touch\\n- `LiveActivityExtension/TalavoLiveActivityWidget.swift` — real Live Activity, keep untouched\\n- Any `dynamicIsland` references inside the Live Activity widget are the real iOS API, not fake code", "status": "completed", "node_id": "analyze", "node_name": "Analyze Project", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 64.4, "started_at": "2026-03-16T22:01:55.663336+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-16T22:03:00.088774+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "plan=\\n\\n# Implementation Plan: Remove Dead Fake Dynamic Island Feature (#886)\\n\\n## Phase 1: Verify AppConstants Usage\\n\\nBefore removing constants, check if `LiveActivityExtension/TalavoLiveActivityWidget.swift` references any of these:\\n- `AppConstants.dynamicIslandCompactHeight`\\n- `AppConstants.dynamicIslandCompactWidth`\\n- `AppConstants.dynamicIslandExpandedHeight`\\n- `AppConstants.dynamicIslandTopOffset`\\n\\nIf referenced by Live Activity → keep them. If not → remove in Phase 3.\\n\\n## Phase 2: Delete Files\\n\\n- **Delete entire folder**: `talavo/Features/DynamicIsland/`\\n  - `ViewModels/DynamicIslandManager.swift`\\n  - `Views/GlobalDynamicIslandView.swift`\\n\\n## Phase 3: Surgical Edits (order matters — work leaf-to-root)\\n\\n### `Features/Settings/Store/SettingsStore.swift`\\n- Remove `dynamicIslandEnabled` case from `Keys` enum\\n- Remove `@Published var dynamicIslandEnabled: Bool` property\\n- Remove its `didSet` UserDefaults persistence\\n- Remove its initialization from `init()`\\n\\n### `Features/Settings/Views/SettingsScreen.swift`\\n- Remove the \\"Dynamic Island\\" toggle tile (~lines 87–92)\\n\\n### `Features/Browser/Views/BrowserScreen.swift`\\n- Remove `@EnvironmentObject private var dynamicIsland: DynamicIslandManager`\\n- Remove the `if !settings.dynamicIslandEnabled` guard around `FloatingMiniPlayerView`\\n- Ensure `FloatingMiniPlayerView` renders unconditionally (keep the view, just remove the conditional wrapper)\\n\\n### `App/RootView.swift`\\n- Remove `@EnvironmentObject private var dynamicIsland: DynamicIslandManager`\\n- Remove the `if dynamicIsland.isVisible { GlobalDynamicIslandView()... }` block\\n\\n### `App/TalavoApp.swift`\\n- Remove `.environmentObject(dependencies.dynamicIslandManager)` line\\n\\n### `Core/DI/AppDependencies.swift`\\n- Remove `let dynamicIslandManager: DynamicIslandManager` property\\n- Remove its initialization in `init()`\\n\\n### `Core/Constants/AppConstants.swift` (conditional on Phase 1)\\n- If not used by Live Activity: remove `dynamicIslandCompactHeight`, `dynamicIslandCompactWidth`, `dynamicIslandExpandedHeight`, `dynamicIslandTopOffset`\\n\\n## Phase 4: Xcode Project File\\n\\n- Remove deleted files from the Xcode project/build system if using `.pbxproj` (check if the project uses SPM file discovery or explicit file references)\\n\\n## Phase 5: Verify & Clean Up\\n\\n- Grep entire repo for `DynamicIslandManager`, `GlobalDynamicIslandView`, `dynamicIslandEnabled` — confirm zero remaining references (excluding Live Activity's native `.dynamicIsland` API calls)\\n- Grep for orphaned imports of the deleted files\\n- Check for any dead `import` statements in edited files\\n\\n## Risks & Edge Cases\\n\\n1. **BrowserScreen mini player visibility** — The `dynamicIslandEnabled` guard currently hides `FloatingMiniPlayerView`. After removal, the mini player will always show when appropriate. This is the **intended behavior** (the guard was a bug since the fake DI never worked).\\n\\n2. **UserDefaults key persistence** — The `dynamicIslandEnabled` key will remain in users' UserDefaults storage as orphaned data. This is harmless and standard practice — no migration needed.\\n\\n3. **Xcode project file conflicts** — If `.pbxproj` has explicit file references, deleting files without updating it will cause build errors. Must remove references from the project file too.\\n\\n4. **Live Activity constants** — Must verify before removing from `AppConstants`. The native `.dynamicIsland {}` API in `TalavoLiveActivityWidget.swift` might use custom sizing constants, even though it's unlikely.\\n\\n## Estimated Scope\\n\\n- **2 files deleted**\\n- **7 files edited** (6 certain + AppConstants conditional)\\n- **0 files created**\\n- Low risk — purely subtractive change with no behavioral dependencies", "status": "completed", "node_id": "plan", "node_name": "Plan", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 26.5, "started_at": "2026-03-16T22:03:00.163279+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-16T22:03:26.702137+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "dev_result=https://github.com/bakicelebi/talavo/pull/892", "status": "completed", "node_id": "develop", "node_name": "Develop", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 146.0, "started_at": "2026-03-16T22:03:26.753469+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-16T22:05:52.798704+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "review_result=There's a trailing blank line at 87 before the closing brace, but that's minor formatting — not a functional issue.\\n\\n**APPROVED**\\n\\nThe PR cleanly removes the fake Dynamic Island feature:\\n\\n1. **Deleted files**: `DynamicIslandManager.swift` and `GlobalDynamicIslandView.swift` — the entire `Features/DynamicIsland/` folder is gone.\\n2. **RootView.swift** — Removed the `@EnvironmentObject` for `DynamicIslandManager` and the conditional `GlobalDynamicIslandView` overlay.\\n3. **TalavoApp.swift** — Removed `.environmentObject(dependencies.dynamicIslandManager)` from the environment chain.\\n4. **AppDependencies.swift** — Removed the `dynamicIslandManager` property and its initialization.\\n5. **AppConstants.swift** — Removed the 4 Dynamic Island dimension constants.\\n6. **SettingsStore.swift** — Removed the `dynamicIslandEnabled` published property, its UserDefaults key, and its initialization.\\n7. **SettingsScreen.swift** — Removed the Dynamic Island toggle from the UI.\\n8. **BrowserScreen.swift** — Removed the `@EnvironmentObject` for `dynamicIsland` and the `if !settings.dynamicIslandEnabled` guard that was wrapping the `FloatingMiniPlayerView`. The mini player now always shows (correct behavior — it was previously hidden when the fake island was enabled).\\n9. **project.pbxproj** — All file references and group entries for the deleted files are removed.\\n\\nNo remaining references to the fake Dynamic Island in the iOS app code. The Live Activity extension's `DynamicIsland` references are Apple's real API — correctly left untouched. No dead code left behind., review_verdict=APPROVED", "status": "completed", "node_id": "review", "node_name": "Review", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 50.6, "started_at": "2026-03-16T22:05:52.852171+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-16T22:06:43.494451+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "review_verdict=APPROVED → done", "status": "completed", "node_id": "review_gate", "node_name": "Review Gate", "node_type": "condition", "duration_s": 0.1, "started_at": "2026-03-16T22:06:43.546042+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-16T22:06:43.596258+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "Issue #886 implemented and reviewed. PR ready to merge.", "status": "completed", "node_id": "done", "node_name": "Ready to Merge", "node_type": "end", "duration_s": 323.5, "started_at": "2026-03-16T22:06:43.643729+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-16T22:06:43.643734+00:00"}]	\N
123	2	5cfe89a0a187	/projects/Doohub	136	FCM messages missing iOS (APNS) sound configuration	FCM messages missing iOS (APNS) sound configuration	done	\N	doohub/issue-136-fcm-messages-missing-ios-apns-sound-conf	185	https://github.com/Lenkomotive/doohub/pull/185	\N	0	claude-opus-4-6	0	\N	2026-03-08 13:41:49.648465+00	2026-03-08 13:43:22.101002+00	8	[{"error": null, "output": null, "status": "completed", "node_id": "start", "node_name": "Start", "node_type": "start", "duration_s": 0.1, "started_at": "2026-03-08T13:41:50.520344+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T13:41:50.572461+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "blocker_status=READY, blocker_reason=Issue #136 contains no \\"blocked by\\", \\"depends on\\", or dependency keywords. It's a standalone backend fix with no references to other issues.\\n\\n**READY**", "status": "completed", "node_id": "check_blockers", "node_name": "Check Blockers", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 8.6, "started_at": "2026-03-08T13:41:50.615508+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T13:41:59.186191+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "blocker_status=READY → check_clarity", "status": "completed", "node_id": "blocker_gate", "node_name": "Blocker Gate", "node_type": "condition", "duration_s": 0.0, "started_at": "2026-03-08T13:41:59.232509+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T13:41:59.280648+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "clarity_status=CLEAR, clarity_reason=CLEAR\\n\\nThe issue specifies exactly what file to change (`backend/app/core/fcm.py`), which function to modify (`send_push()`), and provides the exact code to add. No ambiguity.", "status": "completed", "node_id": "check_clarity", "node_name": "Check Clarity", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 5.3, "started_at": "2026-03-08T13:41:59.326173+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T13:42:04.675621+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "clarity_status=CLEAR → analyze", "status": "completed", "node_id": "clarity_gate", "node_name": "Clarity Gate", "node_type": "condition", "duration_s": 0.0, "started_at": "2026-03-08T13:42:04.721394+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T13:42:04.765382+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "project_context=The file is small and the fix is clear. Here's the context summary:\\n\\n## Project Context\\n\\n**Relevant file:** `backend/app/core/fcm.py:19` — contains the sole `send_push()` function.\\n\\n**Current state:** The `messaging.Message` on line 27 has `token`, `notification`, and `data` fields but no `apns` field. iOS devices need `APNSConfig` → `APNSPayload` → `Aps(sound=\\"default\\")` to trigger alert sounds.\\n\\n**Coding patterns/conventions:**\\n- All needed classes (`APNSConfig`, `APNSPayload`, `Aps`) are already available via the existing `from firebase_admin import credentials, messaging` import — no new dependencies needed.\\n- The fix is purely additive: add an `apns=` kwarg to the existing `messaging.Message(...)` constructor call.\\n- The function signature and logging pattern stay unchanged.\\n\\n**No other files need changes.** This is a single-function, single-file fix.", "status": "completed", "node_id": "analyze", "node_name": "Analyze Project", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 12.2, "started_at": "2026-03-08T13:42:04.808030+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T13:42:16.982995+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "plan=\\n\\n## Implementation Plan\\n\\n### Change\\n\\n**File:** `backend/app/core/fcm.py` — modify the `messaging.Message()` call in `send_push()` (~line 27)\\n\\n**What to do:** Add an `apns` keyword argument to the existing `messaging.Message(...)` constructor:\\n\\n- Add `apns=messaging.APNSConfig(payload=messaging.APNSPayload(aps=messaging.Aps(sound=\\"default\\")))` as a new kwarg alongside the existing `token`, `notification`, and `data` args.\\n\\n### No other changes needed\\n\\n- No new imports — `APNSConfig`, `APNSPayload`, `Aps` are all on `firebase_admin.messaging`, already imported.\\n- No new files, no test changes, no config changes.\\n\\n### Edge cases / risks\\n\\n- **Android unaffected** — `APNSConfig` is iOS-only; Android ignores it, so no regression risk.\\n- **Sound value** — `\\"default\\"` is the standard iOS system sound. Custom sounds would require the sound file bundled in the app; `\\"default\\"` is the correct choice here.\\n- **Silent/DND** — iOS respects user device settings regardless of this field, so no concern about overriding user preferences.", "status": "completed", "node_id": "plan", "node_name": "Plan", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 12.7, "started_at": "2026-03-08T13:42:17.032792+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T13:42:29.727016+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "dev_result=https://github.com/Lenkomotive/doohub/pull/185", "status": "completed", "node_id": "develop", "node_name": "Develop", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 31.6, "started_at": "2026-03-08T13:42:29.774226+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T13:43:01.387621+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "review_result=The change is clean and correct. The fix adds the standard APNS sound configuration (`\\"default\\"`) to the FCM `Message` object, which is the correct way to enable notification sounds on iOS via the Firebase Admin SDK.\\n\\n**APPROVED**\\n\\nThe implementation:\\n- Uses the correct `messaging.APNSConfig` / `APNSPayload` / `Aps` nesting from the Firebase Admin SDK\\n- `sound=\\"default\\"` is the standard value for playing the device's default notification sound on iOS\\n- No Android-side change is needed since Android uses the notification channel's sound setting by default\\n- The change is minimal and focused on the issue\\n- Existing error handling and guard clauses remain intact, review_verdict=APPROVED", "status": "completed", "node_id": "review", "node_name": "Review", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 20.5, "started_at": "2026-03-08T13:43:01.436197+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T13:43:21.900202+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "review_verdict=APPROVED → done", "status": "completed", "n