144	2	8864349eba85	/projects/talavo	609	Refresh icon stuck in animation loop in bottom drawer	Refresh icon stuck in animation loop in bottom drawer	done	\N	doohub/issue-609-refresh-icon-stuck-in-animation-loop-in-	622	https://github.com/bakicelebi/talavo/pull/622	\N	0	claude-opus-4-6	0	\N	2026-03-08 19:37:12.961542+00	2026-03-08 19:39:01.842812+00	8	[{"error": null, "output": null, "status": "completed", "node_id": "start", "node_name": "Start", "node_type": "start", "duration_s": 0.1, "started_at": "2026-03-08T19:37:14.063946+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T19:37:14.170650+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "blocker_status=READY, blocker_reason=READY\\n\\nThe issue has no dependencies or blockers. It's a self-contained one-liner fix in `_NowPlayingStripState._onRefreshTap()`.", "status": "completed", "node_id": "check_blockers", "node_name": "Check Blockers", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 7.3, "started_at": "2026-03-08T19:37:14.288516+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T19:37:21.619234+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "blocker_status=READY → check_clarity", "status": "completed", "node_id": "blocker_gate", "node_name": "Blocker Gate", "node_type": "condition", "duration_s": 0.1, "started_at": "2026-03-08T19:37:21.670698+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T19:37:21.730556+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "clarity_status=CLEAR, clarity_reason=CLEAR\\n\\nThe issue is well-defined with specific file, method, exact broken code, exact fix, and acceptance criteria. It's a one-liner bug fix in `_NowPlayingStripState._onRefreshTap()` in `browser_bottom_bar.dart`.", "status": "completed", "node_id": "check_clarity", "node_name": "Check Clarity", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 8.0, "started_at": "2026-03-08T19:37:21.777396+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T19:37:29.733754+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "clarity_status=CLEAR → analyze", "status": "completed", "node_id": "clarity_gate", "node_name": "Clarity Gate", "node_type": "condition", "duration_s": 0.0, "started_at": "2026-03-08T19:37:29.785482+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T19:37:29.831730+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "project_context=## Project Context Summary for Issue #609\\n\\n**Relevant File:** `app/lib/features/browser/presentation/widgets/browser_bottom_bar.dart`\\n\\n### The Bug (line 411)\\nIn `_NowPlayingStripState._onRefreshTap()`:\\n```dart\\n_spinAnim.forward(from: 0);  // no reset → gets stuck\\n```\\n\\n### The Fix Pattern (already used at line 75-77)\\nIn `_BrowserBottomBarState._syncRefreshAnim()`:\\n```dart\\n_refreshSpin.forward().then((_) {\\n  if (mounted) _refreshSpin.reset();\\n});\\n```\\n\\n### Key Details\\n- `_spinAnim` is an `AnimationController` with 600ms duration (line 398–400), initialized in `initState`, disposed in `dispose`\\n- The fix is a one-liner: add `.then((_) { if (mounted) _spinAnim.reset(); })` after `forward(from: 0)` on line 411\\n- The `mounted` guard is critical to avoid calling `reset()` after widget disposal\\n- `RotationTransition` at line 473 uses `_spinAnim` directly — no other wiring changes needed\\n- Conventions: `HapticFeedback.lightImpact()` before animation (already present), `dart format .` before committing\\n\\n### Nothing else to change\\n- No new dependencies, no new widgets, no architectural changes required\\n- The fix is entirely self-contained in `_onRefreshTap()` (line 409–413)", "status": "completed", "node_id": "analyze", "node_name": "Analyze Project", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 17.0, "started_at": "2026-03-08T19:37:29.877042+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T19:37:46.862495+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "plan=\\n\\n## Implementation Plan for Issue #609\\n\\n### File to Modify\\n\\n**`app/lib/features/browser/presentation/widgets/browser_bottom_bar.dart`** — line 411\\n\\n### Change\\n\\nIn `_NowPlayingStripState._onRefreshTap()`, add a `.then()` callback to reset the animation controller after the spin completes:\\n\\n- **Current (line 411):** `_spinAnim.forward(from: 0);`\\n- **Change to:** `_spinAnim.forward(from: 0).then((_) { if (mounted) _spinAnim.reset(); });`\\n\\n### Why This Works\\n\\n- `forward()` returns a `TickerFuture` — chaining `.then()` fires after the 600ms animation completes\\n- `reset()` returns the controller to value `0.0`, ready for the next tap\\n- `mounted` guard prevents calling `reset()` on a disposed controller (e.g., user navigates away mid-animation)\\n- This exact pattern is already used in `_BrowserBottomBarState._syncRefreshAnim()` (lines 75–77)\\n\\n### Edge Cases\\n\\n- **Rapid taps:** `forward(from: 0)` restarts the animation from the beginning on each tap, cancelling any in-progress spin. The `.then()` from the cancelled animation won't fire (the future completes immediately with a cancelled status), so no double-reset issue.\\n- **Widget disposal mid-animation:** The `mounted` guard handles this. The `AnimationController` is already disposed in `dispose()`.\\n\\n### Pre-commit\\n\\n- Run `dart format .` before committing (per project conventions)\\n\\n### No Other Changes Needed\\n\\n- No new files, dependencies, widgets, or architectural changes\\n- `RotationTransition` at line 473 already reads from `_spinAnim` — no wiring changes", "status": "completed", "node_id": "plan", "node_name": "Plan", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 12.6, "started_at": "2026-03-08T19:37:46.912390+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T19:37:59.480641+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "dev_result=https://github.com/bakicelebi/talavo/pull/622", "status": "completed", "node_id": "develop", "node_name": "Develop", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 26.5, "started_at": "2026-03-08T19:37:59.529490+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T19:38:25.980308+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "review_result=So all 5 commits are unique to this branch (main is at `5b23de5`). The branch bundles multiple issues (#609, #612, #616, #617, plus a dart format commit). That's not ideal for a PR titled for #609, but let me focus on correctness.\\n\\nThe #609 fix specifically (commit `4868e19`):\\n\\n```dart\\n_spinAnim.forward(from: 0).then((_) {\\n  if (mounted) _spinAnim.reset();\\n});\\n```\\n\\n**APPROVED**\\n\\nThe fix is correct and clean:\\n\\n1. **Animation reset**: `_spinAnim.forward(from: 0)` plays the spin animation, and `.then((_) => reset())` resets the controller to its initial state after completion. This prevents the animation from getting stuck at `value == 1.0` where subsequent `forward(from: 0)` calls on an already-completed `AnimationController` could cause the stuck loop described in #609.\\n\\n2. **`mounted` guard**: Properly checks `mounted` before calling `reset()` in the async callback, preventing use-after-dispose crashes if the widget is unmounted while the animation is running.\\n\\n3. **No side effects**: The `reset()` call doesn't trigger a visual change since the animation has already completed (value is at the end), and resetting to 0 just prepares it for the next tap.\\n\\nThe other changes in the branch (idleDismiss hardening, bottom bar border radius removal, miniplayer hiding on non-video sites, dart format) all look reasonable and well-implemented, though bundling them into a single #609 PR is a bit noisy. If you want a cleaner git history, consider splitting them, but functionally everything looks correct., review_verdict=APPROVED", "status": "completed", "node_id": "review", "node_name": "Review", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 35.6, "started_at": "2026-03-08T19:38:26.029274+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T19:39:01.648482+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "review_verdict=APPROVED → done", "status": "completed", "node_id": "review_gate", "node_name": "Review Gate", "node_type": "condition", "duration_s": 0.1, "started_at": "2026-03-08T19:39:01.695663+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T19:39:01.762164+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "Issue #609 implemented and reviewed. PR ready to merge.", "status": "completed", "node_id": "done", "node_name": "Ready to Merge", "node_type": "end", "duration_s": 107.8, "started_at": "2026-03-08T19:39:01.806999+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T19:39:01.807005+00:00"}]	\N
175	1	a02cb7ae33b7	/projects/talavo	810	Scrolling up in video tab should not minimize to miniplayer	Scrolling up in video tab should not minimize to miniplayer	done	\N	doohub/issue-810-scrolling-up-in-video-tab-should-not-min	843	https://github.com/bakicelebi/talavo/pull/843	\N	0	claude-opus-4-6	0	\N	2026-03-16 08:07:35.739771+00	2026-03-16 08:14:21.921987+00	24	[{"error": null, "output": null, "status": "completed", "node_id": "start", "node_name": "Start", "node_type": "start", "duration_s": 0.1, "started_at": "2026-03-16T08:07:36.901544+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-16T08:07:36.984282+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "blocker_status=READY, blocker_reason=**READY**\\n\\nIssue #810 has no dependencies, no \\"blocked by\\" references, and no comments indicating blockers. It's a self-contained bug fix related to scroll gesture handling in the video tab triggering unintended miniplayer minimization.", "status": "completed", "node_id": "check_blockers", "node_name": "Check Blockers", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 18.4, "started_at": "2026-03-16T08:07:37.141445+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-16T08:07:55.521335+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "blocker_status=READY → check_clarity", "status": "completed", "node_id": "blocker_gate", "node_name": "Blocker Gate", "node_type": "condition", "duration_s": 0.0, "started_at": "2026-03-16T08:07:55.575775+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-16T08:07:55.624823+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "clarity_status=CLEAR, clarity_reason=**CLEAR**\\n\\nThe issue describes a specific bug: scrolling up inside the video tab unintentionally triggers the miniplayer minimize behavior. The fix is clear — scroll gestures within the video tab content should not cause the video to minimize to the miniplayer. A competent iOS developer would know to look at the gesture recognizer or scroll delegate logic that handles miniplayer minimize and add a condition to ignore it when the scroll originates from within the video tab.", "status": "completed", "node_id": "check_clarity", "node_name": "Check Clarity", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 13.6, "started_at": "2026-03-16T08:07:55.671248+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-16T08:08:09.291053+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "clarity_status=CLEAR → analyze", "status": "completed", "node_id": "clarity_gate", "node_name": "Clarity Gate", "node_type": "condition", "duration_s": 0.0, "started_at": "2026-03-16T08:08:09.359737+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-16T08:08:09.407796+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "project_context=Now I have a thorough understanding. Here's the focused context summary for implementing issue #810:\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Project Context: Issue #810\\n\\n### The Bug\\n\\nIn `VideoOverlayView.swift`, the `PersistentWebViewWrapper` adds a `UIPanGestureRecognizer` to the container that calls `onSwipeDown()` → sets `miniPlayerProgress = 1.0` → minimizes the video. The gesture requires `v.y > 50` (downward) to begin. The problem is the **rubber-band/bounce effect**: when the user is at the top of the YouTube page and scrolls up, iOS bounces the content downward (positive `y` velocity), which satisfies `v.y > 50` and can exceed the `velocity > 300 || translation > 150` threshold in `handlePan`.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Key Files\\n\\n| File | Purpose |\\n|------|---------|\\n| `talavo-ios/talavo/Features/Browser/Views/VideoOverlayView.swift` | The **only file to modify**. Contains `PersistentWebViewWrapper` and its `Coordinator` with the pan gesture logic. |\\n| `talavo-ios/talavo/Features/Browser/Views/BrowserScreen.swift:25` | `@State private var miniPlayerProgress` — the binding passed into VideoOverlayView |\\n| `talavo-ios/talavo/Features/Browser/Services/VideoWebViewHolder.swift:50-51` | Creates the `WKWebView` with `wv.scrollView.isScrollEnabled = true` |\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Gesture Logic (VideoOverlayView.swift)\\n\\n**`gestureRecognizerShouldBegin` (line 136–140):**\\n```swift\\nreturn abs(v.y) > abs(v.x) * 1.5 && v.y > 50  // Only downward\\n```\\n\\n**`handlePan` (line 126–134):**\\n```swift\\nif velocity > 300 || translation > 150 { onSwipeDown?() }\\n```\\n\\n**`shouldRecognizeSimultaneouslyWith` (line 142–147):**\\n```swift\\nreturn true  // ← The problem: allows simultaneous recognition with WKWebView scroll\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Root Cause\\n\\n`shouldRecognizeSimultaneouslyWith` returns `true`, meaning the pan gesture can fire **at the same time** as WKWebView's internal scroll gesture recognizer. During a fast upward scroll:\\n1. The WKWebView's `scrollView.panGestureRecognizer` handles the scroll\\n2. The content bounces downward (rubber-band at top of page)\\n3. Our pan gesture also fires with positive `v.y`, passing `gestureRecognizerShouldBegin`\\n4. The bounce translation/velocity crosses the threshold → minimize triggered\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Fix Pattern\\n\\n**In `shouldRecognizeSimultaneouslyWith`, reject simultaneous recognition with the WKWebView's own scroll pan gesture.** This requires the `Coordinator` to hold a reference to the `WKWebView` so it can compare against `webView.scrollView.panGestureRecognizer`.\\n\\nThe `Coordinator` needs a `var webView: WKWebView?` property, set in `makeUIView` after calling `holder.getOrCreateWebView()`. Then:\\n\\n```swift\\nfunc gestureRecognizer(_ gestureRecognizer: UIGestureRecognizer,\\n                        shouldRecognizeSimultaneouslyWith other: UIGestureRecognizer) -> Bool {\\n    // Don't recognize simultaneously with the WKWebView's own scroll gesture\\n    if let wv = webView, other === wv.scrollView.panGestureRecognizer {\\n        return false\\n    }\\n    return true\\n}\\n```\\n\\nThis is surgical: it blocks the rubber-band false-positive while keeping simultaneous recognition with any other gestures (e.g., tap recognizers on video controls).\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Conventions to Follow\\n\\n- All gesture delegate logic stays in the `Coordinator` inner class of `PersistentWebViewWrapper`\\n- `makeUIView` is the right place to pass the `webView` reference into the coordinator (`context.coordinator.webView = webView`)\\n- The holder already exposes `holder.webView` (private(set)), but since we're inside `makeUIView` we already have the `webView` directly from `holder.getOrCreateWebView()` — assign it to the coordinator there\\n- No new files needed — all changes are in `VideoOverlayView.swift`\\n- Run `dart format .` is Flutter-only; Swift formatting is handled automatically by Xcode (no explicit format step needed before committing)", "status": "completed", "node_id": "analyze", "node_name": "Analyze Project", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 290.5, "started_at": "2026-03-16T08:08:09.451468+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-16T08:12:59.990946+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "plan=\\n\\n## Implementation Plan: Issue #810 — Scrolling up in video tab should not minimize to miniplayer\\n\\n### File to Modify\\n\\n**`talavo-ios/talavo/Features/Browser/Views/VideoOverlayView.swift`**\\n\\n### Changes\\n\\n1. **Add `webView` property to `Coordinator`**\\n   - Add `weak var webView: WKWebView?` to the `Coordinator` class inside `PersistentWebViewWrapper`\\n\\n2. **Set the reference in `makeUIView`**\\n   - After `holder.getOrCreateWebView()` returns the web view, assign it to `context.coordinator.webView`\\n\\n3. **Update `shouldRecognizeSimultaneouslyWith`**\\n   - Instead of always returning `true`, check if `other` is the WKWebView's `scrollView.panGestureRecognizer`\\n   - If it is, return `false` (block simultaneous recognition with the scroll gesture)\\n   - Otherwise return `true` (preserve simultaneous recognition with other gestures like tap/pinch)\\n\\n### Why This Works\\n\\n- The rubber-band bounce happens inside `WKWebView.scrollView.panGestureRecognizer`\\n- By refusing simultaneous recognition with that specific gesture, our swipe-down pan gesture won't fire during scroll bounces\\n- The user can still swipe down to minimize when they're not actively scrolling — our gesture just won't compete with the scroll gesture\\n- All other simultaneous gesture recognition (taps, long presses, video controls) is preserved\\n\\n### Edge Cases & Risks\\n\\n- **Deliberate swipe-down while scrolling**: User must lift finger and swipe again (not mid-scroll). This is acceptable UX — it matches how most video apps (YouTube, Instagram) handle minimize gestures.\\n- **`webView` reference could be nil**: If nil, falls through to `return true` (current behavior), so no regression risk.\\n- **Use `weak` for the webView property**: The coordinator doesn't own the web view (the holder does), so use a weak reference to avoid retain cycles.\\n- **`updateUIView` re-assignment**: If `makeUIView` isn't called again but the web view changes, the reference could go stale. Check whether `updateUIView` also needs to update `context.coordinator.webView`. Based on the current code, `getOrCreateWebView()` returns the same instance, so this shouldn't be an issue — but worth verifying.\\n\\n### No Other Files Needed\\n\\nAll changes are confined to `VideoOverlayView.swift`. No new files, no dependency changes, no other view modifications.", "status": "completed", "node_id": "plan", "node_name": "Plan", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 17.9, "started_at": "2026-03-16T08:13:00.046830+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-16T08:13:17.988905+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "dev_result=https://github.com/bakicelebi/talavo/pull/843", "status": "completed", "node_id": "develop", "node_name": "Develop", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 47.0, "started_at": "2026-03-16T08:13:18.045315+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-16T08:14:05.025769+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "review_result=**APPROVED**\\n\\nThe fix is clean and correct. Here's the summary:\\n\\n**Problem:** Scrolling up inside the video tab's web content was being recognized simultaneously as a swipe-down gesture, triggering the miniplayer minimize.\\n\\n**Fix:** In `gestureRecognizer(_:shouldRecognizeSimultaneouslyWith:)`, the coordinator now returns `false` when the other gesture is the WKWebView's scroll view pan gesture. This prevents the custom swipe-to-minimize pan from firing while the user is scrolling web content. All other simultaneous gesture combinations still return `true`.\\n\\nChecklist notes:\\n- **Memory safety** — `webView` is correctly declared as `weak` to avoid a retain cycle with the WKWebView.\\n- **Code quality** — Uses identity comparison (`===`) appropriately for gesture recognizer matching. No force unwraps.\\n- **Architecture** — Minimal, focused change in the correct file. No unnecessary abstractions.\\n- **Matches requirements** — Directly addresses the issue: scrolling in the video tab no longer triggers miniplayer minimize., review_verdict=APPROVED", "status": "completed", "node_id": "review", "node_name": "Review", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 16.7, "started_at": "2026-03-16T08:14:05.080124+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-16T08:14:21.732415+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "review_verdict=APPROVED → done", "status": "completed", "node_id": "review_gate", "node_name": "Review Gate", "node_type": "condition", "duration_s": 0.0, "started_at": "2026-03-16T08:14:21.785192+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-16T08:14:21.833779+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "Issue #810 implemented and reviewed. PR ready to merge.", "status": "completed", "node_id": "done", "node_name": "Ready to Merge", "node_type": "end", "duration_s": 405.1, "started_at": "2026-03-16T08:14:21.885362+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-16T08:14:21.885367+00:00"}]	\N
