: "Check Clarity", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 5.9, "started_at": "2026-03-08T13:47:55.390330+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T13:48:01.276722+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "clarity_status=CLEAR → analyze", "status": "completed", "node_id": "clarity_gate", "node_name": "Clarity Gate", "node_type": "condition", "duration_s": 0.0, "started_at": "2026-03-08T13:48:01.324246+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T13:48:01.370296+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "project_context=The fix described in the issue is **already implemented** in the file. Lines 23–27 of `app/lib/services/fcm.dart` already contain:\\n\\n```dart\\nawait messaging.setForegroundNotificationPresentationOptions(\\n  alert: true,\\n  badge: true,\\n  sound: true,\\n);\\n```\\n\\nThis was added in the most recent commit (`25460be feat: add foreground notification presentation options for FCM`). The issue has already been resolved — no further changes are needed.\\n\\n**Summary:**\\n- `app/lib/services/fcm.dart` — `registerFcmToken()` already calls `setForegroundNotificationPresentationOptions` with `alert`, `badge`, and `sound` all set to `true`, placed immediately after `requestPermission`.\\n- The current branch (`doohub/issue-137-add-foreground-notification-presentation`) reflects this completed fix.", "status": "completed", "node_id": "analyze", "node_name": "Analyze Project", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 11.3, "started_at": "2026-03-08T13:48:01.414805+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T13:48:12.748762+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "plan=\\n\\n## Implementation Plan for Issue #137\\n\\n**Status: Already implemented.** No further code changes needed.\\n\\n### What was done (commit `25460be`)\\n\\n- **Modified:** `app/lib/services/fcm.dart` — added `setForegroundNotificationPresentationOptions(alert: true, badge: true, sound: true)` after `requestPermission()` in `registerFcmToken()`\\n\\n### Remaining steps\\n\\n1. **Create a PR** from branch `doohub/issue-137-add-foreground-notification-presentation` to `main`\\n2. **Link PR to issue #137** so it auto-closes on merge\\n3. **Test on iOS** — this API primarily affects iOS foreground notification display (Android uses notification channels instead)\\n4. **Verify on Android** — confirm no regressions; Android should continue showing notifications via its default channel behavior\\n\\n### Edge cases / notes\\n\\n- `setForegroundNotificationPresentationOptions` is **iOS-only** in practice — on Android it's a no-op. Android foreground notifications require a notification channel, which should already be configured via `firebase_messaging` defaults.\\n- The call is correctly placed after `requestPermission`, so permission is granted before setting presentation options.\\n- No additional dependencies or package changes required.", "status": "completed", "node_id": "plan", "node_name": "Plan", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 12.3, "started_at": "2026-03-08T13:48:12.852831+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T13:48:25.163232+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "dev_result=https://github.com/Lenkomotive/doohub/pull/186", "status": "completed", "node_id": "develop", "node_name": "Develop", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 22.7, "started_at": "2026-03-08T13:48:25.212839+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T13:48:47.902967+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "review_result=**APPROVED**\\n\\nThe change is correct and matches the issue requirements exactly. It adds `setForegroundNotificationPresentationOptions` with `alert`, `badge`, and `sound` enabled, placed logically right after `requestPermission` and before token retrieval. This is the standard Firebase Messaging API for enabling foreground notification display on iOS. The call is already inside the existing try/catch block, so errors are handled. No issues found., review_verdict=APPROVED", "status": "completed", "node_id": "review", "node_name": "Review", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 15.2, "started_at": "2026-03-08T13:48:47.951470+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T13:49:03.174932+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "review_verdict=APPROVED → done", "status": "completed", "node_id": "review_gate", "node_name": "Review Gate", "node_type": "condition", "duration_s": 0.0, "started_at": "2026-03-08T13:49:03.222754+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T13:49:03.269928+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "Issue #137 implemented and reviewed. PR ready to merge.", "status": "completed", "node_id": "done", "node_name": "Ready to Merge", "node_type": "end", "duration_s": 80.0, "started_at": "2026-03-08T13:49:03.315846+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-08T13:49:03.315853+00:00"}]	\N
164	2	d5a99515fdfe	/projects/talavo	823	Make check updates work in native iOS settings	Make check updates work in native iOS settings	done	\N	doohub/issue-823-make-check-updates-work-in-native-ios-se	829	https://github.com/bakicelebi/talavo/pull/829	\N	0	claude-opus-4-6	0	\N	2026-03-15 10:02:32.458235+00	2026-03-15 10:08:59.253748+00	24	[{"error": null, "output": null, "status": "completed", "node_id": "start", "node_name": "Start", "node_type": "start", "duration_s": 0.1, "started_at": "2026-03-15T10:02:33.635469+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-15T10:02:33.687459+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "blocker_status=READY, blocker_reason=Issue #823 has no language indicating it's blocked by or depends on any other issue. The description is self-contained — it's a port of existing Flutter functionality to native iOS with all implementation details provided.\\n\\n**READY**\\n\\nIssue #823 has no blockers. It's an independent feature port with all required implementation details (API endpoint, UI spec, key Flutter files) provided in the description.", "status": "completed", "node_id": "check_blockers", "node_name": "Check Blockers", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 13.1, "started_at": "2026-03-15T10:02:33.764851+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-15T10:02:46.824242+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "blocker_status=READY → check_clarity", "status": "completed", "node_id": "blocker_gate", "node_name": "Blocker Gate", "node_type": "condition", "duration_s": 0.1, "started_at": "2026-03-15T10:02:46.875793+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-15T10:02:46.972270+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "clarity_status=CLEAR, clarity_reason=**CLEAR**\\n\\nThe issue provides everything a competent iOS developer needs:\\n- The exact API endpoint to call\\n- Business logic (24h cooldown, force update behavior, version parsing format)\\n- Complete UI specs for the dialog and all settings tile states\\n- App Store URL\\n- Reference Flutter implementation files to port from", "status": "completed", "node_id": "check_clarity", "node_name": "Check Clarity", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 10.0, "started_at": "2026-03-15T10:02:47.053438+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-15T10:02:57.005799+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "clarity_status=CLEAR → analyze", "status": "completed", "node_id": "clarity_gate", "node_name": "Clarity Gate", "node_type": "condition", "duration_s": 0.1, "started_at": "2026-03-15T10:02:57.061415+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-15T10:02:57.111902+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "project_context=## Project Context: Issue #823 - Check for Updates in Native iOS Settings\\n\\n### What Already Exists\\n\\nThe core feature is **already implemented** — it just needs to be wired up in the Settings screen.\\n\\n**Key files:**\\n- `talavo-ios/talavo/Features/UpdateCheck/ViewModels/UpdateCheckManager.swift` — `@ObservableObject` with `@Published var updateAvailable`, `@Published var updateUrl`, and an async `checkForUpdate()` method. Hits `https://api.talavo.app/api/app/version`.\\n- `talavo-ios/talavo/Features/UpdateCheck/Views/UpdateDialogView.swift` — Modal overlay with \\"Update Now\\" / \\"Later\\" buttons, already shown in `RootView.swift` when `updateAvailable == true`.\\n- `talavo-ios/talavo/Features/Settings/Views/SettingsScreen.swift:116-119` — Stub \\"Check for Updates\\" button with **empty action**.\\n- `talavo-ios/talavo/Core/DI/AppDependencies.swift` — `UpdateCheckManager` already registered and injected into the environment.\\n\\n### What's Missing\\n\\n1. **Settings tile states** — The stub button doesn't reflect \\"Checking...\\", \\"You're up to date\\", or \\"New version available\\" states.\\n2. **Manual trigger** — The button's action is empty; needs to call `updateCheckManager.checkForUpdate()`.\\n3. **Loading/result feedback** — Need `@Published var isChecking: Bool` and `@Published var isUpToDate: Bool` in `UpdateCheckManager` (or equivalent state).\\n4. **24-hour cooldown** — Unclear if this exists; the Flutter version has it, needs to be verified or added.\\n5. **Force update** — The `forceUpdate` flag from the API should hide the \\"Later\\" button in `UpdateDialogView`.\\n\\n### Patterns to Follow\\n\\n**State management in UpdateCheckManager:**\\n```swift\\n@Published var isChecking: Bool = false\\n@Published var lastChecked: Date?  // persisted to UserDefaults\\n```\\n\\n**UserDefaults persistence** (follow SettingsStore pattern):\\n```swift\\nprivate enum Keys { static let lastUpdateCheck = \\"last_update_check\\" }\\n// didSet saves to UserDefaults, init() loads from UserDefaults\\n```\\n\\n**Settings tile** — Use the existing `SettingsListTile` component already used throughout `SettingsScreen`. The tile needs conditional trailing content: `ProgressView()` when checking, text label for result state.\\n\\n**EnvironmentObject access** — `UpdateCheckManager` is already injected at root. In `SettingsScreen`, add `@EnvironmentObject var updateCheckManager: UpdateCheckManager`.\\n\\n**Dialog** — `UpdateDialogView` is shown via `ZStack` in `RootView` at `zIndex: 10`. The force update non-dismissible behavior needs to be driven by a `forceUpdate: Bool` published property.\\n\\n### Technical Considerations\\n\\n- The API returns `{ latestVersion, updateUrl, forceUpdate }` — version comparison uses `.numeric` ordering\\n- App Store URL: `https://apps.apple.com/app/talavo/id6744076701` (likely already in `UpdateCheckManager` or `AppConstants`)\\n- The auto-check on launch is already wired in `AppDependencies.initialize()` — the manual check from Settings must reuse the same `checkForUpdate()` method\\n- Use `AppLogger` (not raw `print`) for error logging, consistent with other managers\\n- No external dependencies — pure URLSession\\n\\n### Summary\\n\\nThe implementation is mostly plumbing: add `isChecking`/`isUpToDate` state to `UpdateCheckManager`, persist `lastChecked` timestamp for the cooldown, wire the Settings button to call `checkForUpdate()`, update the button's appearance based on state, and ensure `forceUpdate` from the API hides the \\"Later\\" button in `UpdateDialogView`.", "status": "completed", "node_id": "analyze", "node_name": "Analyze Project", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 92.9, "started_at": "2026-03-15T10:02:57.181554+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-15T10:04:30.037879+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "plan=## Implementation Plan: #823 — Check for Updates in Native iOS Settings\\n\\n### Overview\\n\\nWire up the existing stub button in `SettingsScreen` to call `checkForUpdate()`, add loading/result states to `UpdateCheckManager`, implement 24-hour cooldown with UserDefaults persistence, and handle force updates in `UpdateDialogView`.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Step 1: Update `UpdateCheckManager.swift`\\n\\n**File:** `talavo-ios/talavo/Features/UpdateCheck/ViewModels/UpdateCheckManager.swift`\\n\\n- Add `@Published var isChecking: Bool = false`\\n- Add `@Published var isUpToDate: Bool = false`\\n- Add `@Published var forceUpdate: Bool = false`\\n- Add `private var lastChecked: Date?` — load from `UserDefaults` in `init()`, save after successful check\\n- Add `private let defaults = UserDefaults.standard` and `Keys.lastUpdateCheck` constant\\n- Modify `checkForUpdate()` to accept `force: Bool = false` parameter\\n  - If `!force` and `lastChecked` is within 24 hours, skip the network call and set `isUpToDate = true` (unless `updateAvailable` is already true)\\n  - Set `isChecking = true` at start, `isChecking = false` at end (on `MainActor`)\\n  - On success where no update needed: set `isUpToDate = true`\\n  - On success where update found: set `forceUpdate` from `response.forceUpdate ?? false`\\n  - Persist `lastChecked = Date()` to UserDefaults after successful check\\n  - Reset `isUpToDate = false` after ~3 seconds (via `Task.sleep`) so the tile returns to default state\\n- Replace `print` with `AppLogger` for error logging\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Step 2: Update `SettingsScreen.swift`\\n\\n**File:** `talavo-ios/talavo/Features/Settings/Views/SettingsScreen.swift`\\n\\n- Add `@EnvironmentObject private var updateCheckManager: UpdateCheckManager`\\n- Replace the stub `SettingsListTile` (lines 114–119) with a version that:\\n  - **Action:** calls `Task { await updateCheckManager.checkForUpdate(force: true) }`\\n  - **Subtitle:** conditional based on state:\\n    - `isChecking` → `\\"Checking...\\"`\\n    - `updateAvailable` → `\\"New version available\\"`\\n    - `isUpToDate` → `\\"You're up to date\\"`\\n    - default → `nil` (no subtitle)\\n  - **Trailing content:** show `ProgressView()` when `isChecking` is true (if `SettingsListTile` supports trailing content — otherwise embed the spinner in the subtitle)\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Step 3: Update `UpdateDialogView.swift`\\n\\n**File:** `talavo-ios/talavo/Features/UpdateCheck/Views/UpdateDialogView.swift`\\n\\n- Read `updateCheck.forceUpdate` to conditionally hide the \\"Later\\" button\\n- When `forceUpdate` is true:\\n  - Remove the \\"Later\\" button (only show \\"Update\\" button, full width)\\n  - Disable dismiss gestures (the ZStack background tap should not dismiss)\\n- Update body text to include version number if available (optional enhancement)\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Step 4: Verify `SettingsListTile` supports subtitle\\n\\n**File:** `talavo-ios/talavo/Features/Settings/Views/SettingsListTile.swift` (or wherever it's defined)\\n\\n- Confirm `subtitle: String?` parameter exists and renders correctly\\n- If no trailing view slot exists for a spinner, either:\\n  - Add an optional `trailing: AnyView?` parameter, or\\n  - Use the subtitle text \\"Checking...\\" as sufficient feedback (simpler)\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Files Changed Summary\\n\\n| File | Action |\\n|------|--------|\\n| `UpdateCheckManager.swift` | Modify — add `isChecking`, `isUpToDate`, `forceUpdate` states, 24h cooldown, UserDefaults persistence |\\n| `SettingsScreen.swift` | Modify — add `@EnvironmentObject`, wire button action, dynamic subtitle |\\n| `UpdateDialogView.swift` | Modify — hide \\"Later\\" button when `forceUpdate` is true |\\n| `SettingsListTile.swift` | Possibly modify — verify subtitle support, optionally add trailing view |\\n\\nNo new files needed.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Edge Cases & Risks\\n\\n- **Race condition:** User taps \\"Check for Updates\\" while auto-check from launch is in flight → guard with `isChecking` to avoid duplicate requests\\n- **Thread safety:** All `@Published` mutations must happen on `MainActor` (already using `MainActor.run`)\\n- **Cooldown bypass:** Manual check from Settings should use `force: true` to bypass the 24h cooldown (user explicitly asked to check)\\n- **\\"Up to date\\" auto-dismiss:** The `isUpToDate` state should auto-clear after a few seconds so the tile doesn't permanently show \\"You're up to date\\" on re-entry to Settings\\n- **Force update persistence:** If user kills the app during a force update dialog, the dialog should reappear on next launch — the existing auto-check at init handles this\\n- **Network failure:** On error, set `isChecking = false` and optionally show a brief error subtitle, then clear it", "status": "completed", "node_id": "plan", "node_name": "Plan", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 78.9, "started_at": "2026-03-15T10:04:30.105544+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-15T10:05:49.008601+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "dev_result=The PR is open with no review feedback. All changes are already committed and pushed. The implementation includes:\\n\\n1. **`UpdateCheckManager.swift`** — Added `isChecking`, `isUpToDate`, `forceUpdate` states, 24-hour cooldown with UserDefaults persistence, `@MainActor` annotation, and AppLogger error logging\\n2. **`SettingsScreen.swift`** — Wired the button to `checkForUpdate(force: true)`, added dynamic subtitle and loading spinner via generic `Trailing` view on `SettingsListTile`\\n3. **`UpdateDialogView.swift`** — Hides \\"Later\\" button when `forceUpdate` is true\\n\\nhttps://github.com/bakicel