, "node_id": "check_clarity", "node_name": "Check Clarity", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 11.9, "started_at": "2026-03-15T10:02:47.170162+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-15T10:02:59.107946+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "clarity_status=CLEAR → analyze", "status": "completed", "node_id": "clarity_gate", "node_name": "Clarity Gate", "node_type": "condition", "duration_s": 0.1, "started_at": "2026-03-15T10:02:59.162022+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-15T10:02:59.225406+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "project_context=## Project Context for Issue #822: Debug Panel (Native Swift)\\n\\n### Relevant Existing Files\\n\\n**Reference (Flutter):**\\n- `/projects/talavo/app/lib/features/browser/presentation/widgets/debug_info_panel.dart` — Full reference panel with all 8 sections, glassmorphism styling, 3-second auto-refresh, and action buttons\\n\\n**iOS Core:**\\n- `Core/Widgets/GlassCard.swift` — Primary glass container; use for the debug panel itself\\n- `Core/Theme/AppTheme.swift` + `AppColors.swift` — Theme helpers (`.success`, `.error`, `.warning`, `textPrimary`, `card` colors)\\n- `Core/Constants/AppConstants.swift` — Layout constants and API base URL\\n- `Core/Utils/PlaybackLogger.swift` — Already stores entries with `[DART]`/`[JS]`/`[IOS]` source tags; `getRecentEntries(count:)` is ready to use\\n- `Core/Utils/AppLogger.swift` — os.Logger categories\\n\\n**iOS Feature Services (all accessible via EnvironmentObject):**\\n- `Features/AdBlock/Services/ContentRuleManager.swift` — `@Published blockedCount: Int`, `ruleLists: [WKContentRuleList]`, `enabled: Bool`\\n- `Features/AdBlock/Services/ScriptManager.swift` — `scriptCount: Int`\\n- `Features/Browser/ViewModels/BrowserViewModel.swift` — `tabs: [TabInfo]`, `activeTabId`\\n- `Features/Settings/Store/SettingsStore.swift` — `adBlockEnabled`, other toggles\\n- `Core/DI/AppDependencies.swift` — The full dependency graph; holds references to all managers\\n\\n### Coding Patterns & Conventions\\n\\n- **File location:** New file goes in `Features/Browser/Views/` (or `Widgets/`) as `DebugInfoPanel.swift`\\n- **MVVM:** Create a `DebugInfoPanelViewModel: ObservableObject` with `@Published` properties; inject services via initializer or EnvironmentObject\\n- **State management:** Use `@EnvironmentObject` to access `BrowserViewModel`, `ContentRuleManager`, `SettingsStore`, `AppDependencies` — all 19 are pre-injected at root\\n- **Auto-refresh:** Use `Timer.publish(every: 3, on: .main, in: .common)` with `.onReceive` in the view\\n- **Glass UI:** Wrap content in `GlassCard`; use `.ultraThinMaterial` + rounded rect fill for inner section headers\\n- **Action feedback:** `@State var actionMessage: String?` + `.task` with a 1.5s delay to clear it — matches Flutter's `_actionMessage` pattern\\n- **Colors:** `Color(.success)`, `Color(.error)`, `Color(.talavoMint)` from AppColors; opacity modifiers for glass layers\\n- **Naming:** camelCase properties, PascalCase types; section labels as `String` constants inside the view\\n\\n### Reusable Components\\n\\n- `GlassCard` — direct drop-in for the outer container (22pt corner radius, backdrop blur built-in)\\n- `PlaybackLogger.getRecentEntries(count: 40)` — returns last N log strings exactly as needed\\n- `ContentRuleManager.blockedCount` + `ruleLists.count` — already `@Published`, reactive\\n- `BrowserViewModel.tabs.count` — tab count\\n- `ProcessInfo.processInfo.physicalMemory` + `os_proc_available_memory()` for RAM stats\\n- `FileManager.default.attributesOfFileSystem` / `enumerateDirectory` for folder sizes\\n\\n### Technical Considerations\\n\\n1. **Placement:** The panel should overlay the browser view. RootView uses a `ZStack`; add the panel as a conditional overlay in `BrowserView` or `RootView` (similar to tab overview), triggered by a developer shake gesture or hidden tap zone.\\n\\n2. **Access gate:** Since there's no native settings screen, gate visibility with `#if DEBUG` or a hidden tap-count trigger (5 taps on a corner) — check the Flutter panel for how it's toggled.\\n\\n3. **AdBlock logs:** Flutter references a `ContentRuleService.lastLogs` — in iOS, `ContentRuleManager` uses `AppLogger.contentRules` (os.Logger). To surface logs in-panel, you'll need to buffer recent log lines manually (similar to `PlaybackLogger`) since os.Logger has no in-process log retrieval API.\\n\\n4. **Storage size:** Folder size calculation with `FileManager` is synchronous; run on a background actor or `Task { }` to avoid blocking the UI during the 3-second refresh.\\n\\n5. **Network status:** Use `NWPathMonitor` (already likely in the app) or `Network` framework to get connectivity status — the Flutter panel checks `NetworkInfo.instance.status`.\\n\\n6. **No external deps:** Confirm any new utility (e.g., `NWPathMonitor` wrapper) doesn't duplicate an existing one — check for any network monitor in `Core/Utils/`.\\n\\n7. **project.yml:** Add the new file to the `sources` list under the `talavo` target to ensure XcodeGen picks it up.", "status": "completed", "node_id": "analyze", "node_name": "Analyze Project", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 131.1, "started_at": "2026-03-15T10:02:59.275003+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-15T10:05:10.402288+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "plan=Now I have a thorough understanding of the codebase. Here's the implementation plan:\\n\\n---\\n\\n# Implementation Plan: Debug Panel (Native Swift) — Issue #822\\n\\n## Files to Create\\n\\n### 1. `Features/Browser/ViewModels/DebugPanelViewModel.swift`\\n\\n**DebugPanelViewModel: ObservableObject** — aggregates all debug data, refreshes every 3 seconds.\\n\\n- **Injected dependencies** (via initializer): `BrowserViewModel`, `ContentRuleManager`, `ScriptManager`, `PlaybackLogger`, `SettingsStore`\\n- **@Published properties:**\\n  - `appVersion: String` — from `Bundle.main.infoDictionary`\\n  - `buildNumber: String` — from Bundle\\n  - `environment: String` — `#if DEBUG` → \\"Debug\\", else \\"Release\\"\\n  - `swiftVersion: String` — hardcoded or derived from compiler flag\\n  - `uptime: String` — `ProcessInfo.processInfo.systemUptime` formatted via `FormatUtils.formatDuration`\\n  - `deviceModel: String` — `utsname` syscall or `UIDevice.current.model`\\n  - `osVersion: String` — `UIDevice.current.systemVersion`\\n  - `tabCount: Int` — from `BrowserViewModel.tabs.count`\\n  - `activeUrl: String` — from `BrowserViewModel.activeTab.currentUrl`\\n  - `networkStatus: String` — from `NWPathMonitor` (see new utility below)\\n  - `ruleListCount: Int` — from `ContentRuleManager.ruleLists.count`\\n  - `blockedCount: Int` — from `ContentRuleManager.blockedCount`\\n  - `scriptCount: Int` — from `ScriptManager.scriptCount`\\n  - `ramUsage: String` — `os_proc_available_memory()` vs `ProcessInfo.processInfo.physicalMemory`\\n  - `downloadsFolderSize: String` — computed async via `FileManager`\\n  - `screenshotsFolderSize: String` — computed async via `FileManager`\\n  - `playbackLogs: [String]` — from `PlaybackLogger.getRecentEntries(count: 40)`\\n  - `actionMessage: String?` — transient feedback for action buttons\\n- **Methods:**\\n  - `refresh()` — updates all dynamic properties; runs folder size calculations in `Task { }` on background\\n  - `clearCache()` — clears `URLCache.shared`, sets actionMessage\\n  - `clearCookies()` — clears `WKWebsiteDataStore.default()` cookies\\n  - `clearScreenshots()` — removes screenshots directory contents via `FileManager`\\n  - `exportLogs()` — returns playback log file URL for share sheet\\n  - `reloadScripts()` — calls `ScriptManager.initialize()` again\\n- **Timer:** `Timer.publish(every: 3, on: .main, in: .common)` — connected in the View via `.onReceive`\\n\\n### 2. `Core/Utils/NetworkMonitor.swift`\\n\\n**NetworkMonitor: ObservableObject** — lightweight `NWPathMonitor` wrapper.\\n\\n- `@Published var isConnected: Bool`\\n- `@Published var connectionType: String` (WiFi / Cellular / None)\\n- `init()` — starts `NWPathMonitor` on a background `DispatchQueue`\\n- `deinit` — cancels monitor\\n- Inject as `@EnvironmentObject` from `AppDependencies`\\n\\n### 3. `Features/Browser/Views/DebugPanelView.swift`\\n\\n**DebugPanelView: View** — the main debug panel UI.\\n\\n- **Layout:** Fixed width 240pt, max height 70% screen via `GeometryReader`, scrollable `ScrollView`\\n- **Outer container:** `GlassCard(cornerRadius: 22)` — reuse existing component\\n- **Sections** (each a `VStack` with a caps label header):\\n  - **APP** — 4 `InfoRow`s: Version, Environment, Swift, Uptime\\n  - **DEVICE** — 2 `InfoRow`s: Model, iOS version\\n  - **BROWSER** — 4 `InfoRow`s: Tabs, Active URL (truncated), Network\\n  - **AD BLOCK** — 3 `InfoRow`s: Rules, Scripts, Blocked count\\n  - **STORAGE** — 3 `InfoRow`s: RAM, Downloads size, Screenshots size\\n  - **ACTIONS** — Horizontal flow of small action buttons (clear cache, cookies, screenshots, export logs, reload scripts); each sets `actionMessage` on tap with haptic feedback (`UIImpactFeedbackGenerator`)\\n  - **PLAYBACK LOGS** — Expandable section, last 40 entries in `.caption` monospace font; color-coded: `[DART]` → `.blue`, `[JS]` → `AppColors.error`, `[IOS]` → `.orange`\\n  - **AD BLOCK LOGS** — Expandable section (placeholder with note: os.Logger has no in-process retrieval; add buffered logger later or show \\"See Console.app\\")\\n- **Sub-views** (private structs inside the file):\\n  - `SectionHeader` — uppercase label, `.ultraThinMaterial` pill background\\n  - `InfoRow` — label + value in `HStack`, `.caption`/`.caption2` fonts\\n  - `ActionChip` — small rounded button with SF Symbol icon + label\\n- **State:**\\n  - `@StateObject var viewModel: DebugPanelViewModel`\\n  - `@State var playbackLogsExpanded = false`\\n  - `@State var adBlockLogsExpanded = false`\\n  - `@Binding var isPresented: Bool` — for dismiss\\n- **Auto-refresh:** `.onReceive(Timer.publish(every: 3, ...))` calls `viewModel.refresh()`\\n- **Positioning:** Overlay aligned `.topTrailing` with some padding, so it floats over browser content\\n\\n### 4. `Core/Utils/ContentRuleLogger.swift`\\n\\n**ContentRuleLogger** — in-memory buffer for ad block logs (same pattern as `PlaybackLogger`).\\n\\n- `log(_ message: String)` — appends with timestamp, caps at 50 entries\\n- `getRecentEntries(count: Int) -> [String]`\\n- Replace `AppLogger.contentRules.info(...)` calls in `ContentRuleManager` with dual-logging: keep `os.Logger` AND append to `ContentRuleLogger`\\n- Inject via `AppDependencies`\\n\\n## Files to Modify\\n\\n### 5. `Core/DI/AppDependencies.swift`\\n\\n- Add properties:\\n  - `let networkMonitor: NetworkMonitor`\\n  - `let contentRuleLogger: ContentRuleLogger`\\n- Initialize them in `init()`\\n- Pass `contentRuleLogger` to `ContentRuleManager` initializer\\n\\n### 6. `App/TalavoApp.swift`\\n\\n- Add `.environmentObject(dependencies.networkMonitor)` to the injection chain\\n- Add `.environmentObject(dependencies.contentRuleLogger)` to the injection chain\\n- Note: `PlaybackLogger` is already injected (it's already an `ObservableObject` but not in the environment chain — verify and add `.environmentObject(dependencies.playbackLogger)` if missing)\\n\\n### 7. `Features/AdBlock/Services/ContentRuleManager.swift`\\n\\n- Accept `ContentRuleLogger` in initializer\\n- At each `AppLogger.contentRules.info/error/warning(...)` call, also call `contentRuleLogger.log(...)` so entries are buffered for the debug panel\\n\\n### 8. `Features/Browser/Views/BrowserScreen.swift`\\n\\n- Add `@State private var showDebugPanel = false`\\n- Add debug panel overlay in the `ZStack`:\\n  ```\\n  if showDebugPanel {\\n      DebugPanelView(isPresented: $showDebugPanel, ...)\\n          .frame(maxWidth: .infinity, maxHeight: .infinity, alignment: .topTrailing)\\n          .padding()\\n          .transition(.opacity.combined(with: .move(edge: .trailing)))\\n  }\\n  ```\\n- Add toggle trigger — **hidden 5-tap gesture** on the top-right corner area:\\n  ```\\n  .overlay(alignment: .topTrailing) {\\n      Color.clear\\n          .frame(width: 44, height: 44)\\n          .contentShape(Rectangle())\\n          .onTapGesture(count: 5) { showDebugPanel.toggle() }\\n  }\\n  ```\\n- Wrap in `#if DEBUG` so the trigger only exists in debug builds\\n\\n### 9. `project.yml`\\n\\n- **No changes needed** — the `sources` key already uses `- talavo` which includes all files under `talavo/` recursively. XcodeGen will pick up new files automatically.\\n\\n## Implementation Order\\n\\n1. **ContentRuleLogger** — simple utility, no dependencies\\n2. **NetworkMonitor** — simple utility, no dependencies\\n3. **Modify AppDependencies** — wire up new utilities\\n4. **Modify TalavoApp** — inject new environment objects\\n5. **Modify ContentRuleManager** — add dual-logging\\n6. **DebugPanelViewModel** — core logic\\n7. **DebugPanelView** — UI\\n8. **Modify BrowserScreen** — add overlay + 5-tap trigger\\n\\n## Edge Cases & Risks\\n\\n- **Folder size calculation** — `FileManager` enumeration can be slow for large directories. Must run in `Task { }` / background actor. Cache the result and only recompute every 3s refresh cycle.\\n- **Memory readings** — `os_proc_available_memory()` is available iOS 13+, safe to use. Returns bytes of available RAM (not used RAM). Compute used = physical - available.\\n- **`PlaybackLogger` not in environment** — it's in `AppDependencies` but NOT injected via `.environmentObject()` in `TalavoApp.swift`. Must add it.\\n- **Ad block logs** — `os.Logger` has no in-process retrieval API. The `ContentRuleLogger` buffer solves this, but requires modifying `ContentRuleManager` to dual-log.\\n- **Thread safety** — `ContentRuleLogger.log()` may be called from async contexts. Use `@MainActor` or a serial queue for the buffer.\\n- **Panel dismissal** — tapping outside the panel should dismiss it. Add a full-screen transparent tap catcher behind the panel.\\n- **Device model string** — `UIDevice.current.model` returns generic \\"iPhone\\". For specific model (e.g. \\"iPhone 15 Pro\\"), use `utsname` + `machine` field with a lookup table, or just show the generic name to keep it simple.\\n- **Export logs action** — needs to present a `UIActivityViewController` / ShareLink. Use SwiftUI's `ShareLink` (iOS 16+) or a `@State var showShareSheet` with the log file URL.\\n- **No `ScriptletManager` in environment** — it exists in `AppDependencies` but isn't injected as environment object. Access it through `AppDependencies` directly (`@EnvironmentObject var deps: AppDependencies`) for rule count.", "status": "completed", "node_id": "plan", "node_name": "Plan", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 179.9, "started_at": "2026-03-15T10:05:10.453466+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-15T10:08:10.402353+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "dev_result=PR is open and branch is fully pushed (no local commits ahead of remote).\\n\\nhttps://github.com/bakicelebi/talavo/pull/830", "status": "completed", "node_id": "develop", "node_name": "Develop", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 14.7, "started_at": "2026-03-15T10:17:34.458832+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-15T10:17:49.166290+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "review_result=I've reviewed the full diff and verified all referenced APIs against the existing codebase. Here's my assessment:\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Review: #822 Add debug panel in native Swift version\\n\\n### Checklist Results\\n\\n| # | Check | Result |\\n|---|-------|--------|\\n| 1 | **SwiftUI correctness** | `@StateObject` for VM, `@EnvironmentObject` for monitors, `@State` for local UI — all correct. No business logic in view bodies. |\\n| 2 | **Memory safety** | `[weak self]` in `NetworkMonitor.pathUpdateHandler`, `Task.detached` in VM, and `clearCookies` callback. Timer subscription managed by SwiftUI `.onReceive` lifecycle. |\\n| 3 | **Liquid Glass** | Uses `GlassCard(cornerRadius: 22)` for the panel. `.ultraThinMaterial` on chips/headers is fine for small elements. |\\n| 4 | **Theme compliance** | Uses `AppColors.talavoMint`, `.success`, `.error`, and system `.secondary`/`.primary`. No hardcoded colors. |\\n| 5 | **Architecture** | MVVM with `DebugPanelViewModel` + `DebugPanelView` in `Features/Browser/`. Utils in `Core/Utils/`. Dependencies registered in `AppDependencies`. |\\n| 6 | **Persistence** | No new persistence — reads existing `adblock_last_fetch` only. |\\n| 7 | **Networking** | No new network calls. `NetworkMonitor` uses `NWPathMonitor` (local, no URLs). |\\n| 8 | **Code quality** | No force unwraps, no force casts. Proper access control. DEBUG-gated. |\\n| 9 | **Matches requirements** | Debug panel with app info, device info, browser state, ad block stats, storage, actions, and logs. Activated via 5-tap gesture. |\\n\\n### Issues Found\\n\\n**1. ISO8601DateFormatter created on every log call** (`ContentRuleLogger.swift:8`)\\n\\nA new `ISO8601DateFormatter()` is allocated per `log()` call. These are expensive to create — cache it as a property:\\n\\n```swift\\nclass ContentRuleLogger: ObservableObject {\\n    private var entries: [String] = []\\n    private let maxEntries = 50\\n    private let formatter = ISO8601DateFormatter()\\n\\n    func log(_ message: String) {\\n        let timestamp = formatter.string(from: Date())\\n        ...\\n    }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n**2. Unnecessary `environmentObject` injections** (`TalavoApp.swift`)\\n\\n`.environmentObject(dependencies.playbackLogger)` and `.environmentObject(dependencies.contentRuleLogger)` are added but neither type is consumed as `@EnvironmentObject` in any view. They're accessed via `dependencies.playbackLogger` / `dependencies.contentRuleLogger` in `DebugPanelViewModel`. Only `networkMonitor` is actually used as `@EnvironmentObject` in `DebugPanelView`. The other two can be removed from TalavoApp to keep the environment clean.\\n\\n### Notes (non-blocking)\\n\\n- `DebugPanelView.swift` is 321 lines, but the main view is well under 200 — the rest is private helper views (`Section`, `InfoRow`, `ActionChip`, etc.) tightly coupled to this panel. Acceptable.\\n- `deviceModelString()` is a file-scope free function rather than a static method on the VM. Works fine, just unconventional.\\n- `showAction()` can have overlapping `Task.sleep` timers if called rapidly, but for a debug panel this is negligible.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**CHANGES_REQUESTED**\\n\\nTwo fixes needed:\\n1. Cache the `ISO8601DateFormatter` in `ContentRuleLogger` instead of creating one per call.\\n2. Remove the unnecessary `.environmentObject(dependencies.playbackLogger)` and `.environmentObject(dependencies.contentRuleLogger)` from `TalavoApp.swift`., review_verdict=CHANGES_REQUESTED", "status": "completed", "node_id": "review", "node_name": "Review", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 95.2, "started_at": "2026-03-15T10:17:49.221318+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-15T10:19:24.387305+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "review_verdict=CHANGES_REQUESTED → failed", "status": "completed", "node_id": "review_gate", "node_name": "Review Gate", "node_type": "condition", "duration_s": 0.1, "started_at": "2026-03-15T10:19:24.442374+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-15T10:19:24.492850+00:00"}, {"error": "Pipeline failed after max review rounds for issue #822", "output": null, "status": "failed", "node_id": "failed", "node_name": "Failed", "node_type": "failed", "duration_s": 1010.7, "started_at": "2026-03-15T10:19:24.543762+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-15T10:19:24.543767+00:00"}]	\N
