_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 13.8, "started_at": "2026-03-15T10:14:14.026329+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-15T10:14:27.819333+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "clarity_status=CLEAR → analyze", "status": "completed", "node_id": "clarity_gate", "node_name": "Clarity Gate", "node_type": "condition", "duration_s": 0.0, "started_at": "2026-03-15T10:14:27.890290+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-15T10:14:27.938975+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "project_context=## Project Context Summary: Issue #806 — Fix Add Shortcut on Home Screen\\n\\n### Root Cause\\nThe `onAddTap` callback in `HomeScreen.swift` is empty — the button exists but does nothing:\\n\\n```swift\\n// HomeScreen.swift ~line 114\\nonAddTap: {\\n    // Show add shortcut dialog  ← EMPTY, never implemented\\n}\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Relevant Files\\n\\n| File | Purpose |\\n|---|---|\\n| `Features/Home/Views/HomeScreen.swift` | Main home screen — where the fix goes |\\n| `Features/Home/Widgets/ReorderableShortcutGrid.swift` | Grid with AddShortcutCard + `onAddTap` closure |\\n| `Features/Home/Widgets/AddShortcutCard.swift` | The \\"+\\" button UI component |\\n| `Features/Shortcuts/Store/ShortcutsStore.swift` | `@EnvironmentObject` with `addShortcut(name:url:)` |\\n| `Features/Home/Store/HomeGridStore.swift` | Reactive grid state (updates automatically) |\\n| `Features/Home/HomeConstants.swift` | `maxVisibleShortcuts = 6`, card sizes |\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Patterns to Follow\\n\\n**Sheet presentation pattern** (used throughout Settings):\\n```swift\\n@State private var showAddShortcutSheet = false\\n\\n// In body:\\n.sheet(isPresented: $showAddShortcutSheet) { AddShortcutSheet() }\\n    .presentationDetents([.height(X)])\\n    .presentationDragIndicator(.visible)\\n    .frostedSheetBackground()\\n```\\n\\n**Existing sheet examples to mirror:** `ClearDataSheet.swift` in Settings — small, focused, frosted glass bottom sheet.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Reusable Components\\n- `ShortcutsStore.addShortcut(name: String, url: String)` — already handles favicon fetching, UUID generation, UserDefaults persistence\\n- `.frostedSheetBackground()` modifier — standard sheet styling\\n- `TapScaleButton` — standard interactive button\\n- `GlassCard` — card container used throughout home screen\\n- `HomeScreen` already has `@EnvironmentObject private var shortcuts: ShortcutsStore` injected\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Technical Considerations\\n- The grid reacts automatically to `ShortcutsStore` changes — no manual refresh needed after calling `addShortcut`\\n- Max 6 shortcuts shown on home screen; a \\"See All\\" card appears beyond that (already handled by `ReorderableShortcutGrid`)\\n- URL validation should be applied before calling `addShortcut` — check how other URL inputs are handled (e.g., browser address bar)\\n- The sheet should be a new file: `Features/Home/Widgets/AddShortcutSheet.swift` to follow the existing folder/naming convention\\n- Localization keys should be added to the `.lproj` string files for all 16 languages (or at minimum `en.lproj`)", "status": "completed", "node_id": "analyze", "node_name": "Analyze Project", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 73.2, "started_at": "2026-03-15T10:14:27.985446+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-15T10:15:41.154122+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "plan=## Implementation Plan: Issue #806 — Fix Add Shortcut on Home Screen\\n\\n### Overview\\nWire up the empty `onAddTap` callback in `HomeScreen.swift` to present a bottom sheet with name/URL inputs, then call `ShortcutsStore.addShortcut()`. One new file, one modified file.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Step 1: Create `AddShortcutSheet.swift`\\n\\n**New file:** `Features/Home/Widgets/AddShortcutSheet.swift`\\n\\n- **Structure:** A SwiftUI `View` with two `TextField`s (name, URL) and a Save button\\n- **State:**\\n  - `@State private var name: String = \\"\\"`\\n  - `@State private var url: String = \\"\\"`\\n  - `@FocusState private var focusedField` (enum: `.name`, `.url`)\\n  - `@Environment(\\\\.dismiss) private var dismiss`\\n  - `@EnvironmentObject private var shortcuts: ShortcutsStore`\\n- **Layout (mirror `ClearDataSheet` pattern):**\\n  - `NavigationStack` wrapping a `VStack` or `List`\\n  - `.navigationTitle(\\"Add Shortcut\\")` with `.inline` display mode\\n  - Two text fields: \\"Name\\" and \\"URL\\" (URL field with `.keyboardType(.URL)` and `.textInputAutocapitalization(.never)`)\\n  - Save button using `TapScaleButton` or `.borderedProminent` style\\n  - Cancel via navigation bar trailing/leading button or sheet dismiss\\n- **Validation:**\\n  - Save button `.disabled()` when URL is empty\\n  - On save: normalize URL with `URLUtils.resolveInput(url)` (prepends `https://` if needed), then call `shortcuts.addShortcut(name:url:)`\\n  - If name is empty, derive a default from the URL host (or pass empty — check what `addShortcut` does with empty name)\\n  - Dismiss sheet after saving\\n- **Styling:**\\n  - Use `AppTheme` colors (`textPrimaryColor`, `surfaceColor`)\\n  - Respect `@Environment(\\\\.colorScheme)`\\n- **Presentation detent:** `.height(280)` (two fields + button + padding — adjust as needed)\\n- **Apply:** `.frostedSheetBackground()`, `.presentationDragIndicator(.visible)`\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Step 2: Modify `HomeScreen.swift`\\n\\n**File:** `Features/Home/Views/HomeScreen.swift`\\n\\nTwo changes:\\n\\n1. **Add state variable** (near other `@State` declarations):\\n   - `@State private var showAddShortcutSheet = false`\\n\\n2. **Wire up `onAddTap`** (~line 114):\\n   - Replace the empty closure with `showAddShortcutSheet = true`\\n\\n3. **Add `.sheet()` modifier** on the shortcut grid or body:\\n   ```\\n   .sheet(isPresented: $showAddShortcutSheet) {\\n       AddShortcutSheet()\\n           .presentationDetents([.height(280)])\\n           .presentationDragIndicator(.visible)\\n           .frostedSheetBackground()\\n   }\\n   ```\\n\\n---\\n\\n### What Does NOT Need to Change\\n\\n| Component | Reason |\\n|---|---|\\n| `ReorderableShortcutGrid` | Already passes `onAddTap` through — no changes needed |\\n| `AddShortcutCard` | UI widget works fine — just wasn't being triggered |\\n| `ShortcutsStore` | `addShortcut(name:url:)` already handles persistence, favicon fetch, UUID |\\n| `HomeGridStore` | Reactively rebuilds when `ShortcutsStore.shortcuts` changes |\\n| Localization files | No `.lproj` files exist in the project — all strings are hardcoded |\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Edge Cases & Considerations\\n\\n- **Max shortcuts:** The grid already handles >6 shortcuts by showing a \\"See All\\" card — no cap enforcement needed in the sheet\\n- **Duplicate URLs:** `ShortcutsStore.addShortcut()` doesn't prevent duplicates — acceptable for v1, matches current behavior\\n- **URL normalization:** Use `URLUtils.resolveInput()` so users can type `google.com` without `https://` — consistent with the browser address bar behavior\\n- **Empty name:** If the user leaves name blank, either derive from URL host or pass empty and let the shortcut display the URL — check existing shortcut cards for how they handle missing names\\n- **Keyboard handling:** Auto-focus the name field on sheet open via `@FocusState`; URL field should use `.keyboardType(.URL)` and `.autocorrectionDisabled(true)`\\n\\n---\\n\\n### File Summary\\n\\n| File | Action |\\n|---|---|\\n| `Features/Home/Widgets/AddShortcutSheet.swift` | **Create** — new bottom sheet view |\\n| `Features/Home/Views/HomeScreen.swift` | **Modify** — add state, wire `onAddTap`, attach `.sheet()` |\\n\\n**Total scope:** ~60-80 lines new code, ~5 lines modified.", "status": "completed", "node_id": "plan", "node_name": "Plan", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 122.7, "started_at": "2026-03-15T10:15:41.206532+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-15T10:17:43.903035+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "dev_result=Everything is already done — the commit is pushed and the PR exists.\\n\\nhttps://github.com/bakicelebi/talavo/pull/831", "status": "completed", "node_id": "develop", "node_name": "Develop", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 10.7, "started_at": "2026-03-15T10:20:17.220255+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-15T10:20:27.915682+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "review_result=Good — `ShortcutsStore` is injected at the app level via `TalavoApp.swift`, so the sheet will inherit it.\\n\\n**APPROVED**\\n\\nThe PR is clean and correct:\\n\\n1. **SwiftUI correctness** — `@State` for the sheet toggle is appropriate. `@EnvironmentObject` for `ShortcutsStore` and `@FocusState` are used correctly. No business logic in the view body.\\n2. **Memory safety** — No closures that could cause retain cycles. No Combine subscriptions needed.\\n3. **Liquid Glass consistency** — Uses `.frostedSheetBackground()` matching other sheets in the project (e.g., `ClearDataSheet`, `LandingPageSheet`).\\n4. **Theme compliance** — Uses `AppTheme.primaryColor(for:)`, no hardcoded colors.\\n5. **Architecture** — New widget placed in `Features/Home/Widgets/`, consistent with existing structure. `ShortcutsStore.addShortcut()` already exists and handles persistence.\\n6. **Code quality** — No force unwraps, proper URL resolution via `URLUtils.resolveInput`, graceful name fallback to hostname. `canSave` validation prevents empty URLs. File is 65 lines — well under limit.\\n7. **Matches requirements** — The \\"Add Shortcut\\" button on the home screen was a no-op (empty closure comment); now it presents a proper sheet for adding shortcuts., review_verdict=APPROVED", "status": "completed", "node_id": "review", "node_name": "Review", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 39.4, "started_at": "2026-03-15T10:20:27.967434+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-15T10:21:07.319726+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "review_verdict=APPROVED → done", "status": "completed", "node_id": "review_gate", "node_name": "Review Gate", "node_type": "condition", "duration_s": 0.0, "started_at": "2026-03-15T10:21:07.373805+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-15T10:21:07.423280+00:00"}, {"err