me).\\n- **Scope:** Small, well-defined UI + logic change to an existing sheet component.", "status": "completed", "node_id": "check_clarity", "node_name": "Check Clarity", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 14.4, "started_at": "2026-03-15T10:29:39.149608+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-15T10:29:53.575800+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "clarity_status=CLEAR → analyze", "status": "completed", "node_id": "clarity_gate", "node_name": "Clarity Gate", "node_type": "condition", "duration_s": 0.0, "started_at": "2026-03-15T10:29:53.627333+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-15T10:29:53.675320+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "project_context=## Project Context Summary for Issue #817\\n\\n### Relevant Files\\n\\n| File | Purpose |\\n|------|---------|\\n| `Features/Settings/Widgets/ClearDataSheet.swift` | **Primary file to modify** - currently has 2 buttons (Clear History, Clear Web Cache) with `.height(220)` detent |\\n| `Features/Settings/Store/SettingsStore.swift` | May need a new enum/setting if preferences are persisted |\\n| `Features/History/Store/HistoryStore.swift` | **Reuse directly** - already has `clearByPeriod(before:)` and `clearEntries(since:)` |\\n| `Features/History/Views/HistoryScreen.swift` | Reference for time period grouping and `confirmationDialog` pattern |\\n| `Features/Settings/Views/SettingsScreen.swift` | Shows how sheets are presented; `ClearDataSheet` triggered here |\\n| `Core/Widgets/AppSheet.swift` | `frostedSheetBackground()` modifier |\\n\\n### Current ClearDataSheet Implementation\\n\\nUses `WKDataStore.default()` with `allWebsiteDataTypes()` — clears everything at once. Sheet is `NavigationStack` + `List` with `.listStyle(.plain)`, `.scrollContentBackground(.hidden)`, and `.frostedSheetBackground()`.\\n\\n### Coding Patterns to Follow\\n\\n- **Sheet structure:** `NavigationStack` → `List` → `ForEach` with checkmarks (see `ThemeBottomSheet`, `VideoQualitySheet`)\\n- **State:** `@State` for local selection, `@EnvironmentObject` for injected stores (`HistoryStore`, `SettingsStore`)\\n- **Dismiss:** `@Environment(\\\\.dismiss) private var dismiss`\\n- **Sizing:** Increase `.presentationDetents` from `.height(220)` as options expand\\n- **Enums:** Follow `ThemeMode: String, CaseIterable` pattern if adding a new type\\n- **Strings:** Hardcoded inline (no `.strings` files in use)\\n- **Time periods:** `Calendar.current.date(byAdding: .hour, value: -1, to: Date())` etc. — same as HistoryScreen\\n\\n### Existing Code to Reuse\\n\\n- `HistoryStore.clearAll()` and `clearEntries(since:)` handle history time periods directly\\n- `WKWebsiteDataStore` type constants: `.diskCache`, `.memoryCache`, `.cookies`, `.localStorage` (subsets of `allWebsiteDataTypes()`)\\n- Time period date math from `HistoryScreen` (Today/Last 7 Days pattern)\\n\\n### Technical Considerations\\n\\n1. **WKWebsiteDataStore has no timestamps** — `WKWebsiteDataRecord` does not expose creation/modification dates. Time-based filtering for web data (cache, cookies, local storage) is **not natively supported**. The time period option can realistically apply only to **History** (which has timestamps in `HistoryStore`), while web data types (cache/cookies/local storage) should be \\"clear all of this type\\" toggles.\\n\\n2. **Granular type clearing:** Pass specific type sets to `removeData(ofTypes:for:)`:\\n   - Cache: `[WKWebsiteDataTypeDiskCache, WKWebsiteDataTypeMemoryCache]`\\n   - Cookies: `[WKWebsiteDataTypeCookies]`\\n   - Local storage: `[WKWebsiteDataTypeLocalStorage, WKWebsiteDataTypeIndexedDBDatabases, WKWebsiteDataTypeWebSQLDatabases]`\\n\\n3. **UX recommendation:** Two-stage UI — first let user pick *what* to clear (checkboxes for each data type), then (optionally) for History only, pick the time period. This avoids misrepresenting time filtering for web data.\\n\\n4. **Sheet height:** Current `.height(220)` must increase — likely `.height(420–500)` or `.medium` detent depending on final option count.\\n\\n5. Commit `#824` recently redesigned this sheet, so check the current UI carefully before modifying.", "status": "completed", "node_id": "analyze", "node_name": "Analyze Project", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 95.0, "started_at": "2026-03-15T10:29:53.725762+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-15T10:31:28.756083+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "plan=## Implementation Plan for #817 — Add Granular Clear Browsing Data Options\\n\\n### Overview\\n\\nRedesign `ClearDataSheet` from two simple buttons into a checklist UI with toggleable data types and a time-period picker (for history only). Single file change — all modifications stay in `ClearDataSheet.swift`.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Files to Modify\\n\\n#### 1. `Features/Settings/Widgets/ClearDataSheet.swift` (primary — rewrite)\\n\\n**Add enums (top of file):**\\n\\n- `ClearableDataType: String, CaseIterable` — cases: `history`, `cache`, `cookies`, `localStorage`\\n  - Computed properties for `label` (String) and `icon` (SF Symbol name)\\n  - `history` → \\"History\\" / `clock.arrow.circlepath`\\n  - `cache` → \\"Cache\\" / `internaldrive`\\n  - `cookies` → \\"Cookies\\" / `server.rack`\\n  - `localStorage` → \\"Local Storage\\" / `externaldrive`\\n\\n- `TimePeriod: String, CaseIterable` — cases: `lastHour`, `lastDay`, `lastWeek`, `allTime`\\n  - Computed `label` property: \\"Last Hour\\", \\"Last 24 Hours\\", \\"Last 7 Days\\", \\"All Time\\"\\n  - Computed `date` property: returns `Calendar.current.date(byAdding:...)` or `nil` for `.allTime`\\n\\n**Rewrite `ClearDataSheet` body:**\\n\\n- `@State private var selectedTypes: Set<ClearableDataType> = []`\\n- `@State private var selectedPeriod: TimePeriod = .allTime`\\n- `@State private var showConfirmation = false`\\n\\n**UI structure (still `NavigationStack` → `List`):**\\n\\n- **Section 1 — \\"Data to Clear\\"**: `ForEach(ClearableDataType.allCases)` with toggle-style rows\\n  - Each row: `Button` that toggles membership in `selectedTypes`\\n  - Show `checkmark` icon when selected (follow `ThemeBottomSheet` HStack + Spacer + checkmark pattern)\\n  - Use `.foregroundStyle(AppTheme.textPrimaryColor(for: colorScheme))`\\n\\n- **Section 2 — \\"Time Period\\"** (only visible when `selectedTypes.contains(.history)`)\\n  - `ForEach(TimePeriod.allCases)` with single-selection rows\\n  - Same checkmark pattern as Section 1, bound to `selectedPeriod`\\n  - Add a `Section` footer or caption: \\"Time period applies to history only\\"\\n\\n- **Bottom — \\"Clear\\" button**\\n  - Destructive `Button` at bottom of list, disabled when `selectedTypes.isEmpty`\\n  - On tap: set `showConfirmation = true`\\n\\n- **Confirmation dialog** (`.confirmationDialog`):\\n  - Title: \\"Clear selected data?\\"\\n  - Single destructive action that calls `clearSelectedData()` then `dismiss()`\\n\\n**Add `clearSelectedData()` private method:**\\n\\n- If `selectedTypes.contains(.history)`:\\n  - If `selectedPeriod == .allTime` → `history.clearAll()`\\n  - Else → `history.clearEntries(since: selectedPeriod.date!)`\\n- Build `Set<String>` of WK data types from remaining selections:\\n  - `.cache` → `[WKWebsiteDataTypeDiskCache, WKWebsiteDataTypeMemoryCache]`\\n  - `.cookies` → `[WKWebsiteDataTypeCookies]`\\n  - `.localStorage` → `[WKWebsiteDataTypeLocalStorage, WKWebsiteDataTypeIndexedDBDatabases, WKWebsiteDataTypeWebSQLDatabases]`\\n- If WK types non-empty → `WKWebsiteDataStore.default().fetchDataRecords(ofTypes:)` then `removeData(ofTypes:for:)`\\n\\n**Update presentation:**\\n- Change `.presentationDetents([.height(220)])` → `.presentationDetents([.height(480), .medium])`\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Files NOT Modified\\n\\n- **HistoryStore.swift** — already has `clearAll()` and `clearEntries(since:)`, no changes needed\\n- **SettingsStore.swift** — no persistence of clear-data preferences needed (selections are ephemeral)\\n- **SettingsScreen.swift** — already presents `ClearDataSheet`, no changes needed\\n- No new files needed — everything fits in the existing sheet file\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Edge Cases & Risks\\n\\n1. **WKWebsiteDataStore has no timestamps** — time period filtering applies only to History. The UI must make this clear (section footer). Do not attempt to time-filter cookies/cache.\\n2. **Async WebKit removal** — `removeData(ofTypes:for:)` is async but currently fire-and-forget. Keep this pattern (matches existing code) — no need to block the UI.\\n3. **Empty selection** — disable the Clear button when nothing is selected to prevent no-op clears.\\n4. **Sheet height** — with 4 data types + 4 time periods + button + headers, test that `.height(480)` fits. May need adjustment; `.medium` detent as fallback.\\n5. **`WKWebsiteDataTypeDiskCache`/`WKWebsiteDataTypeMemoryCache`** — verify these constants compile on the minimum deployment target. They're available from iOS 9+, so no issue expected.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Implementation Order\\n\\n1. Add `ClearableDataType` and `TimePeriod` enums\\n2. Rewrite the sheet body with sections and selection state\\n3. Implement `clearSelectedData()` method\\n4. Update detent height\\n5. Test: verify each data type clears independently, time period applies only to history, confirmation dialog works\\n6. Run `dart format .` (n/a — Swift file, but check for any Dart files touched)\\n7. Clean up unused imports if any", "status": "completed", "node_id": "plan", "node_name": "Plan", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 51.3, "started_at": "2026-03-15T10:31:28.812399+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-15T10:32:20.117820+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "dev_result=https://github.com/bakicelebi/talavo/pull/833", "status": "completed", "node_id": "develop", "node_name": "Develop", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 92.1, "started_at": "2026-03-15T10:32:20.176474+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-15T10:33:52.267727+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "review_result=Everything checks out. The code:\\n\\n1. **SwiftUI correctness** — `@State` for local selection state, `@EnvironmentObject` for stores, no business logic in the view body. File is 169 lines (under 200).\\n2. **Memory safety** — No closures capturing `self`; the WKWebsiteDataStore callback `{}` is a no-op. Fine.\\n3. **Theme compliance** — Uses `AppTheme.primaryColor` and `AppTheme.textPrimaryColor` with `colorScheme`. No hardcoded colors.\\n4. **Architecture** — Code stays in the existing `Settings/Widgets` folder. Enums are local to this file, which is appropriate.\\n5. **Code quality** — No force unwraps, no force casts, proper access control (`private` on `clearSelectedData`). The `WKDataStore` typealias is fine.\\n6. **Matches requirements** — Granular data type selection (history, cache, cookies, localStorage) with time period filtering for history. Confirmation dialog before destructive action. Uses existing `HistoryStore.clearEntries(since:)` which already exists.\\n7. **Existing patterns** — Uses `.frostedSheetBackground()`, `.presentationDetents`, same list styling as before.\\n\\n**APPROVED**\\n\\nThe implementation is clean and well-structured. It correctly reuses existing `HistoryStore` methods (`clearAll`, `clearEntries(since:)`), follows theme conventions, adds a confirmation dialog for the destructive action, and keeps the view under 200 lines. The `ClearableDataType` and `TimePeriod` enums are well-designed with appropriate WKWebsiteDataStore type mappings., review_verdict=APPROVED", "status": "completed", "node_id": "review", "node_name": "Review", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 35.8, "started_at": "2026-03-15T10:33:52.321678+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-15T10:34:28.149032+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "review_verdict=APPROVED → done", "status": "completed", "node_id": "review_gate", "node_name": "Review Gate", "node_type": "condition", "duration_s": 0.1, "started_at": "2026-03-15T10:34:28.204848+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-15T10:34:28.256789+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "Issue #817 implemented and reviewed. PR ready to merge.", "status": "completed", "n