, "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 15.7, "started_at": "2026-03-16T22:01:36.835109+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-16T22:01:52.506331+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "clarity_status=CLEAR → analyze", "status": "completed", "node_id": "clarity_gate", "node_name": "Clarity Gate", "node_type": "condition", "duration_s": 0.1, "started_at": "2026-03-16T22:01:52.558759+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-16T22:01:52.610097+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "project_context=## Project Context: Issue #877\\n\\n### Relevant Files\\n\\n| File | Purpose |\\n|------|---------|\\n| `Features/Settings/Widgets/LandingPageSheet.swift` | **Target file** — current list-based picker using `NavigationStack` + `List` |\\n| `Features/Home/Widgets/ReorderableShortcutGrid.swift` | Grid layout to adapt (4-col, `HomeGridItem`, drag-to-reorder) |\\n| `Features/Home/Widgets/CustomShortcutCard.swift` | Individual card with favicon + label + `TapScaleButtonStyle` |\\n| `Features/Home/Store/HomeGridStore.swift` | `orderedItems: [HomeGridItem]` — combined sites + custom shortcuts in user order |\\n| `Features/Shortcuts/Store/ShortcutsStore.swift` | `shortcuts: [ShortcutItem]` — custom shortcut data |\\n| `Features/Settings/Store/SettingsStore.swift` | `defaultLandingPage: Int` — `-1` = Home, `≥0` = index into `SupportedSites.all` |\\n| `Core/Constants/SupportedSites.swift` | `SupportedSites.all` — YouTube, YouTube Music, Twitch, Dailymotion |\\n| `Core/Widgets/GlassCard.swift` | Card container (iOS 26 `.glassEffect`, fallback `.ultraThinMaterial`) |\\n| `Core/Widgets/AppSheet.swift` | `frostedSheetBackground()` modifier + drag handle |\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Current `LandingPageSheet` Behavior\\n- `NavigationStack` + plain `List`\\n- Shows \\"Home\\" row, then `SupportedSites.all` rows\\n- `.presentationDetents([.medium])` + `frostedSheetBackground()`\\n- On tap: sets `settings.defaultLandingPage`, dismisses\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Key Patterns to Follow\\n\\n**Bottom sheet structure** (all sheets use this):\\n```swift\\n.sheet(isPresented: $show) {\\n    ContentView()\\n        .presentationDetents([.height(X)])\\n        .presentationDragIndicator(.visible)\\n        .frostedSheetBackground()\\n}\\n```\\n\\n**`HomeGridItem` enum** — wraps both site configs and custom shortcuts, use this as the data type for grid items.\\n\\n**`ReorderableShortcutGrid`** accepts `columns: Int` and renders up to `maxVisible` items. For a picker, strip out edit/reorder logic and replace long-press with a simple tap selection.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Technical Considerations\\n\\n1. **Data source**: Use `HomeGridStore.orderedItems` to mirror the exact home screen order. Always prepend a \\"Home\\" option (sentinel value `-1`).\\n\\n2. **Selection mapping**: Site items map to their index in `SupportedSites.all`; custom shortcuts have no corresponding `defaultLandingPage` integer currently — check if the store needs extending or if only sites are selectable.\\n\\n3. **No edit mode needed**: Strip `isEditMode`, drag gesture, and the \\"Add\\"/\\"More\\" buttons from the adapted grid.\\n\\n4. **Sheet height**: Card (56pt) + label (~20pt) + spacing = ~76pt per row. Two rows + title + padding ≈ `~320–380pt`. Use `.height(360)` detent (adjustable).\\n\\n5. **Checkmark indication**: The current list uses `Image(systemName: \\"checkmark\\")`. In the grid, overlay a checkmark badge on the selected card's `GlassCard`.\\n\\n6. **`HomeGridStore` access**: It's injected as an `@EnvironmentObject` at root — available inside the sheet if the sheet is presented from a view that has it in its environment.", "status": "completed", "node_id": "analyze", "node_name": "Analyze Project", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 100.7, "started_at": "2026-03-16T22:01:52.680997+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-16T22:03:33.368158+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "plan=Now I have a complete picture. Here's the implementation plan:\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Implementation Plan: #877 — Landing Page Picker with Shortcuts Grid\\n\\n### Overview\\n\\nReplace the `List`-based picker in `LandingPageSheet` with a grid of shortcut cards (matching the home screen layout), presented in a bottom sheet. Users tap a card to select it as their default landing page, with a checkmark overlay on the selected card.\\n\\n### Files to Modify\\n\\n#### 1. `Features/Settings/Widgets/LandingPageSheet.swift` — **Full rewrite**\\n\\nReplace the entire `NavigationStack` + `List` implementation with:\\n\\n- **Remove**: `NavigationStack`, `List`, all `ForEach` row logic\\n- **Add**: A `VStack` with a title label (\\"Default Landing Page\\") and a grid of cards\\n- **\\"Home\\" card**: Prepend a special card before the shortcut items — uses `Image(systemName: \\"house\\")` inside a `GlassCard`, name \\"Home\\". Tap sets `settings.defaultLandingUrl = nil`\\n- **Shortcut cards**: Iterate `gridStore.orderedItems` (not `shortcuts.shortcuts`) to match home screen order\\n- **Grid layout**: Reuse the same layout math from `ReorderableShortcutGrid`:\\n  - 4-column grid using `ZStack` + manual `position()` placement\\n  - Same constants: `HomeConstants.cardSize`, `HomeConstants.cardBorderRadius`, `HomeConstants.gridSpacing`, `HomeConstants.gridRunSpacing`\\n- **Card rendering**: Reuse the same `cardContent` pattern from `ReorderableShortcutGrid` (GlassCard + favicon + label) — copy the private `cardContent(for:)` method directly\\n- **Selection indicator**: Overlay a checkmark badge on the selected card:\\n  - Small circle with `checkmark` SF Symbol, positioned at top-trailing corner of the `GlassCard`\\n  - Use `AppTheme.primaryColor` for the checkmark tint\\n  - \\"Home\\" is selected when `settings.defaultLandingUrl == nil`\\n  - A shortcut is selected when `settings.defaultLandingUrl == shortcut.url`\\n- **Tap action**: On tap, set `settings.defaultLandingUrl` (or `nil` for Home) and `dismiss()`\\n- **Use `TapScaleButtonStyle`** on each card button for consistent press feedback\\n- **Sheet presentation**: Keep `.presentationDragIndicator(.visible)` and `.frostedSheetBackground()`\\n- **Sheet detent**: Use `.presentationDetents([.height(360)])` — fits title + 2 rows of cards + padding. If items exceed 8, add expand/collapse chevron button (same pattern as `ReorderableShortcutGrid`)\\n- **Environment objects needed**: Add `@EnvironmentObject private var gridStore: HomeGridStore` (in addition to existing `settings` and `shortcuts`)\\n- **On appear**: Call `gridStore.rebuild(shortcuts: shortcuts.shortcuts)` to ensure grid data is fresh\\n\\n### What NOT to Do\\n\\n- **Do NOT create a new reusable grid component** — the grid layout is simple enough to inline. Extracting a shared component would be premature since the picker grid has different behavior (no edit mode, no drag, has selection state, has a \\"Home\\" sentinel card)\\n- **Do NOT modify `ReorderableShortcutGrid`** — it stays as-is for the home screen\\n- **Do NOT modify `HomeGridStore` or `SettingsStore`** — the existing `defaultLandingUrl: String?` already handles the selection mapping perfectly (`nil` = Home, URL string = specific shortcut)\\n- **Do NOT add new model types** — `ShortcutItem` already has everything needed\\n\\n### Implementation Details\\n\\n**Grid structure** (pseudocode layout):\\n```\\nTitle: \\"Default Landing Page\\"\\n─────────────────────────\\n[ Home ]  [ YT ]  [ YTM ]  [ Twitch ]\\n[DailyM]  [custom1] [custom2] ...\\n```\\n\\n**Selection checkmark overlay**: A small (20×20) circle with SF Symbol `checkmark` at `.topTrailing` offset, using `.overlay(alignment: .topTrailing)` on the `GlassCard`. Background: `AppTheme.primaryColor`, foreground: white.\\n\\n**\\"Home\\" card data flow**:\\n- Not a `ShortcutItem` — render it separately before the `ForEach`\\n- Position it at index 0, offset all shortcut item positions by +1\\n- Uses `house` SF Symbol at 24pt inside a `GlassCard`\\n\\n### Edge Cases & Risks\\n\\n1. **Empty shortcuts list**: If user has deleted all shortcuts, only \\"Home\\" card shows. Grid should handle gracefully (single card, single row).\\n\\n2. **Grid height calculation**: Total items = 1 (Home) + `gridStore.orderedItems.count`. Calculate rows dynamically: `ceil(totalItems / 4)`. Adjust sheet detent height accordingly, or use `.medium` as a safe fallback for many items.\\n\\n3. **HomeGridStore availability**: `HomeGridStore` is injected as `@EnvironmentObject` at the app root. Since `LandingPageSheet` is presented from Settings (which is within the root view hierarchy), it should already be available. **Verify** the environment injection chain from where the sheet is presented — if the sheet is presented via `.sheet()` modifier, environment objects propagate automatically in SwiftUI.\\n\\n4. **Custom shortcuts without URLs**: All `ShortcutItem`s have a `url` field, so mapping to `defaultLandingUrl` is straightforward.\\n\\n5. **Scroll for many shortcuts**: If the user has many custom shortcuts (>8), either:\\n   - Use a `ScrollView` wrapping the grid, OR\\n   - Cap visible items at `maxVisible` with the expand/collapse chevron\\n   - **Recommendation**: Use expand/collapse (consistent with home screen behavior), with a `.medium` detent when expanded\\n\\n### Testing Checklist\\n\\n- Tap \\"Home\\" card → `defaultLandingUrl` becomes `nil`, sheet dismisses\\n- Tap a shortcut card → `defaultLandingUrl` becomes that shortcut's URL, sheet dismisses\\n- Checkmark appears on the currently selected card on open\\n- Grid order matches home screen order\\n- Adding/removing custom shortcuts reflects in the picker\\n- Sheet displays correctly in both light and dark mode\\n- Works with 0, 1, 4, 8, and 12+ shortcuts", "status": "completed", "node_id": "plan", "node_name": "Plan", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 92.5, "started_at": "2026-03-16T22:03:33.419721+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-16T22:05:05.874839+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "dev_result=https://github.com/bakicelebi/talavo/pull/893", "status": "completed", "node_id": "develop", "node_name": "Develop", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 161.0, "started_at": "2026-03-16T22:05:05.933630+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-16T22:07:46.919530+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "review_result=**APPROVED**\\n\\nThe code is clean and well-structured. Here's my review summary:\\n\\n**SwiftUI correctness** — Property wrappers are correct: `@EnvironmentObject` for shared stores, `@Environment` for dismiss/colorScheme. No business logic in the body. View is 166 lines, well under the 200-line limit.\\n\\n**Liquid Glass consistency** — Uses `GlassCard` and `.frostedSheetBackground()` properly, matching existing patterns from the home screen grid.\\n\\n**Theme compliance** — All colors go through `AppTheme` (`primaryColor`, `textPrimaryColor`, `surfaceColor`). No hardcoded colors. Dark mode supported via `colorScheme`.\\n\\n**Architecture** — Stays in the correct `Features/Settings/Widgets/` location. Reuses `HomeGridStore` and `HomeConstants` from the home feature to ensure visual consistency between the picker and the actual home grid.\\n\\n**Code quality** — No force unwraps or force casts. The `PickerItem` enum cleanly models the \\"Home + shortcuts\\" concept. Grid layout math is straightforward. `contentShape(Rectangle())` ensures the full card area is tappable.\\n\\n**Matches requirements** — Issue #877 asked for the landing page picker to show the shortcuts grid instead of a plain list. The implementation replaces the `List`-based picker with a visual grid using `GlassCard` icons, matching the home screen appearance. Selection is indicated with a checkmark badge overlay.\\n\\nOne minor observation: the ZStack-based manual positioning approach works but is unconventional compared to `LazyVGrid`. However, this matches the pattern already used in the home screen's `ReorderableShortcutGrid`, so it's consistent with the codebase. No changes needed., review_verdict=APPROVED", "status": "completed", "node_id": "review", "node_name": "R