nd animation curve in `JiggleModifier` to mimic the well-known iOS home screen wiggle effect.", "status": "completed", "node_id": "check_clarity", "node_name": "Check Clarity", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 15.5, "started_at": "2026-03-16T22:01:36.467169+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-16T22:01:51.968896+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "clarity_status=CLEAR → analyze", "status": "completed", "node_id": "clarity_gate", "node_name": "Clarity Gate", "node_type": "condition", "duration_s": 0.1, "started_at": "2026-03-16T22:01:52.039866+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-16T22:01:52.122967+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "project_context=## Project Context for Issue #876\\n\\n### Current JiggleModifier (`ReorderableShortcutGrid.swift:231–262`)\\n\\nThe existing implementation:\\n- **Rotation angle:** ±0.5 degrees (alternates by seed parity — even items go right, odd go left)\\n- **Animation:** `easeInOut(duration: 0.25).repeatForever(autoreverses: true)`\\n- **Exit:** `easeOut(duration: 0.15)` → resets to 0\\n- **Applied at line 73:** `JiggleModifier(isJiggling: isEditMode && !isDragged, seed: item.id.hashValue)`\\n- **Dragged items skip jiggle** (the `!isDragged` flag)\\n\\n### iOS Home Screen Jiggle Reference Values\\nThe native iOS home screen jiggle uses:\\n- **Rotation:** ~±2.0–2.5 degrees peak\\n- **Duration:** ~0.13–0.15 seconds per half-cycle (faster than the current 0.25s)\\n- **Phase offset:** Staggered start times so icons don't all jiggle in sync\\n- **Animation curve:** Linear or very mild ease — not pronounced easeInOut\\n\\n### What Needs to Change\\nThe current values were intentionally softened in commit `f72961d` (#748) from ±1.8° / 0.1s → ±0.5° / 0.25s. The result is too slow and too subtle — it reads more like a gentle sway than an iOS-style jiggle. The native feel requires:\\n1. **Higher angle** (~2.0–2.5°)\\n2. **Faster cycle** (~0.12–0.15s duration)\\n3. **Phase staggering** — use the existing `seed` to add a randomized startup delay (`DispatchQueue.main.asyncAfter`) so icons don't oscillate in lockstep\\n\\n### Technical Considerations\\n- `seed` (from `item.id.hashValue`) is already available and used for direction — it can also drive a phase delay offset\\n- The `@State private var jiggle = false` boolean approach limits the animation to a single value — to add phase stagger, a short delay before calling `withAnimation` is sufficient\\n- `onAppear` already handles the case where items enter edit mode pre-displayed\\n- No other files need changes — everything is self-contained in `JiggleModifier`\\n\\n### Relevant Files\\n| File | Purpose |\\n|---|---|\\n| `talavo-ios/talavo/Features/Home/Widgets/ReorderableShortcutGrid.swift` | **Primary target** — JiggleModifier at line 231 |\\n| `talavo-ios/talavo/Features/Home/Store/HomeGridStore.swift` | Owns `isEditMode` state |\\n| `talavo-ios/talavo/Features/Home/HomeConstants.swift` | Shared sizing constants (no jiggle values here) |\\n\\n### Conventions to Follow\\n- ViewModifiers are private structs within the same file\\n- `@State` for local animation state\\n- `withAnimation(.easeInOut(...).repeatForever(autoreverses: true))` is the established pattern for looping animations\\n- Spring animations (`interactiveSpring`) are used for drag/snap; easeInOut is appropriate for jiggle\\n- No magic numbers should be introduced without comment — the angle and duration values are the key tunables", "status": "completed", "node_id": "analyze", "node_name": "Analyze Project", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 89.1, "started_at": "2026-03-16T22:01:52.250738+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-16T22:03:21.387173+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "plan=## Implementation Plan for #876: Shortcut reorder jiggle should match iOS home screen\\n\\n### File to modify\\n`talavo-ios/talavo/Features/Home/Widgets/ReorderableShortcutGrid.swift` — `JiggleModifier` (lines 216–247). No other files need changes.\\n\\n### Changes\\n\\n**1. Increase rotation angle (line 221–223)**\\n- Change from `±0.5` degrees to `±2.0` degrees\\n- Keep the seed-based direction (even → positive, odd → negative)\\n\\n**2. Speed up animation cycle (lines 230, 241)**\\n- Change `.easeInOut(duration: 0.25)` to `.linear(duration: 0.12)` in both the `onChange` and `onAppear` blocks\\n- Linear curve matches the iOS home screen feel — easeInOut creates a noticeable pause at extremes that reads as \\"sway\\" rather than \\"jiggle\\"\\n\\n**3. Add phase staggering via startup delay**\\n- Add a computed `phaseDelay` property derived from `seed`:\\n  - `Double(abs(seed) % 50) / 1000.0` — gives 0–0.05s random-looking offset per item\\n- In both `onChange(of: isJiggling)` and `onAppear`, wrap the `withAnimation` call in `DispatchQueue.main.asyncAfter(deadline: .now() + phaseDelay)` so icons don't all start oscillating on the same frame\\n- Keep the exit animation (`.easeOut(duration: 0.15)`) immediate with no delay — all icons should stop together\\n\\n### Edge cases & risks\\n- **Dragged items** — already excluded via `!isDragged` at line 76, no change needed\\n- **Items entering mid-jiggle** — `onAppear` already handles this; the phase delay just adds a short stagger before it kicks in\\n- **DispatchQueue timing** — delays are tiny (0–50ms), so there's no visible \\"pop-in\\"; they just desynchronize the oscillation phase\\n- **Seed stability** — `item.id.hashValue` is stable for a given item across re-renders, so the phase offset won't jump around\\n\\n### Summary of value changes\\n| Parameter | Current | New |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Rotation angle | ±0.5° | ±2.0° |\\n| Cycle duration | 0.25s | 0.12s |\\n| Animation curve | easeInOut | linear |\\n| Phase stagger | none | 0–50ms from seed |\\n| Exit animation | easeOut 0.15s | unchanged |", "status": "completed", "node_id": "plan", "node_name": "Plan", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 33.5, "started_at": "2026-03-16T22:03:21.437164+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-16T22:03:54.955024+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "dev_result=https://github.com/bakicelebi/talavo/pull/889", "status": "completed", "node_id": "develop", "node_name": "Develop", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 38.4, "started_at": "2026-03-16T22:03:55.013522+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-16T22:04:33.400894+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "review_result=**APPROVED**\\n\\nThe change is clean and focused. Here's what it does:\\n\\n1. **Increases rotation angle** from ±0.5° to ±2.0° — matches iOS home screen jiggle intensity.\\n2. **Faster animation** — switches from `.easeInOut(duration: 0.25)` to `.linear(duration: 0.12)`, which better matches the snappy iOS jiggle feel.\\n3. **Phase staggering** — adds a 0–50ms random delay per icon so they don't all rotate in lockstep, which is how iOS does it.\\n4. **Extracts `jiggleAnimation`** as a computed property to avoid duplicating the animation definition between `onChange` and `onAppear`.\\n\\nNo issues found:\\n- No force unwraps or force casts\\n- `abs(seed)` prevents negative modulo edge cases\\n- `DispatchQueue.main.asyncAfter` is fine here — the delay is tiny (max 50ms) and only fires on state change or appear\\n- View stays well under 200 lines\\n- No hardcoded colors or theme violations\\n- Matches the issue requirements (make jiggle match iOS home screen), review_verdict=APPROVED", "status": "completed", "node_id": "review", "node_name": "Review", "node_type": "claude_agent", "duration_s": 36.4, "started_at": "2026-03-16T22:04:33.490436+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-16T22:05:09.875376+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "review_verdict=APPROVED → done", "status": "completed", "node_id": "review_gate", "node_name": "Review Gate", "node_type": "condition", "duration_s": 0.1, "started_at": "2026-03-16T22:05:09.946519+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-16T22:05:10.016192+00:00"}, {"error": null, "output": "Issue #876 implemented and reviewed. PR ready to merge.", "status": "completed", "node_id": "done", "node_name": "Ready to Merge", "node_type": "end", "duration_s": 231.0, "started_at": "2026-03-16T22:05:10.067872+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-03-16T22:05:10.067876+00:00"}]	\N
